PVD("serbia_ndp_2021-2023",{"docs":["","RS Economic Reform Programme 2021 2023"],"s":{"1":[[1,"57","7","VAT Anti-Erosion Measures","The increase in the level of VAT collection in terms of the implementation of independent anti-erosion measures in the field of VAT has",""],[1,"58","1","Tax Administration Strengthening and Modernization","there is room for further improvements, through strengthening and modernizing the tax administration.",""],[1,"77","1","Tax Administration Modernization Action Plan","Action plan for the transformation of the Tax Administration for the period 2018-2023 adopted in December 2017, defines strategic guidelines and deadlines in which the activities necessary for the creation of a modern tax administration will be implemented, which will, with the use of modern electronic processes provide better and more comprehensive service to taxpayers and better control and collection of revenues, i.e. accelerate the fight against the grey economy, together with the reform and modernization of inspection supervision.",""],[1,"77","1","Tax Administration Organizational Consolidation and Process Reengineering","In 2019, the organizational separation of basic activities from those that are considered secondary was carried out, with the basic activities now being performed in a smaller number of organizational units, i.e. their consolidation was performed.",""],[1,"77","1","Tax Administration Information Systems Replacement","The next phase of reforms is focused on information systems, and a tender to replace the existing system with a new one is expected next year.",""],[1,"77","1","VAT Refund Acceleration Measures","The implementation of measures aimed at reducing the average time for VAT refunds, i.e. respecting the prescribed deadlines, continues, with the application of the precautionary principle, in order to reduce the possibility of fraud to a minimum, and refunds to low-risk taxpayers to be paid as soon as possible.",""],[1,"77","1","Large Taxpayers Centre Expansion","The Centre for Large Taxpayers (CLT) will expand its scope, i.e. the number of entities that pay their tax obligations through this system will be increased, and at the same time, the capacity of this very important organizational unit within the Tax Administration is being strengthened.",""],[1,"77","1","Asset Origin and Special Tax Investigation Unit","With the adoption of the Law on Determining the Origin of Property and Special Tax and the formation of a special organizational unit of the Tax Administration, conditions were created for cross-analysis of property and income of persons, in order to investigate cases of unjust enrichment and determine special tax.",""],[1,"77","1","Tax Administration Business Process Reengineering","A procedure has been initiated for the selection of an external consultant, who will review the existing business processes and lead the process of their reengineering and modernization.",""],[1,"79","5","Electronic Tax Declaration and Payment System","the development of electronic systems for submitting tax declarations and paying taxes (ePorezi portal)",""],[1,"84","7","Tax Administration Transformation Reform","Transformation of the Tax Administration as a reform process with the aim of creating an organization characterized by modern digital business, orientation towards providing services to taxpayers, as well as providing services in accordance with the best international standards.",""],[1,"84","9","Tax Administration Reform Programme","continue to implement the Tax Administration reform program in order to simplify the activities of the Tax Administration, while providing sufficient human and technological resources for this purpose, improving tax collection and combating the informal economy.",""],[1,"121","2","Monthly Monitoring of SME and Sole Trader Lending","Systematic monitoring of SMEs and sole traders lending has been established on a monthly basis since 2017, showing a constant improvement in the conditions of SMEs and sole traders financing (lower interest rates, longer loan maturity, higher loan volume).",""],[1,"121","3","National Program for Countering Grey Economy","The National Program for Countering Grey Economy in Serbia for the period 2019/2020 was adopted with the Action Plan in April 2019, which envisages further improvement of the work of inspection bodies, stricter penal policy and more efficient collection of tax revenues.",""],[1,"121","5","Tax Administration Digitalization Reform","An important part of the reform is digital economy, so that as of 1 January 2018, the taxpayers can file tax returns for all revenues administered by the Tax Administration and check the status of their tax cards through the E-taxes portal, and as of March 1, 2019, they can receive an electronic certificate of tax settlement as well.",""],[1,"121","5","Flat-Rate Taxation Regulation and Software Development","At the end of 2019, the Regulation on closer conditions, criteria and elements for flat-rate taxation of taxpayers of self-employment income tax (\"Official Gazette of the RS\", No. 94/19 and 96/19- correction) was adopted, becoming applicable as of 1 January 2020.",""],[1,"121","5","Unified Tax and Contributions Collection Software","It still remains to develop a software for the unified collection of taxes and contributions for lump sum taxpayers in the same way that is already in operation for other taxpayers.",""],[1,"121","5","Automated Social Insurance Data Exchange","In the flat-rate taxation system, the exchange of data between PDIF (Pension and Disability Insurance Fund), NHIF (National Health Insurance Fond) and CROSO (Central registry of compulsory social insurance) is fully automated.",""],[1,"122","1","Fiscalization Law Reform","the new legislative framework on fiscalization should eliminate the observed shortcomings of the current model and lead to more efficient control of all deliveries of goods and services provided",""],[1,"122","2","Electronic Invoicing Transition and Centralized Exchange Platform","the goal is to completely replace the paper form of invoice with the digital, and the challenge in this domain is the introduction of a centralized platform for the exchange of electronic invoices.",""],[1,"122","3","eInspector Integrated Inspection Information System","a unique information system eInspector was launched, which integrated 43 inspection services",""],[1,"125","8","Tax Administration Transformation and Modernization Reform","Intensifying reform efforts, focusing on significant structural changes and strengthening administrative capacity is performed in order to provide predictable public revenues of the central budget of the Republic of Serbia.",""],[1,"126","1","Tax Administration Transformation Programme","A new Tax Administration Transformation Programme for the period 2021-2025 is currently being drafted.",""],[1,"126","2","Emergency Tax Relief Measures","The Government of the RS adopted the Decree on Tax Measures during the State of Emergency in order to mitigate the economic consequences caused by the COVID-19 pandemic, which stipulated that TARS would not ex officio revoke decisions on deferment of payment of due tax and would not conduct the procedure of forced collection, whereby no interest would be calculated in the specified period.",""],[1,"126","4","Tax Administration Business Process Reengineering","Reengineering of business processes for the introduction of international good practices in the operational functions of the RS Tax Administration",""],[1,"126","5","TAMP Procurement Plan Implementation","Implementation of the TAMP Procurement Plan (Tax Administration Modernization Project)",""],[1,"126","6","Record Management System Introduction","Introduction of a new record management system through a comprehensive information management model",""],[1,"126","8","Procurement of New ICT Platform Systems","Procurement of systems for the new ICT platform",""],[1,"126","16","Automatic and Electronic Tax Procedure Reform","Through automatic/electronic, simple and free tax procedures, administration of tax liabilities leaves more resources and time to the companies to dedicate them to improving the quality of products and services, which directly affects the increase of competitiveness.",""],[1,"126","16","Grey Economy Reduction Measures","The reduction of the grey economy increases the competitiveness of economic entities that operate in compliance with tax regulations.",""],[1,"127","1","Modern Records Management System","the implementation of the following activities: introduction of a modern record management system through a comprehensive information management model",""],[1,"127","1","Business Network Consolidation Phase Two Preparation","preparation for the second phase of business network consolidation",""],[1,"127","1","New ICT Platform Procurement","procurement of a system for a new ICT platform and implementation of activities from the Procurement Plan",""],[1,"127","2","Tax Administration Efficiency Reform","Improving the efficiency of the Tax Administration will make the process of assessment and paying taxes simpler, more predictable, more consistent and more economical, which will improve the equality of market participants.",""],[1,"127","3","Environmental Risk Management and Monitoring Support","Environmental protection experts have been engaged through the project, whose task is to assist TARS: to successfully implement and monitor project activities that are subject to environmental risks and to manage their impacts; to prepare specific environmental management plans (including mitigation and monitoring plans for subprojects) in order to ensure effective environmental protection, health and safety at work.",""],[1,"127","8","Inter-Institutional Coordination and Communication Improvement","Work on improving coordination / communication between state institutions",""],[1,"127","15","E-Fiscalization and Electronic Invoicing Reform","Structural reform implies two measures - the introduction of a new model of fiscalization (e- fiscalization) and the transition to electronic invoicing.",""],[1,"127","16","Centralized Digital Fiscalization Platform","The first measure involves the introduction of a new model of fiscalization through a centralized digital platform within the Tax Administration, as well as online transmission and verification of data sent from fiscal cash registers to the Tax Administration.",""],[1,"128","1","Centralized Electronic Invoicing Platform","The second measure implies the introduction of a centralized platform for the exchange of electronic invoices both in the segment between legal entities in the business segment (business to business), i.e. B2B, and in the segment of business operations and transactions between the private and the public sector (business to government), i.e. B2G.",""],[1,"128","6","E-Fiscalization Reform","The reform related to e-fiscalization will enter into force on 1 January 2022, but taking into account the wider coverage of taxpayers, the implementation period in the table is set to two years, as a precaution, due to the intention to gradually introduce new groups of taxpayers into the system (the timeline is not yet specified).",""],[1,"128","7","E-Invoice Reform Transition","When it comes to e-invoice reform, for the B2G segment (business to government), the date foreseen for transition to the new system is 1 July 2021, and for the B2B segment (business to business) the transition to the new system is foreseen in the following phases: 1) 1 July 2022, the obligation of all VAT payers to receive invoices in electronic form; and 2) 1 January 2023, the obligation of all VAT payers to receive and send invoices in electronic form.",""],[1,"128","8","Fiscalization Bylaw Adoption","Adoption of bylaws in the field of fiscalization",""],[1,"128","9","Centralized Fiscalization Platform","Launching a new centralized fiscalization platform",""],[1,"128","10","Electronic Invoicing Legislative Framework","Adoption of the legislative framework in the field of electronic invoicing",""],[1,"128","11","Centralized Electronic Invoicing Platform","Launching a centralized platform for electronic invoices",""],[1,"128","12","Expansion of the Electronic Invoices System","The expansion of electronic invoices system to encompass the entire sector of the economy",""],[1,"128","13","Fiscalization and Electronic Invoicing User Transition Communication","Educating and communicating with future users of the fiscalization platform and the electronic invoicing platform in order to prepare them for the transition to the new system",""],[1,"129","5","Fiscalization Model Reform","The new fiscalization model will have a significant impact on increasing the competitiveness of the economy, taking into account lower operating costs and increased efficiency, in terms of: elimination of the double ribbon on the fiscal printer and cancellation of the obligation to keep it, the possibility to use various devices in addition to the classic electronic device cash register (computer, mobile phone, etc.), automation and reduction of costs related to data transmission to the Tax Administration, raising the efficiency of business entities through the use of modern software, etc.",""],[1,"129","5","Electronic Invoicing Implementation","The application of electronic invoicing will significantly affect the acceleration of liquidity flows in the economy, the harmonization with the acquis communautaire and the appropriate business environment.",""],[1,"129","6","Tax Administration Reform and Compliance Improvement","It is expected to achieve greater financial discipline and significantly higher collection of tax revenues, creation of equal conditions in terms of competitiveness for the private sector, enabling the Tax Administration partnership access to taxpayers, better and improved tax control, discouraging companies to avoid tax calculation and payment, etc.",""],[1,"129","7","E-Fiscalization Model Introduction","Introduction of the new model of e-fiscalization is envisaged to be financed with funds from the World Bank loan in the amount of EUR 8.6 million.",""],[1,"129","8","Taxpayer Support for Electronic Device and Cash Register Adjustment","Subsidies in the amount of EUR 25 million, envisaged in the budget for 2021, refer to providing support to taxpayers in order to adjust their electronic devices and cash registers to the requirements of the new improved IT technical solution.",""],[1,"129","9","Electronic Invoicing Centralized Platform","In order to introduce electronic invoicing, funds needed to purchase and create a centralized platform have been provided and it was procured during 2019.",""],[1,"129","11","System Transition Training and Communication Support","During 2021 and 2022, a small portion of the costs is expected to be generated for the purpose of connection of other systems to a centralized platform, as well as additional costs for education, training and communication, whereas all three activities are aimed at the widest range of end users of both systems, in terms of making them fully prepared for transition to a new system of work.",""],[1,"130","1","Electronic Fiscalization and E-Invoicing Reform","Taking into account the complete transition to a new, and largely electronic form of fiscalization, as well as to the electronic form of invoicing, this structural reform will greatly reduce the amount of paper and toner that are in circulation in business operations, which significantly affects environmental protection.",""]],"2":[[1,"86","18","Preschool Participation Expansion for Vulnerable Children","increase the participation of children in preschool education, especially children from vulnerable areas.",""]],"3":[[1,"160","19","National Qualifications Framework System Establishment","The establishment of the NQFS system will contribute to the development of a modern, relevant and flexible education system adapted to the requirements of socio-economic development, providing support for the application of the concept of lifelong learning and enabling easier mobility of the workforce.",""],[1,"161","5","Recognition of Prior Learning Pilot","Funds for piloting the recognition of prior learning procedure were provided from IPA 2014, the implementation of which began in February 2019",""],[1,"161","6","Self-Evaluation and External Quality Control of PROA","Implementation of the procedure of self-evaluation and external quality control of PROA and improvement of the NQFS Register will be financed from the funds of the Agency for Qualifications.",""],[1,"161","6","Agency for Qualifications Operating Financing","For the functioning of the Agency for Qualifications in the period from 2021 to 2023, funds in the amount of EUR 1,190,525 per year are projected from the RS Budget.",""],[1,"161","6","Sectoral Councils Work Financing","Within the funds of the Agency for Qualifications, funds for the work of Sectoral Councils have been integrated, which will participate in the implementation of most of the activities described in the document.",""],[1,"161","8","Qualifications System Reform","Implementation of reforms in the qualifications system will ensure the participation of social partners in the development of qualifications that are in line with market needs, and thus confidence in the (market) relevance and flexibility of the education system as a whole.",""],[1,"229","2","Recognition of Prior Learning Pilot","Piloting of the process of recognition of prior learning",""],[1,"229","3","Recognition of Prior Learning Implementation Procedure","Handbook on standards and ways of implementing the process of recognition of prior leaarning (RPL) is ready to be published in the Official Gazette.",""]],"4":[[1,"156","4","Secondary Vocational Education Modernization","Profiles that are not based on the qualification standard are excluded from the plan for enrolling students in secondary schools and are replaced by those that have qualification standards and modernized curricula.",""],[1,"156","4","State Matura Implementation Support","In the financial plan of the Sector for Secondary Education and Adult Education, a new program activity has been introduced, which refers to the support in the implementation of the state matura.",""],[1,"156","4","Dual Education Expansion","Acquisition, improvement and development of competencies in accordance with the needs of the labour market are provided also by dual education, a model of secondary vocational education in which theoretical classes and exercises take place at school while learning takes place through work in companies.",""],[1,"157","2","Labour Market Monitoring System","it is necessary to establish a system for monitoring continuous changes in the labour market.",""],[1,"157","3","Adult Education Investment and Quality Assurance","there is a need for significant investment in adult education.",""],[1,"159","1","Dual Education and National Qualifications Framework Implementation","The development of dual education and the implementation of the system of the National Qualifications Framework in Serbia (NQFS) create a system in which the qualification is an expression of actually acquired competencies, which responds to the needs of the economy and labour market, modern technical and technological changes which aims to increase the employability of young people.",""],[1,"159","2","Recognition of Prior Learning and Dual Education Development","we will continue to pilot the process of recognition of prior learning (RPL) and the implementation of the RPL, by establishing standards and procedures for self-evaluation and external quality control of publicly recognized organizers of activities (PROA), promotional activities of the National Model of Dual Education in accordance with the adopted Communication Strategy which offers the reference framework and directions for improving communication in the process of further development of dual education in Serbia will also be continued, as well as the development of new qualification standards in secondary vocational education and the modernization of existing educational profiles that are not currently based on qualification standards",""],[1,"159","2","Regional Training Centres in Secondary Vocational Schools","activities on the establishment of regional training centres within secondary vocational schools will be implemented as a form of support for both formal dual and non-formal education, through training, vocational training, additional training and retraining of staff in accordance with the needs of the labour market, since they were not implemented in the previous period due to the situation caused by COVID-19",""],[1,"159","3","Monitoring and Evaluation Framework for Dual Education","One of them refers to the establishment and implementation of a framework for monitoring and evaluation of the National Model of Dual Education and dual educational profiles, which will enable data-based decision-making and ensure the quality of dual education.",""],[1,"159","3","Development of Market-Relevant Dual Education Programmes","Special attention will be paid to the development of market-relevant dual programmes in order to encourage the revitalization of domestic companies as well as attract foreign investment (companies).",""],[1,"159","3","NQFS Register Establishment","activities will be undertaken on the establishment of the NQFS Register for all levels of NQFS.",""],[1,"159","5","Online Database for Teaching Units and Work-Based Learning Topics","As one of the answers to the new epidemiological situation, an online database will be created that will contain teaching units that are implemented in educational institutions and topics for learning through work in companies.",""],[1,"160","1","Online Database for Dual Educational Programmes","Creating and updating an online database of dual educational programmes",""],[1,"160","2","Market-Relevant Dual Programme Development and Revision","Creating and revising market-relevant dual programmes to revitalize domestic companies and attract foreign investment",""],[1,"160","3","Development of Dual Educational Profile Studies","Development of studies necessary for the development of dual educational profiles.",""],[1,"160","4","Promotion of the Dual Education Model","Promotion of the dual model of education (round tables, conferences, etc.)",""],[1,"160","5","Regional Training Centres Establishment and Equipping","Establishment, infrastructural arrangement and equipping of regional training centres",""],[1,"160","7","Development of New Qualification Standards in Secondary Vocational Education","Development of new qualification standards in secondary vocational education",""],[1,"160","8","Monitoring and Evaluation Framework for Dual Education","Establishment of a framework for monitoring and evaluation of the National Model of Dual Education and Dual Education Profiles",""],[1,"160","10","PPU Procedure Piloting and Implementation","Piloting and implementation of the PPU procedure",""],[1,"160","18","Dual Education Development Programme","The development of dual education at the level of secondary and higher education will contribute to the improvement of human capital, which will further ensure easier and faster integration of high school and university students into the world of work, as well as improving the competitiveness of economic entities.",""],[1,"160","18","Regional Training Centres Establishment","The establishment of regional training centres will also contribute to the greater relevance of the education system.",""],[1,"160","18","Dual Education Quality Monitoring and Improvement","Monitoring and, based on the obtained data, improving the quality of dual education will affect the quality of professional competencies that young people acquire in the formal education system, as well as their competitiveness on the labour market.",""],[1,"161","1","Online Database and Promotion for Dual Education Model","No additional funds are needed to create an online database of dual educational programmes and to implement promotional activities of the dual education model.",""],[1,"161","4","Studies for Development of Dual Educational Profiles","For the preparation of studies for the needs of the development of dual educational profiles, planned funds from the budget of the Republic of Serbia amount to EUR 123,600.00 for 2021.",""],[1,"161","7","Market-Relevant Dual Education Programmes","Creating market-relevant dual programmes as well as programmes for revitalization of domestic companies and attracting foreign investment and attending them, will improve the level of competence and employability of pupils and students and their faster integration into the world of employment, i.e. it will contribute to reducing unemployment, faster youth employment in the labour market and activities of the unemployed over 15 years of age.",""],[1,"161","7","Dual Education Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","During the data collection process by applying the framework for monitoring and evaluation of the National Model of Dual Education, data for boys and girls will be segregated in order to see the impact of current dual education policies on gender and make recommendations for improving this aspect if necessary.",""],[1,"161","7","Socio-Economic Status Impact Review in Dual Education","The framework will also assess the fairness and impact of students' socio-economic status (SES) on their experience and success, and propose changes in educational policies and practices in line with the findings.",""],[1,"162","3","Business Incentives for Work-Based Learning Placements","Creating a document that will contain benefits for businesses that accept students for realization of learning through work",""],[1,"228","2","Regulation of Dual Higher Education Studies","Adoption of by-laws regulating the dual model of high education studies, in accordance with the Law on Dual Model of High Education Studies",""],[1,"228","3","Dual Study Programme Accreditation By-law","Proposal of the by-law 'Standards for accreditation of study programmes according to the dual model' has been drafted and is currently in the adoption procedure.",""],[1,"228","4","Dual Schooling Model Promotion","Promotion of the dual schooling model (round tables, workshops etc.)",""],[1,"228","5","Industry 4.0 Integration into the Dual Education System","Introduction of 4.0 industry into the dual education system",""],[1,"228","6","Dual Education Programmes for Industry 4.0 Occupations","Dual educational programmes are created and they include industry 4.0 as well: IT electro-technician, air mechatronics technician, and security technician for ICT sistems in air transport",""],[1,"228","8","Accreditation of Companies and Study Programmes for Dual Higher Education","Accreditation of companies and study programmes/modules to realise the dual model of high education studies",""],[1,"228","9","Dual Study Programme Accreditation Standard","On adoption of the proposed Standard for accreditation of study programmes based on a dual model, the process of accreditation of study programmes/modules for the realisation of dual study models in high education will commence.",""],[1,"242","6","School Curriculum Flexibility Reform","schools should be given more flexibility in terms of the ability to add and subtract classes, to be able to offer the classes the market needs (e.g. information technology classes) without some over-approvals and thus to adjust their teaching programme.",""],[1,"243","1","Curriculum Development and Work-Based Learning Framework","Based on the qualification standard, the Institute for the Improvement of Education and Upbringing prepares a proposal for the curriculum of teaching and learning and submits it to the Ministry of Education, Science and Technological Development.","Ministry of Education, Science and Technological Development"]],"5":[[1,"85","4","Scientific Research Capacity Strengthening Support","Support for scientific research activity through strengthening scientific research capacities",""],[1,"85","5","Research Sector Reform","The reform of the research sector implies considering the capacity of scientific research institutes, with the aim of improving the quality of scientific research work, adequate use of financial resources and research equipment.",""],[1,"85","5","Science Fund Programs Support","Also, it is planned to continue supporting Science Fund Programs, which provide support to the best scientists, teams and their ideas.",""],[1,"85","7","Increase National Research Funding","further increase national research funding; encourage more intensive cooperation between industry and academia, in line with the national research strategy.",""],[1,"85","7","Industry-Academia Research Cooperation","encourage more intensive cooperation between industry and academia, in line with the national research strategy.",""],[1,"85","8","Institutional Support for Smart Specialization and Innovation Development","Improvement of institutional support for the development of smart specializations and innovations",""],[1,"85","9","Business Acceleration Program for Innovative Entrepreneurship","Establishment of a new instrument of institutional support for innovative entrepreneurship and development of cooperation between the economy and the academic sector through the Business Acceleration Program financed by the Innovation Activity Fund.",""],[1,"85","9","Institute for Artificial Intelligence Establishment and Support","Also, support is provided for the establishment and activities of the Institute for Artificial Intelligence, with the aim of using artificial intelligence in the function of economic growth, employment and a better quality of life.",""],[1,"85","11","Smart Specialization Strategy Implementation","start implementing the Smart Specialization Strategy.",""],[1,"85","11","Development of New Financial Instruments for Companies","New financial instruments need to be developed in order to better respond to the needs of companies, especially the most innovative ones.",""]],"6":[[1,"84","16","Improve Predictability of the Business Environment","make additional efforts to increase the predictability of the business environment.",""],[1,"84","19","Business Environment Predictability Improvement Measures","make additional efforts to increase the predictability of the business environment.",""],[1,"86","20","Administrative Environment Improvement for Business Support","Improvement of the administrative environment for encouraging, supporting",""]],"7":[[1,"255","3","Digital Connectivity Data Innovation and Telecommunications Infrastructure Improvement","The proposal is to innovate data on digital connectivity in Serbia, but also to propose more efficient measures to improve the situation in this area (development of telecommunications infrastructure, promotional activities of operators and providers, new applications, application of standards, development and measuring the quality of infrastructure ... ).",""],[1,"258","7","E-Government Infrastructure and New Technologies Upgrade","Increasing the availability of e-Government by improving infrastructure and introducing new technologies",""],[1,"258","7","National Information and Communication Infrastructure Development","Development and improvement of the national information and communication infrastructure",""],[1,"258","7","5G Spectrum Auction and New Generation Networks Rollout","the auction of 5G spectrum (announced for 2022) and the development of new generation networks throughout Serbia whose implementation MTTT started through the project \"Connected Schools\", i.e. the development of broadband internet in rural areas of Serbia",""],[1,"259","1","Telecommunications Infrastructure Coordination and Electronic Platform Mechanism","The need for better coordination in the planning of infrastructure works and better use of the existing infrastructure through the transposition of the CRD into the national framework and the development of an efficient mechanism (electronic platform) for its implementation is also pointed out.",""],[1,"259","2","Broadband Infrastructure Law","It is planned to pass the Law on Broadband Infrastructure, which will transpose the mentioned \"Cost reduction\" directive by the end of 2021.",""]],"8":[[1,"73","2","National Disaster Risk Management Programme","In December 2014, the Government adopted the National Programme for Disaster Risk Management, which will be implemented in cooperation with the World Bank, the United Nations and the EU.",""],[1,"73","2","Disaster Risk Reduction and Emergency Management Law","In November 2018, another umbrella law was passed that deals with the issue of natural disasters and catastrophes, and that is the Law on Disaster Risk Reduction and Emergency Management.",""]],"9":[[1,"176","11","Strategic and Tactical Project Coordination Mechanisms","Creating effective mechanisms of strategic and tactical coordination in project implementation.",""],[1,"179","3","ERP Monitoring and Evaluation Working Group","Within its structures, the National Convention has established a mechanism for monitoring and evaluation of ERP, through a special horizontal Working Group for ERP and its members actively participate in this process.",""],[1,"234","4","Public Sector Wage System Reform","there is still no reform of support for the restoration of medium-term fiscal sustainability, inter alia through the reform of the public sector wage system.",""],[1,"234","4","Credible and Binding Fiscal Rules","it is necessary to include the establishment of credible and binding fiscal rules, given that the existing ones have not been respected for some time.",""],[1,"234","5","Real Sector Capital Investment Projects","Then, it is desirable to increase capital investment with a direct positive impact on economic growth, partly through, e.g. road infrastructure, but first through other concrete projects in the real sector.",""],[1,"234","5","Fiscal Transparency for Public Companies","It is also necessary to increase the transparency of the fiscal cost of the current operations of public companies.",""],[1,"234","5","Financial Derivatives and Insurance Market Development","It is necessary to additionally support the development of the market of financial derivatives and general elements of insurance against financial risks as part of maintaining the liquidity of the economy and the population, which will suffer certain challenges when COVID-19 turns into economic consequences.",""],[1,"234","7","Use of OECD ERP Prioritisation Tool for Structural Reforms","It is recommended that the Ministry of Labour, Employment, Veteran and Social Policy, as well as other line ministries, use the OECD ERP Prioritisation Tool in formulating structural reforms.","Ministry of Labour, Employment, Veteran and Social Policy | other line ministries"],[1,"239","2","Indicator Methodology Development and Standardization","Adopt a methodology for determining indicators and ways of measuring them.",""]],"10":[[1,"84","11","Electronic Invoicing Exchange Platform","The second measure involves the introduction of a centralized platform for the exchange of electronic invoices in the segment between legal entities, ie. B2B, as well as in the segment of business and transactions of the private sector with the public sector, i.e. B2G.",""],[1,"85","12","E-Government Infrastructure and Technology Upgrade","Increasing the availability of e-government by improving infrastructure and introducing new technologies",""],[1,"85","13","Public Sector Digital Transformation Programme","Digital transformation of the public sector, through the strengthening of infrastructure, as a basis for the application of ICT and e-government in the process of providing services to the economy, citizens and the public sector.",""],[1,"138","5","Expansion of E-Government Services and National Portal","The focus of the Government of the Republic of Serbia is on further introduction and development of e-services, i.e. the positioning of the national portal e- Government as a central place for the provision of e-services.",""],[1,"138","6","E-Government Portal Redesign and Mobile Access Upgrade","the Portal's functions and content were redesigned in February 2020, the \"life events\" section was introduced and it was adapted for access via mobile phones and tablets.",""],[1,"138","6","Personal Data Access Function for Public Administration Registers","Users are also provided with the possibility of insight into their personal data stored in the registers and electronic records of public administration.",""],[1,"138","6","National E-Identification and Two-Factor Authentication System","A national portal for authentication of e-Government users (e- ID) and two-factor (multifactor) identification of users of e-Government services have been established.",""],[1,"138","6","Single Sign-On Integration for E-Health and Public Administration Systems","the e-Health Portal was the first connected public administration information system for which the functionality of a single application (SSO) was enabled via the e-ID portal.",""],[1,"138","6","E-Payment Enablement for E-Government Services","E-Payment is enabled to all users through the e- Government Portal, as follows: any payment card, integrated e-banking and electronic money (iPay see).",""],[1,"138","6","E-Payment Expansion at Public Service Counters","E-Payment is enabled at POS terminals at the counters of local self-government, cadastre and MoI and a solution is being drafted that would enable instant payment at the counters of public administration bodies and the eGovernment Portal.",""],[1,"139","1","Digital Skills and E-Government Training Programme","trainings related to the development and improvement of digital skills are conducted, as well as various trainings related to the use of IS and e-Government services, the Retraining programme for IT for employees, etc.",""],[1,"143","10","Government Digital Transformation Programme","The digitalization programme of the Government of Serbia is implemented mainly through the project Serbia at your fingertips - Digital Transformation for Development, which includes support for the implementation of large infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"144","3","Digital Public Services and E-Government Expansion","The newly established systems and implemented improvements have enabled us to respond quickly to the crisis and in a short time develop a large number of necessary software solutions, platforms and services aimed at epidemiological surveillance, infection control, information and support to citizens and the economy, continuation of regular activities in the field of education, trade, and other areas.",""],[1,"206","7","Digitalization of Administrative Procedures","Improvement of the quality of public service through optimization and digitalization of administrative procedures - e-Paper",""],[1,"216","6","ePAPER Procedure Simplification and Guillotine Reform","SR 7. Simplification and guillotine of procedures essential for the operating of business entities - \"ePAPER\"",""],[1,"216","12","eLicences Platform and eGovernment Procedure Digitalisation","The platform for eLicences has been created and linked with all the required services, such as ePayment services and the data bus for the exchange of data among public administration bodies and organisations.",""],[1,"216","13","Administrative Procedure Simplification Action Plans","Adoption and implementation of action plans for the simplification of administrative procedures",""],[1,"216","14","Public Debate on Administrative Simplification Action Plan","the Office for Cooperation with Civil Society has published a call for participation in Public debate on the Proposal of the Action plan for Implementation of the Programme for the Simplification of Administrative Procedures and Regulations 'ePAPER' for 2020-2021.",""],[1,"217","2","Single Registry of Administrative Procedures Law","Adoption of the law to regulate establishment of the Single registry of administrative procedures",""],[1,"217","4","Single Public Registry of Administrative Procedures Law","Public debate on the Draft Law on the Single Public Registry of Administrative Procedures is finished and the text that will be forwarded to the Government is being finalised.",""],[1,"235","1","Business Process Reform for Digitalization","digitalization does not mean much unless there is a reform of processes that are in fact the main problem.",""],[1,"236","4","e-PAPER Administrative Procedure Digitalization and Simplification Reform","the structural reform Improving the quality of public services through optimization and digitalization of administrative procedures - \"e-PAPER\", in addition to the activities of digitalization of administrative procedures also entails prior optimization of procedures, i.e. simplification of processes by eliminating redundant documentation, ex officio collection of data needed to make decisions at the applicant's request, the possibility of electronic payment of fees/charges directly from the e-Government portal, even the reduction of these fees if legitimate, etc.",""],[1,"238","2","Single Electronic Contact Point Establishment and Operation","the opportunity should be used for the establishment and functioning of the SECP to take a more significant place in the proposed list of structural reforms, as a separate structural reform or a relevant part of the structural reform concerning the e-Paper platform.",""],[1,"238","3","Single Electronic Contact Point Establishment","The registry is the starting point for the establishment of the Single Electronic Contact Point (SECP), which is under the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Trade, Tourism and Telecommunications.","Ministry of Trade, Tourism and Telecommunications"],[1,"238","4","Registry Establishment and Administrative Procedure Simplification","The establishment of the Registry follows the process of simplifying procedures through the elimination of unnecessary documentation and redundant steps or digitalization, as well as merging interdependent procedures, which significantly reduces costs in time and money, both for users and public administration.",""],[1,"238","5","Register of Administrative Procedures Portal","the establishment of the Portal of the Register of Administrative Procedures, which will be a single contact point for all procedures, and at a later stage all business requirements in the Republic of Serbia.",""]],"11":[[1,"12","8","Sustainable Health Sector Financing","Ensure adequate and sustainable funding to strengthen the health care sector with an aim to improve access to quality public health care for all citizens.",""],[1,"12","10","Health System Financing Support","In order to achieve adequate and sustainable financing of the health system as a whole, the Republic of Serbia provides funds from the budget for various purposes, for the health care of persons suffering from rare diseases, for salary compensation in case of temporary incapacity for work due to illness or complications in connection with the pregnancy maintenance, for the health care of persons considered insured under article 16 paragraph 1 of the Law on Health Insurance, for support of the activities of the Reproductive Cell Bank, as well as for the reduced rate for health insurance contributions.",""],[1,"13","1","Health Sector Strengthening for Universal Public Care Access","Strengthening the health sector with the aim of improving access to quality public health care for all citizens is one of the priority tasks of the Republic of Serbia.",""],[1,"247","2","Secure Sustainable Funding for Public Health Care","“Ensure adequate and sustainable funding to strengthen the health care sector with an aim to improve access to quality public health care for all citizens”",""],[1,"247","3","Expand Health Care System Digitization Reform","it is necessary to expand this and the proposed SR24 (Digitization of the health care system)",""],[1,"247","3","Health Care Access Inequality Reduction Reform","the component related to the reduction of inequalities in access to health care, especially in light of the consequences of the COVID-19 epidemic will be added to the reform related to health care",""],[1,"256","2","Integrated Health Information System Development and Public Verification","It has been suggested several times that the concept of the Integrated Health Information System should be developed and publicly verified before accessing digitalization.",""]],"12":[[1,"4","2","Unhindered Financing for the Health Response","The first and most important task of the state treasury was sufficient and unhindered financing of the fight to preserve the health and lives of the people.",""],[1,"4","2","Additional Health Sector Financing for Supplies and Equipment","Additional financing is provided for the purchase of consumables, medical equipment, etc.",""],[1,"4","2","Construction of New COVID Hospitals","The construction of two completely new COVID hospitals has also begun in order to provide the necessary capacity for patients whose condition requires hospital treatment.",""],[1,"12","11","Health Sector Financing and COVID-19 Response Measures","The Republic of Serbia reacted in a timely manner and undertook a series of measures and activities that contributed to adequate and sustainable financing of the health sector and in the new situation caused by the global pandemic of coronavirus COVID-19.",""],[1,"12","11","Health Equipment and Medicines Procurement","Procurement of necessary equipment and medicines was completed, new laboratories and hospitals were built in order to provide quality health care for all citizens.",""],[1,"12","11","Construction of New Laboratories and Hospitals","Procurement of necessary equipment and medicines was completed, new laboratories and hospitals were built in order to provide quality health care for all citizens.",""]],"13":[[1,"5","2","Public Sector Wage System Reform","take concrete steps towards implementing an appropriately designed public sector wage system reform.",""],[1,"5","3","Civil Service Salary Law and Public Sector Job Catalogue Reform","A new Law on Salaries of Civil Servants and General Service Employees, as well as amendments to the job catalogue for public sector institutions and other organizations in the public sector, have been postponed and are now expected to be adopted during 2021.",""],[1,"5","3","Personnel Planning-Based Public Sector Employment System","There is a plan to replace this existing framework with a new system based on personnel planning for institutions.",""],[1,"5","3","Employment Commission Hiring Authorization During Transition","During the transition to the new system, and through 2021, the Employment Commission will continue to allow the hiring of staff within the institutions' budget limits, if the number of new employees exceeds 70%1 .",""],[1,"14","3","Public Sector Wage System Reform","Implement the public sector wage system reform under the 2020 budget covering also security sector employees.",""],[1,"14","4","Public Sector New Wage System Implementation","The new wage system for all public sector employees will be put in place in 2020 and ready for implementation in 2021.",""],[1,"14","4","Decree on New Wage System Coefficients","a decree setting coefficients in the new wage system is planned to be adopted.",""],[1,"14","5","Civil Service Salary Law and Job Catalog Reform","The adoption of the new law on salaries of civil servants and state employees, as well as the amendments to the catalog of jobs in public services and other organizations in the public sector, has been postponed due to the pandemic and is expected during 2021.",""],[1,"59","10","Public Sector Wage System Reform","In the previous period, a comprehensive reform of the public sector wage system was initiated, which aims to ensure fairness and reduce the gap between the salaries of public sector employees.",""],[1,"59","11","Medium-Term Public Sector Staffing Control","A more flexible way of controlling employment is now in place, based on medium- term staffing in all areas of the public sector in line with budget constraints.",""],[1,"75","3","Public Sector Employment and Salary System Reform","reforms in the field of employment, personnel management and the salary system in the public sector are expected to continue.",""],[1,"75","4","Public Sector Pay Grade Reform","It was planned that a new system of pay grades for all employees in the public sector (including the army and police), i.e. a new Law on Salaries of Civil Servants and Public Employees and amendments to the Regulation on the Catalogue of Jobs in Public Services and Other Public Sector Organizations, be drafted this year, in order to be ready for implementation with the budget for 2021.",""],[1,"75","5","Public Sector Personnel Management Reform","Therefore, it is necessary to replace the existing solution with a new one, where personnel would be managed at the level of each public sector organization in the medium term and in accordance with budget constraints.",""],[1,"75","6","Public Sector Human Resources Register","the Ministry of Finance has established a Register for public funds beneficiaries for human resources management (RJEKJS) in order to plan expenditures for employees in the Republic of Serbia","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"75","6","Public Sector Salary Calculation Information System","the development of the Information System for the calculation of salaries (CISOZ) of employees in the public sector is underway",""]],"14":[[1,"4","4","Public Finance Stabilization and Public Investment Expansion","In the medium term, gradual stabilization of public finances and directing the fiscal space to the growth of public investments in order to recover and grow the economy is envisaged.",""],[1,"5","5","Increase Growth-Enhancing Capital Spending","To support economic recovery, further increase growth-enhancing capital spending as a share of GDP in 2020 and over the medium term.",""],[1,"13","8","Infrastructure and Capital Investment Prioritization","Fiscal policy in the coming period will be focused on continuing to reduce the overall tax burden, and on the expenditure side, priority will be given to infrastructure and capital projects, as well as pension and wage policy.",""],[1,"14","6","Public Investment Prioritization and Monitoring Mechanism","Develop a single mechanism for prioritising and monitoring all investment regardless of the source of financing.",""],[1,"14","9","Capital Project Management Decree","the Government adopted a new Decree on Capital Project Management, which enters into force in January 2020, and applies to all capital projects regardless of the source of financing.",""],[1,"14","9","Capital Investment Commission","During April 2019, the Government of the Republic of Serbia also established the Capital Investment Commission as a key decision maker for capital projects, as foreseen by the new Decree on Capital Project Management.",""],[1,"14","9","Capital Projects Evaluation and Monitoring Group","The Ministry of Finance has established a new Group for Capital Projects Evaluation and Monitoring, published seven new rulebooks foreseen in the Decree on Capital Investment Management, which regulate in more detail the mechanisms foreseen by the Decree","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"14","10","Capital Project Management Rulebooks","Pursuant to the Decree on Capital Project Management, the Minister of Finance issued rulebooks, as follows: Rulebook on monitoring the implementation of capital projects, Rulebook on the manner of drafting parameters of financial and economic analysis within the feasibility study and previous feasibility study, Rulebook on the content of capital projects database , Rulebook on the feasibility study and the previous feasibility study, Rulebook on the procedure of rationalization of capital projects, Rulebook on the procedure of including capital projects in the budget and Rulebook on investment documentation","Minister of Finance"],[1,"15","2","Capacity Building for Capital Project Beneficiaries","training courses and workshops for future capital project beneficiaries",""],[1,"15","2","Capital Investment Management Information System Development","started drafting tender documentation for the development of the Capital Investment Management Information System",""],[1,"38","1","Acceleration of Capital Projects and Investment Cycle","Accelerating the implementation of capital projects and the continuation of the ongoing investment cycle, supported by both stable FDI inflows and domestic innovative activities, will provide an increasingly strong contribution of capital and factor productivity to potential GDP growth.",""],[1,"44","10","Continuation of Budget-Financed Development Programmes and Infrastructure Projects","efforts were made not to stop development programmes and infrastructure projects financed from the budget",""],[1,"45","3","Infrastructure and Capital Expenditure Prioritisation","On the expenditure side, priority will be given to infrastructure and capital projects, as well as pension and salary policies.",""],[1,"59","1","State Capital Investment Efficiency Improvement","Special attention will be paid to improving the efficiency of state capital investments.",""],[1,"60","3","National Public Infrastructure Investment Cycle","In the next medium-term period, further growth of investments in public infrastructure is expected.",""],[1,"60","4","Public Infrastructure Investment Expansion","The general commitment of fiscal policy in the medium term is to increase investment in infrastructure at all levels of government.",""],[1,"60","4","Local Self-Government Infrastructure Investment Increase","According to the estimates of the Fiscal Council, investments of local self-government in the medium term should increase by at least 75% compared to their current level, i.e. by about EUR 250 million.",""],[1,"76","1","Public Investment Management Framework Strengthening","Strengthening the public investment management framework intensifies new infrastructure projects and raises the quality of existing infrastructure.",""],[1,"76","1","Rulebook for Feasibility Studies on Strategic Infrastructure Projects","a rulebook will be adopted by the end of the year which will contain a brief overview of feasibility studies for large and strategic infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"76","1","Integrated Investment Projects Database and Single Project Pipeline","The public investment management system includes an integrated database of investment projects, which is currently being developed, and a single list of priority projects (Single Project Pipeline) has been established, so that the system will start functioning in 2021 and become fully functional in 2022.",""]],"15":[[1,"4","3","Economic Support Package for Liquidity and Pandemic Mitigation","Thanks to the macroeconomic and fiscal stability achieved in the previous period, the Republic of Serbia had enough space to help the economy with monetary and fiscal measures in mitigating the negative effects of the coronavirus pandemic.",""],[1,"7","1","Bank Incentives for Guaranteed Dinar Lending","incentives for banks to approve dinar loans from the guarantee scheme of the Republic of Serbia at interest rates for at least 0.50 pp lower than the maximum rate defined by the scheme (1M BELIBOR + 2.5 pp).",""],[1,"7","2","Pandemic Impact Mitigation Measures for the Real Sector","The NBS also adopted additional measures to alleviate negative effect of pandemic to real sector and thus preserve financial stability:",""],[1,"7","9","Business Support for Covid-19 Recovery","With a view of mitigating the economic consequences of Covid-19 pandemic and stimulating economic recovery, ensure effective, transparent and non-discriminatory support to businesses affected by the crisis, in particular micro, small and medium-sized enterprises and self-employed.",""],[1,"7","10","COVID-19 Economic Support Package","A total of RSD 690,3 billion (12.5% of GDP) was set aside to support the economy4 and the population in order to mitigate the economic consequences of the COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[1,"7","10","Tax Policy and Private Sector Liquidity Support Measures","In addition to tax policy measures and direct support to the private sector, measures to preserve the liquidity of the private sector and other measures (moratorium on the payment of dividends and fiscal incentives - and incentives to all adult citizens in the amount of EUR 100) are also covered.",""],[1,"7","11","COVID-19 Liquidity and Working Capital Loan Support Program","The Republic of Serbia through the Development Fund of the Republic of Serbia implements the Program of financial support to economic entities to maintain liquidity and working capital in difficult economic conditions due to COVID-19 pandemics (hereinafter: the Program).",""],[1,"8","3","Working Capital Procurement Support","Support to economic entities for the procurement of working capital;",""],[1,"8","4","Liquidity Support for Economic Entities","Support to economic entities for maintaining current liquidity in order to regularly settle obligations to business partners, employees and the state.",""],[1,"8","8","Direct Non-Refundable Budget Support to Economic Entities","Direct support to economic entities in accordance with the Regulation refer to the right to payment of non-refundable funds from the budget",""],[1,"8","12","Hospitality Industry Support Grant","With sectoral support, the Government helps the hospitality industry, primarily the hotel industry, with funds allocated in the amount of EUR 350 per individual bed and EUR 150 per accommodation unit, and the right is exercised by categorized privately owned hotels.",""],[1,"8","13","COVID-19 Economic Guarantee Scheme","the Decree on establishing a guarantee scheme as a measure of support to the economy for mitigating the consequences of the COVID-19 pandemic was also passed.",""],[1,"9","1","National Loan Guarantee Scheme","This Law constitutes the determination of the national guarantee scheme.",""],[1,"9","2","Bank Loan Guarantee Scheme","In accordance with the guarantee scheme, banks can conclude a loan agreement until June 30, 2021 and place loans until July 31, 2021 up to two billion euros",""],[1,"9","3","COVID-19 Economic Loan Guarantee Scheme","The agreement on the guarantee of the Republic of Serbia for lending to the economy in order to mitigate the negative consequences of the COVID-19 pandemic with the Republic of Serbia and the National Bank of Serbia has been signed by 25 banks and the Government has approved about 30 requests to increase the maximum insured portfolio.",""],[1,"9","4","COVID-19 Economic Guarantee Scheme","The Law on Determining the Guarantee Scheme as a measure of support to the economy for mitigating the consequences of the COVID-19 pandemic entered into force on December 29 2020.",""],[1,"16","2","SME Dinar Lending Support Measures","banks will allocate less capital to cover risk than on the basis of non- dinar and foreign currency indexed placements, which, through more favourable conditions, provides additional support for dinar lending to SMEs.",""],[1,"32","4","Government Loan Guarantee Scheme for Enterprises","The scheme envisages the approval of a EUR 2 billion loan with a state guarantee by the end of January 2021, of which EUR 1.59 billion were approved by 31 December 2020.",""],[1,"32","9","COVID-19 Economic Guarantee Scheme","In accordance with the Decree on establishing a guarantee scheme as a measure of support to the economy for mitigating the consequences of the pandemic of the COVID-19 disease caused by the SARS-COV-2 virus, \"Official Gazette of the RS\", no. 57/20.",""],[1,"44","10","Economic Entity Relief and Credit Access Support","The first component was assistance to economic entities in the form of deferred payment of tax liabilities, direct assistance and facilitating access to credit.",""],[1,"46","6","State Loan Support for Businesses and Farms","The financial support programme referred to loans that the state will give to companies directly through the Development Fund of the Republic of Serbia, and they are intended for entrepreneurs, micro, small and medium enterprises, as well as agricultural farms.",""],[1,"46","6","State-Guaranteed Bank Lending Facility","The second part of the financial support to the economy refers to lending through commercial banks with a state guarantee for these loans.",""],[1,"48","11","COVID-19 Economic Guarantee Schemes","Guarantee schemes to support the economy during the COVID-19 crisis",""],[1,"70","4","Guarantee Scheme Regulation Implementation","the Bank has been able to fully implement the Guarantee Scheme Regulation as a measure to support the economy in mitigating the effects of the COVID-19 pandemic caused by SARS-CoV-2 virus",""],[1,"70","4","Removal of Bank Exposure Limits to Companies","and the limits of exposure to companies that existed until then in the case of the Bank Poštanska štedionica were eliminated",""],[1,"71","7","Economic Guarantee Scheme for Pandemic Support","the adoption of the Decree, i.e. the Law on establishing a guarantee scheme as a measure of support to the economy for mitigating the consequences of the pandemic of the COVID- 19 disease caused by the SARS-CoV-2 virus.",""],[1,"71","8","National Loan Guarantee Scheme","This law constitutes the determination of the national guarantee scheme.",""],[1,"72","1","State Guarantee Scheme for Economic Lending","concluding the Agreement on Guarantee of the Republic of Serbia for economic lending to mitigate the negative consequences of COVID-19 pandemic",""],[1,"72","2","Bank Loan Guarantee Scheme","Banks can invest up to two billion euros for the realization of loans, whereby the amount of one billion euros, i.e. the amount of the initial maximum secured portfolio by banks is determined in accordance with the bank's market share according to the NBS report on 29 February 2020.",""],[1,"72","3","Loan Guarantee Scheme for Economic Support","The agreement on the guarantee of the Republic of Serbia for lending to the economy in order to mitigate the negative consequences of the COVID-19 pandemic with the Republic of Serbia and the NBS has been signed by 25 banks and the Government has approved 22 requests to increase the maximum insured portfolio in the amount of EUR 502.5 million.",""]],"16":[[1,"9","5","Social Protection Expansion and Informal Economy Formalization Incentives","Extend social protection coverage and provide incentives for businesses and employees in the informal economy sector to register and to facilitate their transfer to the formal economy.",""],[1,"9","6","Strengthened Labour Inspection and Formalisation Measures","With intensified work of inspection services, and after the improvement of labor legislation and adopted measures that contribute to tax relief, the number of employees will continue to reduce in the grey zone and it will continue to transfer to the contingent of formally employed.",""],[1,"11","4","Short-Time Work and Active Labour Market Support","Take measures to preserve employment including through short-time work schemes and ensure increased provision of effective active labour market policies to the unemployed.",""],[1,"11","5","Active Employment Policy Measures","On 28 February 2020, the National Employment Service (NES) issued public calls for the implementation of active employment policy measures, and their implementation is in progress.",""],[1,"11","5","Active Job Search Measures","Active job search measures include 32,095 unemployed, additional education and training programs 4,305 unemployed, employment subsidy programs 5,726 unemployed, while the public works program covers 4,306 unemployed.",""],[1,"11","5","Employment Subsidy Programmes","Active job search measures include 32,095 unemployed, additional education and training programs 4,305 unemployed, employment subsidy programs 5,726 unemployed, while the public works program covers 4,306 unemployed.",""],[1,"11","5","Public Works Programme","Active job search measures include 32,095 unemployed, additional education and training programs 4,305 unemployed, employment subsidy programs 5,726 unemployed, while the public works program covers 4,306 unemployed.",""],[1,"22","8","Formalization of Work in Non-Agricultural Sectors","Adopt measures to encourage formalization of work in non-agricultural sectors.",""],[1,"22","9","Expansion of the Scope of the Law on the Grey Economy","The National Programme for the Suppression of the Grey Economy in Serbia in 2019 and 2020 and the accompanying Action Plan envisage the expansion of the scope of the Law on",""],[1,"22","10","Amendment of the Law on Simplified Work Engagement in Seasonal Jobs","A working group was formed to amend the Law on Simplified Work Engagement in Seasonal Jobs in Certain Activities, namely: construction, catering and home help.",""],[1,"23","2","Simplified Employment Regime for Seasonal and Home Support Work","Simplified Employment in Seasonal Activities to other activities - home support services.",""],[1,"23","3","Reduction of High Non-Wage Labour Costs","Reduce high non-wage labour costs for jobs at lower wage distribution levels.",""],[1,"38","2","Labour Inspection and Formalization Measures","Also, with the intensified work of inspection services, and after the improvement of labour legislation and adopted measures in the direction of tax relief of work, the reduction of the number of employees in the grey zone will continue and their transfer to the contingent of formally employed.",""],[1,"45","3","Labour Tax Burden Reduction Policy","Fiscal policy in the coming period will be focused on continuing to reduce the overall tax burden on labour, which further relieves the economy, i.e. increases the competitiveness of the private sector.",""],[1,"56","3","Reduction of the Tax Burden on Wages","On the revenue side, the priority will remain to further reduce the tax burden on wages.",""],[1,"57","3","Grey Economy Enforcement and Wage Tax Compliance Measures","In the case of wage taxes, the fight against the grey economy is crucial, given the significant number of undeclared workers and the payment of wages \"under the table\".",""],[1,"57","3","Strengthened Labour and Employment Inspection and Sanctions","In recent years, controls have been intensified and sanctions have been strengthened, which has yielded results in combating the grey economy in the field of labour and employment, but it is important to continue with continuous engagement in this field in the future.",""],[1,"164","11","Implementation of the Law on Agency Employment","As part of the reform of labour legislation, the implementation of the Law on Agency Employment began on 1 March 2020, since when 66 licenses for temporary employment agencies have been issued.",""],[1,"164","12","Business Start-Up Tax and Contribution Exemption","The measure of exemption of business start-ups from paying taxes and contributions based on the earnings of founders employed in the company, i.e. based on the personal earnings of entrepreneurs and entrepreneur farmers, was used by 1,296 businesses (112 companies and 1,184 entrepreneurs) from January 2019 until the end of November 2020.",""],[1,"164","13","Implementation of the Law on Simplified Employment in Seasonal Jobs","The beginning of the application of the Law on Simplified Employment in Seasonal Jobs in certain activities.",""],[1,"231","3","Tax Incentive Promotion and Employment Procedure Simplification","Presentation and promotion of tax incentives, simplification of employment procedures and return to the country",""]],"17":[[1,"11","5","Additional Education and Training Programmes","Active job search measures include 32,095 unemployed, additional education and training programs 4,305 unemployed, employment subsidy programs 5,726 unemployed, while the public works program covers 4,306 unemployed.",""],[1,"11","6","Youth Employment Promotion Program \"My First Salary\"","The Program will finance training with employer, for 10,000 unemployed young people up to 30 years of age, with secondary and higher education, in order to gain first work experience and increase opportunities for their more competitive entry into the labour market and employment.",""],[1,"38","2","Human Capital Investment and Workforce Quality Improvement","Also, we are continuously working on improving the workforce in terms of quality, as well as investing in human capital, all with the aim of easier general employment, especially in that part of the economy that has greater added value.",""],[1,"38","2","Education System Reform and Labour Market Alignment","At the end of the medium term, complex reforms of the education system and an adequate response to the needs of the economy are expected, while active training, retraining and support for social entrepreneurship will facilitate the availability of jobs for socially vulnerable categories of society and thus further ensure economic growth.",""],[1,"80","3","Institutional Cooperation for Labor Market Qualification Planning","the mismatch of educational profiles and supply with the needs of the labor market is a long-term and systemic problem, which is solved by establishing cooperation between key institutions in the identification and planning of qualifications for the needs of the labor market.",""]],"18":[[1,"12","2","Expansion of Social Transfers","Step up social transfers to ensure adequate income support for people at risk of poverty and social exclusion.",""],[1,"12","3","Review and Coordinate Social Transfer Entitlements","it is necessary to determine the scope and distribution of rights and services defined by law, in order to consider all existing social transfers realized by individuals and families taking into account their cumulative acting on social status.",""],[1,"12","4","Integrated Social Maps System for Social Protection Targeting","it is necessary to introduce an integrated system of social maps as a documented way of measuring the socio-economic power of social protection beneficiaries, envisaged by the structural reform 23.",""],[1,"12","5","Social Card Register Development","So far, the first phase of the development of the Social Card Register has been completed, which includes the internal connection of the data subsystem at the level of the Ministry, and a draft law on the social card has been drafted.",""],[1,"59","1","Better Targeting of Social Assistance Programmes","The social component of the budget has been improved by better targeting of social assistance programmes and greater allocation for health and education functions.",""],[1,"80","5","Social Map Information System","In the following period, in order to assess the social and material status of beneficiaries for the fair distribution of social protection funds, the Social Map Information System will be established for the collection and use of data from all available state administration sources.",""],[1,"170","2","Integrated Social Card System","the introduction of an integrated system of social cards as a documented way of measuring the socio-economic power of social protection beneficiaries is underway.",""],[1,"173","2","Social Card Register Establishment","Fair distribution of funds intended for social protection will be ensured through the establishment of a single Social Card Register which will enable an overview of the social and material status of beneficiaries, and a necessary precondition for that is collecting and using data that determine that status from all available state administration sources.",""],[1,"173","2","Social Protection Information System Network","the application of the information system to support business processes in the implementation of social protection, \"System for protection and automatization of social protection instruments\", will connect social protection institutions, and above all centres for social work in a single network.",""],[1,"173","3","Social Card Register Development","So far, the first phase of the development of the Social Card Register has been completed, which includes internal connection of the data subsystem at the level of the Ministry, and a Draft Law on the Social Card has been drafted.",""],[1,"173","5","Social Protection Instruments Protection and Automation System","the Ministry started the procurement of the System for protection and automatization of social protection instruments, which includes a software solution, with all modules and submodules, and hardware","Ministry"],[1,"173","6","Social Screening and Vulnerability Data Integration System","these systems will seek to support social screening for post-crisis management, especially for socially vulnerable groups, integration with NES unemployment data (systematic review and finding of the most vulnerable unemployed persons), as well as georeferencing of vulnerable groups and individuals by territory with the level of data aggregation provided by the address register.",""],[1,"173","7","Integrated Social Protection Information System","Connecting social work centres into a single network using software, i.e. an information system to support business processes in the implementation of social protection (\"System for protection and automatization of social protection instruments\").",""],[1,"173","9","Social Card Legal and Regulatory Framework","Adoption of respective laws and bylaws - Law on Social Card - Rulebook on technical conditions for establishing and maintaining a social card",""],[1,"174","1","Training for Users of Social Protection Systems","Appropriate instructions prepared and necessary trainings organized for the users of the System for protection and automation of social protection instruments and the Social Card Register.",""],[1,"174","8","Social Card Register Software Solution Phase 2 Preparation","For the implementation of activities related to the Social Card Register, funds are planned in the budget of the Republic of Serbia for 2021 in the amount of RSD 130,000,000 or EUR 1,083,333 for the preparation of the 2nd phase of the software solution",""],[1,"174","9","Social Protection Instruments Protection and Automation System","For the System for protection and automatization of social protection instruments, planned funds for 2021 amount to RSD 269,428,000 or EUR 2,245,233.",""],[1,"174","10","Social Card Registry and Social Protection Automation System","The establishment of the Social Card Registry and the System for Protection and Automatization of Social Protection Instruments will affect the fairer distribution of social assistance and reduce abuse and faster response in case of changes in data that affect socio-economic status, but also poverty prevention and elimination of social exclusion.",""],[1,"175","3","Draft Law Refinement and Resubmission Process","It is necessary to refine the text and re-adopt the procedure in the convocation of the new Government and forward it to the National Assembly for adoption.",""],[1,"175","5","Social Card Register Development","The adoption of the Law on the Social Card is a condition for connecting, i.e. drafting the Social Card Register.",""],[1,"232","8","Social Welfare Information System Network Integration","Linking social welfare centres into the single network through a software - Information system for the support to business processes in the realisation of social protection (Social welfare IS)",""],[1,"232","9","Social Welfare Instruments Protection and Automation System Procurement","Ministry of Labour, Employment, War Veteran and Social Affairs in 2020 started the procurement of the System for Protection and Automatisation of Social Welfare Instruments, which incorporates the software with all modules and submodules, and the hardware.","Ministry of Labour, Employment, War Veteran and Social Affairs"],[1,"233","3","Social Map Registry Development","So far the first development stage of the Social Map Registry has been completed and it involves internal connection of data subsystems at the Ministry level, and the Draft Law on Social Map has been developed.",""],[1,"233","6","Social Map and SOZIS User Training and Guidelines","Guidelines have been prepared and trainings organised for users of the Social Map and SOZIS (Social Welfare Information System)",""],[1,"246","5","Social Card IT System Introduction","what is currently relevant in this structural reform is only the introduction of IT system - Social Card.",""],[1,"246","5","Expansion of Cash Benefit Coverage and Adequacy","It is also necessary to expand the proposed structural reform by returning to it the component related to increasing the scope and adequacy of cash benefits.",""],[1,"246","6","Social Card Register Establishment","This reform has also been proposed for a new ERP.",""],[1,"247","2","Strengthen Social Transfers for Poverty and Social Exclusion","“Step up social transfers to ensure adequate income support for people at risk of poverty and social exclusion”",""],[1,"247","3","Social Protection Cash Benefits Reform","the component related to increasing the coverage and adequacy of cash benefits will be returned to the reform related to social protection",""],[1,"247","4","Social Card Register","the introduction of the Social Card Register \"has no structural connection with what happened this year with the pandemic and the recommendation to carefully monitor the impact of the pandemic on vulnerable groups.\"",""],[1,"247","4","System for Protection and Automation of Social Protection Instruments","the System for Protection and Automation of Social Protection Instruments will support social screening for the needs of managing the period after the pandemic and finding the most endangered individuals, especially in terms of unemployment.",""],[1,"247","5","Social Protection Reform","its overriding goal is more just distribution of social assistance as well as a faster response to changes in data affecting socio-economic status and poverty prevention.",""],[1,"247","6","Expansion of Cash Benefit Scope and Adequacy","The proposal to \"return the component concerning the increase of the scope and adequacy of cash benefits to the ERP\"",""]],"19":[[1,"22","5","Active Labour Market Measures Expansion","Significantly increase funding and implementation of active labour market measures tailored to the needs of the unemployed, especially women, youth, including those who are highly qualified.",""],[1,"22","7","My First Salary Employment Incentive Programme","The \"My First Salary\" programme is implemented in cooperation with the Government of the Republic of Serbia, the Ministry of Labour, Employment, Veteran and Social Policy, the National Employment Service and the Serbian Chamber of Commerce, and on the basis of the Decree on the Employment Incentive Program \"My First Salary\" which was adopted by the Government of the RS at the proposal of the Ministry of Labour, Employment, Veteran and Social Policy.","Ministry of Labour, Employment, Veteran and Social Policy | National Employment Service | Serbian Chamber of Commerce"],[1,"38","2","Labour Market Improvement and Employment Support Measures","Such expectations are the result of continuous work on improving labour market conditions, improving labour market institutions, encouraging employment and inclusion in the labour market of hard-to-employ persons, as well as support for regional and local employment policy.",""],[1,"81","2","National Employment Policy Alignment Reform","SR 20. Improving national employment policy in line with good practice and EU standards.",""],[1,"165","6","Active Employment Policy Measures","For the implementation of the planned programmes and measures of active employment policy in 2021, RSD 5.2 billion has been provided, which is an increase of 40% compared to 2020 (of which 2 billion dinars for the Youth Employment Promotion Program \"My First Salary\").",""],[1,"166","6","Youth Employment Promotion Programme \"My First Salary\"","The implementation of the Youth Employment Promotion Programme \"My First Salary\" has also begun.",""],[1,"230","2","Advancement of the National Employment Policy","SR 20. Advancement of the national employment policy in line with good practice and EU standards",""],[1,"246","1","Data-Based Profiling System Pilot","it would be useful to introduce a data-based profiling system for piloting purposes, and adjust the monitoring framework to measure direct service delivery (programme entry and exit) and user situation after 6, 12 and 18 months.",""],[1,"246","2","Programme Implementation Capacity and Financing Strengthening","In order for Serbia to be able to introduce elements of this programme, it is necessary to make prior efforts and meet certain preconditions with special emphasis on increased budget allocations (in the RS budget and through other sources of funding since Serbia does not have the possibility to use the funds of the European Social Fund), strengthening the capacity of the ministry in charge of employment as well as the National Employment Service.",""],[1,"246","3","Employment Strategy Development","the Ministry of Labour, Employment, Veteran and Social Policy is in the process of developing the Employment Strategy in the Republic of Serbia for the period from 2021 to 2026","Ministry of Labour, Employment, Veteran and Social Policy"]],"20":[[1,"12","6","Reduction of the Tax Wedge for Low-Wage Earners","Reduce the tax wedge considerably for low wage earners to ensure living wages and to incentivise the formalisation of employment.",""],[1,"12","7","Minimum Wage Increase","The minimum price of labor for the period January-December 2021 has been increased and amounts to RSD 183.93 (net) per working hour.",""],[1,"12","7","Personal Income Tax Non-Taxable Threshold Increase","The adopted Law on Personal Income Tax (December 2020) increased the non-taxable personal income from RSD 16,300 to 18,300 per month (by 2,000 RSD), decreasing tax wedge.",""],[1,"13","8","Tax Burden Reduction Policy","Fiscal policy in the coming period will be focused on continuing to reduce the overall tax burden, and on the expenditure side, priority will be given to infrastructure and capital projects, as well as pension and wage policy.",""],[1,"13","10","Pension Indexation Reform","As of 2021, pensions will be indexed according to the Swiss formula, which will ensure a 5-6% nominal growth annually in the long term.",""],[1,"13","10","Tax Burden Reduction Measures","On the revenue side, the plan is to continue reducing the tax burden, in particular the personal income tax rates and social insurance contributions.",""],[1,"23","4","Minimum Wage Increase","The minimum price of labour for the period January - December 2020 has been increased and amounts to RSD 172.54 (net) per working hour.",""],[1,"23","4","Personal Income Tax and Social Security Contribution Amendments","The proposed amendments to the Law on Personal Income Tax and the Law on Compulsory Social Security Contributions (adopted by the Government on 31 October 2019) refer to: increasing the non-taxable amount of salaries from RSD 15,300 to RSD 16,300 per month",""],[1,"23","5","Minimum Wage Increase","The minimum price of labour for the period January-December 2021 has been increased and amounts to RSD 183.93 (net) per working hour.",""],[1,"29","3","Minimum Wage Increase","the decision to increase the minimum labour price to RSD 172.54 per working hour in 2020 from RSD 155.3 in 2019",""]],"21":[[1,"80","3","Education System Digitalization and Unified Information System","the digitalization of the education system and the introduction of the Unified Information System of Education are being intensively continued, in order for teaching to take place unhindered and efficiently in the conditions of the COVID-19 virus pandemic, but also after its completion.",""],[1,"86","15","Education System Digitalization and Unified Information System","Digitalization of the education system and introduction of a uniform information education system",""],[1,"86","16","Unified Information Education System","The reform implies the introduction of the Unified Information Education System, as an IT basis for the modernization of management and decision- making, which will contribute to the modernization and digitalization of the education system.",""],[1,"86","16","Open Educational Resources Repository","It is also planned to develop a repository of open educational resources (didactic materials), as a database of digital resources for schools.",""],[1,"156","2","Distance Learning Continuation and Education Support Measures","Recommendations for mitigating the effects of the crisis include continuation of \"distance learning\", strengthening support for teachers and parents to motivate students, harmonizing knowledge assessment systems to simplify transitions between grades and educational cycles, and regularly reviewing and improving existing measures.",""],[1,"157","8","School ICT Equipment and Internet Connectivity","Equipping schools with ICT equipment and providing the Internet to schools throughout Serbia are necessary preconditions for the digitalization of education.",""],[1,"157","8","Digital Teaching Content and Services Expansion","The advantages that digital technologies provide have been used to improve the teaching process through the introduction of digital teaching content or various services and greater use of ICT in schools.",""],[1,"157","8","Electronic Diary Rollout","The electronic diary (e-Diary), one of the digital services, is available in 1,326 schools.",""],[1,"157","8","Digital Textbooks Provision","It continues with activities on providing digital educational content- digital textbooks that are provided for all students who receive education according to reformed curricula (in the school year 2020/21, they are first, second, third, fifth, sixth and seventh grade), as well as on the development of a unique information system of education,",""],[1,"157","8","Unique Education Information System Development","It continues with activities on providing digital educational content- digital textbooks that are provided for all students who receive education according to reformed curricula (in the school year 2020/21, they are first, second, third, fifth, sixth and seventh grade), as well as on the development of a unique information system of education,",""],[1,"158","3","Distance Learning and Online Class Delivery","The Ministry of Education, Science and Technological Development responded to the challenges of the epidemiological situation and the state of emergency by providing students of all school ages with online classes on RTS2 and RTS3 channels, as well as through the \"My School\" application.","Ministry of Education, Science and Technological Development"],[1,"158","3","Online Self-Assessment Test for Grade 8 Students","In addition to online classes, an online test of self-assessment of knowledge was organized for 8th grade students \"Self-assessment of knowledge 2020\", which was a preparation for taking the primary-school-leaving examination.",""],[1,"158","4","Hybrid Primary and Lower Secondary Schooling Arrangement","In the new school year, from September 2020, classes in primary schools take place so that first-cycle students (grades 1-4) attend classes daily in classes divided into groups, if the class has over 15, exceptionally 18 students.",""],[1,"158","4","Combined Model for Lower Secondary Education","In the second cycle (grades 5-8), education according to the combined model is implemented if the class has over 15, exceptionally 18 students, so that alternately, every other day, one group attends direct classes at school, and the other online classes.",""],[1,"162","6","Digital Education Modernization Programme","The main goal of this reform is to modernize the education system through the introduction of modern digital technologies, which should provide a higher level of learning outcomes and raise the quality of digital competencies of young people enabling them to compete in the labour market through digital transformation.",""],[1,"162","6","Unified Education Management Information System","The advantages that digital technologies can provide will be used to improve the teaching process through the introduction of digital teaching content, as well as the establishment of a Unified Education Management Information System (EMIS) which is the basis for modernizing management, making decisions based on information to ensure quality and efficient education system with rationalization of financing and reduction of administrative burden of all employees in the system of education and upbringing.",""],[1,"162","6","Graduate Labour Market Monitoring and Policy Analytics","The Unified Education Management Information System includes integration with the Central Register of Compulsory Social Insurance, which enables the monitoring of graduates in the labour market.",""],[1,"162","7","Open Educational Resources Repository Development","Within this reform, a new measure has been defined which envisages the development of a repository of open educational resources, as a database of digital resources for schools.",""],[1,"162","7","National Distance Learning Content Inventory","In addition, this activity will support the creation of an inventory of existing content that will be deployed on a national distance learning platform.",""],[1,"162","9","Computer Infrastructure for Distance Learning","it is necessary to provide computer infrastructure for distance learning.",""],[1,"162","9","Open Educational Resources Repository Development","one of the focuses of this reform is the development of a repository of open educational resources, as a database of digital resources for schools.",""],[1,"163","1","Unified Education Management Information System Development","Development of the Unified Education Management Information System and preparation of the first reports",""],[1,"163","2","Expansion of Computer Science and Programming Study Programmes","Increasing the scope of study programmes and profiles in computer science and programming in the field of higher and secondary education in accordance with the needs of the market",""],[1,"163","3","Classroom and Cabinet Computer Equipment Provision","Equipping classrooms and cabinets with computer equipment",""],[1,"163","5","Digital Textbook Quality Assurance System Improvement","Improving the quality assurance system for the application of digital textbooks",""],[1,"163","6","Open Educational Resources Repository Aggregators","Development of open educational resources repository aggregators",""],[1,"163","10","National Framework for Digital Technology Use in Education","Developed national framework of comprehensive policies for the effective use of digital technologies in educational institutions with clearly defined standards",""],[1,"163","14","Digitalization of Secondary and Higher Education","The implementation of digitalization of education at the level of secondary and higher education will contribute to the improvement of digital competencies of all participants in the process, which will ensure easier and faster integration of high school students and teaching staff, as well as improving the competitiveness of businesses operating in Serbia.",""],[1,"163","14","Education Management Information System","The establishment of the Education Management Information System will contribute to the greater relevance of the education system, which will, using modern information technologies, enable raising the quality, efficiency, effectiveness and economy of education, as well as precise monitoring of progress, greater transparency in work, possibility of rational resource planning and future investments.",""],[1,"164","1","ICT Skills and Education Quality Monitoring through EMIS","mastering the necessary ICT knowledge and skills, while constantly monitoring and maintaining the quality of education through the use of EMIS",""],[1,"204","1","Digitalization of the Education System","Digitalization of the education system and introduction of a uniform information education system",""],[1,"209","4","Digitalization of the Education System","Digitalization of the education system and introduction of a uniform information education system",""],[1,"209","4","Uniform Information Education System","Digitalization of the education system and introduction of a uniform information education system",""],[1,"225","2","Electronic Government Service and Education Infrastructure Development","SR 15. Improvement of the electronic government service and education through development of the national information-communication infrastructure",""],[1,"225","4","Connecting Schools ICT Infrastructure Improvement","Activities aimed at the improvement of information and communication infrastructure in all primary and secondary schools in the RS - 'Connecting Schools'",""],[1,"229","4","Digitalization of the Education System","Digitalization of the education system and introduction of an uniform information education system",""],[1,"229","5","ICT Integration in Teaching, Learning, and Grading","Increased usage of ICT in teaching, learning, and grading, so that students could master skills needed to respond to challenges in a fast-paced environment",""],[1,"229","9","Digital Textbook Procurement for Primary School Pupils","Procurement of digital textbooks for all primary school pupils who attend school on a reformed plan and programme",""],[1,"229","11","Provision of Digital Textbook Licences","The provision of annual licences for digital textbooks for all 2nd grades was realised, as well as for the 3rd, 6th and 7th grades in 707 selected schools, whereas for all 1st grades, for 3rd, 6th and 77th grade in 219 schools, as well as for 5th grade in 924 schools a half-year licence for digital textbooks was provided.",""],[1,"229","12","Single Information System Development","Development of the Single Information System in",""]],"22":[[1,"29","3","COVID-19 Economic Support Measures Package","the implementation of a package of economic measures adopted by the Government on two occasions to combat the negative effects of the coronavirus pandemic",""],[1,"46","2","Economic Measures to Reduce COVID-19 Impacts and Support the Economy","At the beginning of April 2020, the Government adopted the \"Programme of economic measures to reduce the negative effects caused by the COVID-19 virus pandemic and support the Serbian economy\" which formulated a set of measures to help the economy in order to preserve liquidity and mitigate the decrease of employment and to preserve the standard of living and liquidity of population.",""],[1,"46","4","Tax Payment Deferral for Private Sector Firms","The first group of tax policy measures referred to the postponement of the payment of taxes and contributions on salaries and profit taxes for the private sector, initially for a period of three months, with the subsequent repayment of liabilities incurred in instalments from 2021 at the earliest.",""],[1,"46","5","Direct Wage Subsidy and Forced Leave Support","The second set of measures included the payment of direct aid in the amount of the minimum wage for entrepreneurs, micro, small and medium enterprises, i.e. subsidies of 50% of the minimum wage to large enterprises, whose employees were sent on forced leave due to reduced business volume or complete suspension.",""],[1,"46","8","Extension of Economic Support Measures","the Government extended the duration of measures to support the economy.",""],[1,"46","8","Tourism and Hospitality Assistance Programme","a programme of assistance to a part of economic entities in the field of tourism and hospitality was additionally prepared and adopted.",""],[1,"47","3","Economic Support Package","The package of economic measures was aimed at preserving the production capacities of the entire economy, maintaining the living standard of the population and providing liquidity to all economic entities.",""],[1,"48","2","Deferred Payroll Tax and Contribution Payment Scheme","Deferred payment of payroll taxes and contributions for the private sector during the state of emergency and for one additional month; private companies will repay these obligations in instalments, but not before January 2021",""],[1,"48","6","Direct Wage Support for Entrepreneurs and MSMEs","Direct support to entrepreneurs who pay a flat tax and entrepreneurs who pay real income tax, micro, small and medium enterprises in the private sector - three months of payment of the net minimum wage and two additional months of payment of 60% of the net minimum wage",""],[1,"48","7","Emergency Wage Support for Employees Facing Termination","Direct support to large private companies - support in the amount of 50% of the net minimum wage (during a state of emergency) to employees who have received a decision on termination of employment (based on Articles 116 and 117 of the Labour Law).",""],[1,"48","8","Hotel Sector Direct Support Scheme","Direct support to the hotel sector - 350 € per bed, 150 € per room, in dinar equivalent calculated according to the official middle exchange rate of the NBS",""],[1,"49","16","Economic Assistance Package for Companies","additional package of economic assistance measures in the form of tax deferrals and direct assistance to companies;",""],[1,"52","5","Direct Aid to Companies and Entrepreneurs","From this category of expenditures, direct aid was paid to companies and entrepreneurs to overcome the crisis caused by the pandemic.",""],[1,"62","4","Comprehensive Economic Assistance Package","The fiscal policy response to the complex economic situation caused by the coronavirus pandemic is represented by a comprehensive package of economic assistance measures estimated at 12.5% of GDP.",""],[1,"64","3","COVID-19 Fiscal Support Package","The fiscal package of measures was aimed at helping businesses, preserving the living standards of the population and investing in the health system.",""],[1,"74","8","COVID-19 Fiscal and Monetary Support Package","in response to the crisis caused by the pandemic, a significant package of fiscal and monetary measures was applied, which supported the economy and citizens, preserved jobs, equipped the health system and provided assistance to the most vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"77","1","COVID-19 Tax Relief and Payment Deferral Measures","The Tax Administration has played a significant role in implementing some of the measures taken in response to the crisis caused by COVID-19: postponing the payment of taxes on salaries and contributions and their payment in 24 instalments, starting 2021, postponing the payment of corporate income tax for second quarter of 2020, three-month moratorium on forced collection and reduction of interest on tax debt.",""],[1,"166","3","Liquidity Preservation and Employment Support Measures","The Government of Serbia has adopted a set of measures in order to preserve the liquidity of economic entities and maintain economic activity and employment78.",""],[1,"166","4","Tax Payment Deferral Measure","The first set of measures enables the postponement of the payment of due tax obligations, for which RSD 189 billion (EUR 1.6 billion) or 3.4% of GDP have been allocated.",""],[1,"166","5","Direct Business Support and Wage Subsidy Package","The second set of measures refers to direct benefits to companies, payment of assistance in the amount of the minimum net salary (May-July) for entrepreneurs, micro, small and medium enterprises, i.e. subsidies of 50% of the minimum net salary to large companies whose employees are sent on forced leave, due to reduced business volume or complete suspension of work.",""],[1,"166","5","Additional Direct Economic Support and Tax Deferral Package","Additional direct support for the economy implies the payment of another two months (August- September) of 60% of direct benefits from the budget of the Republic of Serbia that were paid to them in July 2020 (about RSD 18 thousand or EUR 155), while taxes and contributions on earnings will be postponed for one month.",""],[1,"166","5","Hotel Sector Support Scheme","Also, the set includes support for the hotel sector (EUR 350 per bed, EUR 150 per room).",""],[1,"166","9","COVID-19 Economic Support Package","A total of EUR 5.7 billion was set aside to support the economy in order to reduce the negative effects caused by the COVID-19 pandemic (12.2% of GDP).",""],[1,"166","9","Tax Policy Measures and Direct Business Support","In addition to tax policy measures and direct support to economic entities, measures to preserve liquidity in the private sector and other measures (moratorium on the payment of dividends and direct assistance to all adult citizens) are also included.",""],[1,"242","2","Financial Support Mechanism for Companies","Adding a new component related to the development and implementation of the mechanism of financial support to companies is primarily a response to the crisis and reduction of business volume due to the COVID-19 pandemic.",""]],"23":[[1,"7","3","Loan and Leasing Liability Moratorium","prescribing a first moratorium on loan and leasing liabilities for clients who expressed their interest (individuals, companies, entrepreneurs and farmers) in March for up to 90 days and then another moratorium for liabilities that fall due in the period from August 1, 2020 to September 30, 2020, as well as liabilities that were due in July, and the debtor has not settled them.",""],[1,"7","4","Loan Repayment Restructuring Regulations","adoption of set of regulations to facilitate the repayment of certain loans granted to citizens by which banks are encouraged to offer debtors refinancing or change the maturity date of the last installments of consumer, cash and other loans",""],[1,"7","5","Housing Loan Access and Repayment Regulation Reform","adoption of set of regulations to facilitate access to housing loans by prescribing lower minimum degree of completeness of the building, thus providing support to construction industry; enabling the possibility of extension of housing loan repayment periods for maximum five years and;",""],[1,"7","6","Temporary Relaxation of Household Short-Term Dinar Loan Approval Procedure","temporary relaxation of the approval procedure for household short-term dinar loans up to a certain amount",""],[1,"7","7","Debt Relief Grace Period for Affected Borrowers","in December 2020, new facilities were provided for debtors of banks and financial leasing providers affected by the COVID-19 pandemic in the form of granting a grace period of six months for loans and similar products.",""],[1,"34","5","Bank Debt Repayment Moratorium","in March 2020 the NBS adopted decisions prescribing a delay in repayment of obligations (moratorium) for bank debtors and financial lenders which cannot be shorter than 90 days.",""],[1,"34","5","Additional Loan and Leasing Repayment Moratorium","in July the NBS adopted decisions prescribing an additional delay in the repayment of liabilities to banks/financial leasing providers (additional moratorium) due in the period from 1 August 2020 to 30 September 2020, as well as the delay in the repayment of obligations that were due in July this year, and the debtor has not settled them.",""],[1,"34","7","Housing Loan Regulatory Amendment","the Decision on Amendments to the Decision on Measures for Safeguarding and Strengthening Stability of the Financial System was adopted, which created regulatory preconditions for allocating a smaller share required for granting housing loans to first",""],[1,"35","1","Housing Loan Loan-to-Value Regulation","defining LtV indicators at a maximum of 90%, that is, that the amount of the housing loan secured by a mortgage on the real estate does not exceed 90% of the value of that real estate",""],[1,"35","2","Loan Refinancing and Maturity Extension Measures","banks are encouraged to offer debtors refinancing or change the maturity date of the last instalments of consumer, cash and other loans (which is not a housing loan or current account overdrafts) approved by 18 March 2020 for additional two years longer than the current repayment regime for these loans.",""],[1,"35","3","Temporary Measures to Facilitate Access to Finance for Individuals","a decision was adopted defining measures to facilitate access to finance for individuals - Decision on temporary measures for banks in order to facilitate access to finance for individuals.",""],[1,"35","4","COVID-19 Debt Relief and Loan Repayment Facilities","on 14 December 2020, NBS adopted additional measures, which primarily aim to provide relief to debtors (individuals, companies, farmers and entrepreneurs) affected by the COVID-19 pandemic and for that reason they are not able to settle obligations to the bank or financial leasing provider, i.e. they may have difficulties in settling those obligations.",""]],"24":[[1,"6","6","Timely Monetary Policy Response to COVID-19 Uncertainty","the National Bank of Serbia is carefully monitoring and reacting in a timely manner to the increased global uncertainty caused by the COVID-19 pandemic to preserve price and financial stability and minimize the negative effects on the real sector.",""],[1,"6","8","Bank Liquidity Support Measures","providing additional dinar and FX liquidity to banks at favorable rates (additional swap auction of FX purchases, repo auctions of dinar government securities, temporary change of the principle of realization at regular swap auctions so that the swap of purchase and swap sales of FX no longer had to be equal);",""],[1,"6","9","Foreign Exchange Market Intervention","interventions on the FX market, which preserved the relative stability of the dinar exchange rate against the euro and thus provided support for the preservation of overall financial stability;",""],[1,"6","10","Permanent Purchase of Dinar Government Securities","permanent purchase of dinar government securities from banks, which significantly contributed to maintaining stability in the secondary market of these securities;",""],[1,"6","11","Inclusion of Dinar Corporate Bonds in Monetary Operations","inclusion of dinar corporate bonds in the list of securities that may be subject to monetary operations, thus supporting the economy and corporate market development bond;",""],[1,"39","3","Pandemic Monetary Policy Easing Measures","At the extraordinary session on 11 March, a decision was made to reduce the key policy rate by 50 basis points to 1.75%, narrowing the corridor of basic interest rates, from ± 1.25% to ± 1.0% in relation to the key policy rate and other measures have been adopted in order to preserve favourable financing conditions for the economy and citizens.",""],[1,"39","4","Monetary Liquidity Support and Repo Operations","since the outbreak of the epidemic, the NBS has pre- emptively supported banks' dinar liquidity on favourable terms through direct repo operations for the purchase of government securities and corporate bonds and bilateral operations for permanent purchase of government securities and corporate bonds on the secondary market, by organizing additional swap operations of foreign exchange purchase and temporary change of the manner of conducting auctions of swap purchase and swap sale of foreign exchange",""],[1,"39","4","Expanded Collateral Framework for Monetary Operations","as well as expanding the list of collateral for monetary operations (inclusion of dinar corporate bonds issued by domestic companies, which meet the conditions of adequate creditworthiness, issued by the end of 2020, with the longest original maturity of ten years)",""],[1,"39","4","Reserve Requirement Incentives for Dinar Lending","With the obligatory reserve policy, the NBS continued to stimulate dinar and long-term sources of financing, and from July 2020, lending to the economy in dinars, supporting the Government's economic measures without jeopardizing price stability, by paying higher interest on the allocated dinar reserve requirement to banks that approve dinar loans on favourable terms in accordance with the Government's guarantee scheme",""],[1,"39","4","Foreign Exchange Market Stabilization Operations","Thanks to the timely and measured reactions of the NBS on the foreign exchange market in the form of foreign exchange sales in the conditions of increased uncertainty on the international financial market, the relative stability of the exchange rate was maintained",""],[1,"39","4","ECB Preventive Repo Liquidity Line","A preventive repo line with the ECB has also been established as an additional option to provide liquidity in euros in case of need",""],[1,"74","8","COVID-19 Fiscal and Monetary Support Package","in response to the crisis caused by the pandemic, a significant package of fiscal and monetary measures was applied, which supported the economy and citizens, preserved jobs, equipped the health system and provided assistance to the most vulnerable groups.",""]],"25":[[1,"5","2","Automatic Fiscal Stabilizers and Discretionary Crisis Response","Allow automatic fiscal stabilisers to accommodate crisis-induced economic fall-outs and further mitigate the impact on growth and employment by appropriate discretionary fiscal measures.",""],[1,"5","2","Fiscal Rules Framework","Adopt a credible and binding system of fiscal rules underpinning fiscal sustainability.",""],[1,"5","4","Deficit-Based Fiscal Rule Adoption","As part of a broader revision of the budget system law, during 2021 we will adopt a deficit-based fiscal rule ensuring that the level of public debt is set on a downward trajectory.",""],[1,"5","4","Budget System Law Revision for Fiscal Rules","As part of a broader revision of the budget system law, during 2021 we will adopt a deficit-based fiscal rule ensuring that the level of public debt is set on a downward trajectory.",""],[1,"13","8","Fiscal Stability and Debt Reduction Framework","Fiscal policy objectives are certainly aimed at maintaining fiscal stability and reducing the share of public debt in GDP.",""],[1,"15","4","Fiscal Responsibility Framework Strengthening","Strengthen the fiscal responsibility framework by improving the system of fiscal rules, increasing its credibility and making it more binding and capable of anchoring fiscal policy.",""],[1,"15","5","Budget System Law Amendment for Fiscal Rules","The Ministry of Finance has established a Working Group responsible for amending the Budget System Law, which contains provisions on fiscal rules.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"15","6","Revision of Fiscal Rules and Budget System Law","As part of the broader revision of the Law on Budget System, during 2021, special emphasis will be placed on changing the general rules related to public debt and general government deficit, and special rules related to the sustainable level of expenditures for salaries and pensions.",""],[1,"45","1","Fiscal Policy Stabilization and Crisis Response","The general commitment is to enable a gradual balancing and stabilization of public finances in the post-pandemic crisis, in order to reduce the share of public debt in GDP and create the basis for stable economic growth.",""],[1,"45","3","Budget System Law Reform","the planned changes to the Budget System Law will contribute to the stability of public finances and a sustainable fiscal framework, which will, among other things, redesign a set of fiscal rules, general and special, and define special measures and consequences in case of non-compliance.",""],[1,"49","6","Budget Rebalance for Pandemic Response","This rebalance enabled the operationalization of the Programme of Economic Measures, unhindered financing of the fight to preserve the health and lives of people, and the reduction of the negative economic consequences of the pandemic for the economy and citizens.",""],[1,"55","5","Medium-Term Fiscal Consolidation Framework","The medium-term fiscal framework envisages a gradual reduction of the general government deficit to 1.0% of GDP by 2023 and a decline in the share of public debt to 56.0% of GDP.",""],[1,"64","3","Timely Fiscal Crisis Response Capacity","Until then, it is necessary to ensure the possibility of a timely response of fiscal policy in the event of a deepening crisis.",""],[1,"77","2","New Fiscal Rules Adoption","Next year, a fiscal rule should be adopted, which would be in use from 2022, which defines the level of deficit and which ensures that the level of public debt is set on a downward trajectory.",""]],"26":[[1,"75","2","Public Financial Management Reform Programme 2021-2025","The Ministry of Finance has joined the draft of the Public Financial Management Reform Programme for the period 2021-2025.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"77","3","Budget Execution Information System Development","The Budget Execution Information System - BEIS - is part of the public financial management system that includes processes and procedures carried out by electronic communication with the Treasury Department within the Ministry of Finance.",""],[1,"78","1","National Statistics Data Exchange and Reporting Improvement","Improving the quality and transparency of national statistics is done through the promotion of comprehensive, timely and automatic data exchange between competent institutions.",""],[1,"78","1","General Government Data Dissemination and GFSM 2014 Transition","SORS (in cooperation with the Ministry of Finance and the NBS) from 2021 will submit data to the Extended General Data Dissemination System (e-GDDS).","Ministry of Finance | NBS"],[1,"78","1","Public Finance Data Conversion and Consolidation to GFSM 2014","The Sector for Macroeconomic and Fiscal Analysis and Projections of the Ministry of Finance, in cooperation with the IMF, was the first to initiate the process of converting public finance data from the national methodology into the GFSM 2014 methodology and consolidating them, covering all levels of the general government in order to enable a complete transition to the new methodology in terms of coverage, planning and reporting in the future.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"217","6","Tax Administration Business Process Re-engineering","Re-engineering of business processes to introduce international good practice into operating functions of the Tax Administration of the RS",""],[1,"217","8","Tax Administration Business Process Reengineering","Terms of Reference for the Re-engineering of business processes in tax-related affairs, including the training of trainers for the introduction of new functions in operating units of the Tax Administration of the Republic of Serbia has been written and sent to the World bank for approval.",""],[1,"217","10","Tax Administration Information System and E-Tax Services Upgrade","improvement of the IIS of the Tax Administration, extension of electronic services on the eTaxes Portal, replacement and improvement of the server, storage, and network infrastructure.",""],[1,"217","13","E-Fiscalisation System Procurement and Fiscalisation Law Implementation","For several activities, notably technical specification for the e-fiscalisation system integrator, bidding documentation has been written and submitted to the World Bank for comments. The procurement procedure launch is expected in the beginning of January 2021. The new Fiscalisation Law has been prepared, it has passed the",""],[1,"238","6","Tax Administration Modernization and Consolidation","We continue to support the continuation of this structural measure because there are areas that still need to be regulated, such as tax policy and excise duties on spirits.",""],[1,"239","3","Public Ex-Post Cost Reporting for ERP Activities","Prepare ex-post reports on actual costs, i.e. expenditures, for each activity, according to sources of financing (domestic vs. foreign).",""],[1,"239","4","Tax Administration Capacity Strengthening","Additionally strengthen and improve the capacities of the Tax Administration, not only from the aspect of easier and simpler application of tax regulations, but also in terms of clear and unambiguous interpretation of tax regulations.",""],[1,"239","4","Tax Guidance and Single Electronic Procedure for Inspectors","This problem could be solved by issuing guidelines for controversial issues or by developing a single electronic procedure for all tax inspectors (such as calculators for calculating taxes and contributions of flat-rate entrepreneurs).",""]],"27":[[1,"20","6","Unbundling of State-Owned Energy Companies","Finalize the unbundling of state-owned energy companies: - fully implement the long- delayed separation of Srbijagas and Elektromreža Srbije (EMS), - complete the functional unbundling of Elektroprivreda Srbije",""],[1,"21","3","Electricity Distribution Unbundling and EPS Reorganization Plan","The process of separation of PE EPS and DSO EPS is underway and will take place in accordance with the conclusion of the Government of 17 December 2020, the accepted Plan for the implementation of activities aimed at reorganizing \"EPS Distribution\", Belgrade.",""],[1,"21","3","Srbijagas Reorganization and Conversion to Joint Stock Company","the Plan envisages that the procedure of reorganization of PE Srbijagas and its transfer to a joint stock company will be completed by May 2021.",""],[1,"21","4","Legal and Functional Separation of the Electricity Distribution System Operator","When the Government of the Republic of Serbia approves this document, and when it enters into force, conditions will be created for a complete legal and functional separation of the distribution system operator.",""],[1,"21","4","Unbundling of Energy Activities at PE SRBIJAGAS","PE SRBIJAGAS continued continuous activities on the implementation of unbundling of energy activities in terms of creating business, financial and technical preconditions for functional and sustainable functioning of unbundled energy entities in open market conditions",""],[1,"21","5","Third-Party Access to Gas Infrastructure","provide third parties with access to gas infrastructure.",""],[1,"22","3","Natural Gas Transmission System Lease and Operating Agreements","Capacity Lease Agreement has been signed on an annual and monthly basis, as well as a Lease Agreement which regulates the lease of property for the purpose of performing the activities of the natural gas transmission system.",""],[1,"22","3","Natural Gas Supply Agreement Preparation","The Agreement on the delivery of natural gas for the needs of the transport system is being prepared.",""],[1,"22","3","Regulatory Harmonization for New Gas Companies","Further harmonization and preparation of a number of acts necessary for the operational work of new companies is forthcoming.",""],[1,"79","3","Energy Market Infrastructure Reform","reforms within the energy market will be aimed at improving infrastructure, in order to achieve reliability and facilitate trade in energy products in the national and cross-border markets.",""],[1,"81","8","Electricity Transmission Infrastructure Renewal and Cross-Border Capacity Expansion","Renewal of outdated electricity transmission infrastructure, increase of cross-border transmission capacities, as well as raising the security level of electricity supply to consumers in Serbia (Trans-Balkan Corridor electricity transmission system).",""],[1,"81","10","Gas Market Unbundling and Third-Party Access Reform","fully separate and certify Srbijagas, Transportgas and Jugorosgaz and develop competitiveness in the gas market, provide third party access to the gas network; fully implement the remaining interconnection reform measures it has committed to under the Interconnection Agenda, including the submission of applications for urgent licensing of Elektrosever in the context of the establishment of a regional electricity market.",""],[1,"81","10","Energy Infrastructure Access Reform","Provide third parties with access to gas infrastructure.",""],[1,"88","1","Energy Sector Reform and Modernization Programme","It is necessary to intensify reform measures and activities, harmonize the legislative framework with the EU acquis and achieve a greater degree of regional cooperation.",""],[1,"88","2","Gas and Electricity Sector Unbundling","Activities related to functional unbundling in the gas and electricity sectors continued22.",""],[1,"88","2","EPS Distribucija Reorganization and Unbundling Plan","The implementation of this plan will ensure the independence of the distribution system operator in terms of legal form, organization and separation from other activities not related to electric energy distribution activities and full compliance with the Law on Public Enterprises and the Law on Energy.",""],[1,"88","2","JP EPS Corporate Governance Action Plan Implementation","Further restructuring of JP EPS (PE Electric Power Industry of Serbia) and implementation of activities envisaged by the Corporate Governance Action Plan of JP EPS continues.",""],[1,"88","5","Unbundling and Reorganization of JP Srbijagas","Activities on unbundling of JP Srbijagas have continued23.",""],[1,"88","5","Strengthening of the Energy Agency's Regulatory Capacity","It is necessary for the Energy Agency of the Republic of Serbia (AERS) to expand its own capacities and enhance regulatory activities.",""],[1,"88","5","Revocation of Transmission System Operator Certification","Due to failure to comply with certification conditions, AERS revoked the certificate of the transmission system operator from the company Jugorosgaz - Transport d.o.o. Niš.",""]],"28":[[1,"79","3","Energy Management System for Energy Efficiency","the improvement of conditions for increasing energy efficiency continues through the implementation of the energy management system.",""],[1,"81","11","Energy Efficiency Legislative Harmonization and Financing Mechanism","Improvement of conditions for enhancing energy efficiency through harmonization of the legislative framework and establishing a sustainable mechanism for financing energy efficiency projects",""],[1,"81","12","Energy Efficiency Regulatory Harmonization and Incentive Scheme","Harmonization of regulations with EU regulations in the field of EE through the implementation of energy management systems, eco- design and providing incentives to improve energy efficiency.",""],[1,"81","14","Green Energy Transition and Energy Efficiency Investment","Make progress on the transition to green energy: strengthen human resources capacity and promote investment in energy efficiency, replace coal-fired power plants with gas and renewable energy power plants, measure and calculate energy",""],[1,"82","4","Sustainable Financing System for Energy Efficiency","To strengthen human resources capacities and encourage investment in energy efficiency, inter alia through the establishment of a sustainable financing system, and to initiate reforms to introduce electricity prices that clearly reflect costs, fully taking into account investment needs, obligations in terms of climate change and the implications of social security, as well as the reform of electricity price regulation.",""],[1,"82","4","Energy Efficiency Investment Expansion","It is necessary to increase investments in energy efficiency.",""],[1,"90","5","Energy Efficiency Financing System","In order to establish a sustainable energy efficiency financing system, the Law on Fees for Use of Public Resources introduced fees for energy efficiency.",""],[1,"90","5","Energy Efficiency Institutional and Capacity Strengthening","Improving energy efficiency requires increase of financial resources, establishment of better institutional framework and strengthening human capacity for energy efficiency at the Ministry of Mining and Energy, cooperation and coordination with stakeholders, as well as the introduction of the energy management system.","Ministry of Mining and Energy"],[1,"90","5","Budget Fund for Energy Efficiency Improvement Projects","Most of the projects financed from the Budget Fund for energy efficiency improvement is related to improving the thermal envelope of buildings and thermotechnical system.",""],[1,"95","11","Energy Efficiency Legislative Harmonization and Financing Mechanism","IMPROVEMENT OF CONDITIONS FOR ENHANCING ENERGY EFFICIENCY THROUGH HARMONIZATION OF THE LEGISLATIVE FRAMEWORK AND ESTABLISHING A SUSTAINABLE MECHANISM FOR FINANCING ENERGY EFFICIENCY PROJECTS",""],[1,"95","12","Energy Efficiency Law and Financing Reform","The reform will include the adoption of the new Law on Energy Efficiency in order to harmonize regulations in Serbia with EU regulations in the field of energy efficiency, enact bylaws, strengthen the capacity to implement energy efficiency policy, continue activities to finance energy efficiency and establish sustainable energy efficiency financing mechanism.",""],[1,"95","13","Energy Efficiency Law and Financing Mechanism","the draft of the new Law on Efficient Use of Energy was prepared, the adoption of which is expected at the beginning of 2021, after which the drafting of bylaws will begin.",""],[1,"95","13","Energy Efficiency Fee Collection and Project Financing","The collection of energy efficiency fees based on the Law on Fees has been taking place continuously throughout the year, and the financing of energy efficiency projects is carried out through the activities of the Budget Fund for Energy Efficiency Improvement, loans from international financial institutions and bilateral donations.",""],[1,"96","2","Energy Efficiency Capacity Building and Staffing Support","In order to strengthen the capacity of the Ministry of Mining and Energy in the sector responsible for energy efficiency, 3 new positions have been systematized, and capacity building is being done through IPA.","Ministry of Mining and Energy"],[1,"96","5","Sustainable Funding for Energy Efficiency","Provision of sustainable funding for energy efficiency",""],[1,"96","6","Adoption of Energy Efficiency Bylaws","Adoption of bylaws in order to ensure complete alignment with EU energy efficiency regulations",""],[1,"96","9","Energy Efficiency Policy Implementation Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity to implement energy efficiency policy",""],[1,"96","12","Sustainable Financing for Energy Efficiency Projects","Sustainable financing of energy efficiency projects established",""],[1,"96","13","Eco-Design Compliance for Energy-Efficient Products","Alignment with eco-design rules will ensure only energy-efficient products are marketed in Serbia, on the basis of which energy savings of about 100 ktoe are expected by 2023.",""],[1,"96","13","Sustainable Energy Efficiency Financing","Sustainable funding should increase energy efficiency, both in the public sector (by about 40% per project) and amongst enterprises and citizens.",""],[1,"96","13","Energy Efficiency Improvements for Large Consumers and Public Entities","Large-scale energy consumers and public-sector entities are expected to save about 1% of primary energy annually, which will increase competitiveness in the economy and reduce outlays by beneficiaries of public funds.",""],[1,"96","14","Energy Efficiency Project Financing Mechanism","Until the establishment of a sustainable financing mechanism, energy efficiency projects will be financed through the Program Activity: Incentives for Promotion of Energy Efficiency (since earmarked funds from fees do not flow directly into the Budget Fund), as well as through development loans and donor support.",""],[1,"96","14","Energy Efficiency Capacity Building and Awareness Activities","Capacity building will also be done through trainings within various projects.",""],[1,"96","14","IPA Energy Efficiency Awareness Campaigns","In addition, IPA projects will carry out activities to raise awareness of the importance of investing in energy efficiency.",""],[1,"96","15","Energy Efficiency Project Financing Mechanism","It is expected to establish a sustainable way of financing energy efficiency projects at the beginning of 2021.",""],[1,"97","1","Energy Efficiency Law Amendment and Institutional Support","It is expected to complete the amendments of the Law on Efficient Use of Energy at the beginning of 2021 with IPA technical assistance, as well as other activities for which the funds are provided in 2021 from IPA 2014 (around EUR 0.777 million and contribution from the RS budget of around EUR 0.086 million).",""],[1,"97","1","Product Conformity Assessment Body Establishment","In 2021, activities are also planned for the establishment of a body for conformity assessment of products under Directives 2009/125 and 2010/30 from IPA 2016 (EUR 0.525 million without contribution from the budget).",""],[1,"97","1","Energy Efficiency Project Financing Mechanism","Energy efficiency projects will be financed from the RS budget through the Budget Fund for Improvement of Energy Efficiency (EUR 4.17 million) and local self- government funds (around EUR 1.79 million - 30% contribution).",""],[1,"97","1","Energy Efficiency Fee-Based Financing System","From 2019, the funds for financing energy efficiency in the budget are collected from fees.",""],[1,"97","1","Energy Efficiency Investment and Technical Assistance Package","Funds for financing energy efficiency in 2021 are provided from donations (investments of around EUR 5.15 million from the SECO donations, and technical assistance for implementation of investments: SECO - EUR 0.43 million, KfW district heating V - around EUR 0.8 million, KfW - BMA EUR 0.11 million and CEB EUR 0.255 million) and loans (KfW district heating V - EUR 1.5 million, KfW- BMA EUR 0.2 million and CEB around EUR 0.483 million).",""],[1,"97","2","Sustainable Energy Efficiency Financing Mechanism","In 2022 it is planned to hire two new employees within the sustainable mechanism for financing, while the operating costs will be covered from the budget of the Republic of Serbia (around EUR 52,836 for salaries and around EUR 0,1 million for other costs, including the purchase of cars).",""],[1,"97","2","Energy Efficiency Project Financing","For financing energy efficiency projects EUR 9 million are expected from the budget (from fees), around EUR 1.93 million from contributions of local self-government units and around EUR 6.75 million from participation of citizens (not visible in the budget).",""],[1,"97","2","Sustainable Financing Support under IPA 2021","In addition, funds from IPA 2021 in the amount of EUR 4.25 million are planned to support operation of sustainable way of financing (out of which EUR 0.75 million for technical assistance and EUR 3.5 million for investments).",""],[1,"97","2","Energy Efficiency Law Implementation By-laws and Compliance Capacity","Bylaws related to the Law on Efficient Use of Energy are expected to be drafted in 2021, as well as the implementation of activities of raising awareness and establishing body for assessing compliance and increasing capacity of market inspection from IPA 2014 funds (around EUR 0.116 million and budget contribution of around EUR 0.013 million) and IPA 2016 funds (around EUR 0.413 million).",""],[1,"97","2","Energy Efficiency Investment Programme","Besides that, the implementation of investment activities is expected to be financed from loans (EUR 8.5 million - CEB, EUR 11 million KfW DHS phase V and EUR 5.2 million - KfW - BMA), along with supporting donations (EUR 5.27 million for all loans).",""],[1,"97","3","Sustainable Financing Mechanism for Energy Efficiency Projects","In 2023, the costs are increased for the employment and work of two new employees within the sustainable financing mechanism.",""],[1,"97","4","Energy Efficiency Projects","The implementation of energy efficiency projects will cut the cost of energy, which will also aid in reducing poverty.",""],[1,"98","5","Energy Efficiency Project Financing from the Budgetary Fund","Until sustainable funding has been ensured, projects will be financed from the budgetary Fund for Improvement of Energy Efficiency",""],[1,"202","2","Energy Efficiency Financing Mechanism and Legislative Harmonization","Improvement of conditions for enhancing energy efficiency through harmonization of the legislative framework and establishing a sustainable mechanism for financing energy efficiency projects",""],[1,"211","5","Energy Efficiency Financing Mechanism","Setting up of a sustained means of energy efficiency financing",""],[1,"212","1","Energy Efficiency Policy Capacity-Building and Compliance Bodies","Strengthening capacities for the pursuit of energy efficiency policy through capacity building in MME, LSUs, and market inspections, and by setting up several bodies for the evaluation of product conformity (in accord with directives 2009/125 and 2010/30), as well as the implementation of activities aimed at raising the energy efficiency awareness","MME | LSUs"],[1,"249","7","Energy Efficiency Legislative Harmonization and Financing Mechanism","Improvement of the conditions for enhancing energy efficiency through harmonization of the legislative framework and establishing a sustainable mechanism for financing energy efficiency projects includes strengthening the administrative capacity shown through increasing the number of employees in the Department for EE Improvement.",""]],"29":[[1,"81","13","Energy Development Strategy Implementation Programme","Program for the implementation of the Energy Development Strategy of the Republic of Serbia until 2025 with projections until 2030 for the period from 2017 to 2023",""],[1,"81","13","Law on Fees for the Use of Public Goods","Law on Fees for the Use of Public Goods",""]],"30":[[1,"17","9","Finalize the New Industrial Strategy","Use the results of the implemented smart specialization activities in order to finalize the new industrial strategy.",""],[1,"18","2","Industrial Policy Strategy Development and Action Plan Finalization","In December 2019, the Proposal of the Industrial Policy Strategy of the Republic of Serbia from 2021 to 2030 was prepared and put up for public discussion from 13 December 2019 to 3 January 2020.",""],[1,"79","4","New Industrial Policy for a Knowledge and Innovation Economy","a new industrial policy of Serbia is being implemented, which will be aimed at creating conditions for transforming the existing economy into a knowledge and innovation economy",""],[1,"83","9","Industry Development Policy Coordination and Digitalization Initiative","Creating a focused and better coordinated industry development policy through digitalization of business models of industrial production, increasing the volume of investments in industry and improving the technological structure of exports, in coordination with the Smart Specialization Strategy.",""],[1,"83","11","New Industrial Strategy Action Plan and Implementation","develop an action plan for the implementation of the new industrial strategy using the conclusions obtained from the implementation of smart specialization, as well as to start its implementation.",""],[1,"104","3","Industrial Policy Strategy 2021-2030","the Government of the Republic of Serbia has adopted the Industrial Policy Strategy of the Republic of Serbia 2021-2030",""],[1,"104","3","Digitalisation and Industrial Upgrading Initiative","The new industrial policy will create conditions for transforming the existing economy into a knowledge and innovation economy through digitalisation of business models of industrial production, development of higher stages of technological production, growth of investment quality, improvement of technological structure of exports, as well as development of promising industries that meet the requirements of environmental protection",""],[1,"115","8","Industrial Policy Coordination and Implementation Reform","This reform will help create a focused and better coordinated industry development policy, as well as improve the efficiency of instruments for its implementation.",""],[1,"115","9","Smart Specialization Strategy Implementation Support","The action plan for the implementation of this strategy will support the findings of the Smart Specialization Strategy, and special emphasis will be put on digital transformation, investment quality and improvement of the technological structure of exports, with support for the transition from linear to circular economy.",""],[1,"116","2","Industrial Policy Strategy Action Plan Implementation","a way to promote the performance of the economy and provide conditions for faster growth in the newly arisen circumstances is certainly to intensify the implementation of measures and activities envisaged by the Action Plan for Implementation of the Industrial Policy Strategy 2021-2030",""],[1,"116","2","Digital Transformation of the Economy","especially activities related to the digital transformation of the economy",""],[1,"116","2","Investment Promotion in Medium and High Technologies","encouraging investments in medium and high technologies",""],[1,"116","2","Business Environment Improvement Measures","improving the environment",""],[1,"116","3","Business Digitalisation Promotion and Education Programme","Promotion and education in the field of business digitalisation, with the implementation of the Programme Supporting the Digital Transformation of industry in the Republic of Serbia",""],[1,"116","4","Industrial Investment Promotion and Incentive Programme","Encouraging investments in industrial production through further improvement and adjustment of conditions and criteria for attracting investments, implementing investment incentive programmes, promoting the Republic of Serbia as an investment location, investment in the infrastructure of industrial zones and balancing regional development",""],[1,"116","5","Export-Oriented Industry Internationalisation Support Programme","Encouraging export-oriented industry sectors through the implementation of programmes to support internationalisation and entry into the supply chains of multinational companies",""],[1,"116","7","Industrial Production Business Model Digitization","Improving the digitization of business models of industrial production;",""],[1,"116","8","Industrial Innovation and Higher-Value Technological Production Development","Development of industry based on innovation and development of higher stages of technological production;",""],[1,"116","10","Export Technological Upgrading","Improving the technological structure of exports;",""],[1,"117","1","Industrial Restructuring Toward Innovative and Technology-Intensive Sectors","The Industrial Policy Strategy of the Republic of Serbia from 2021 to 2030 puts emphasis on industrial restructuring in the direction of approaching innovative and technologically intensive sectors, while moving away from labour- intensive sectors.",""],[1,"117","1","Industrial Policy Measures for Competitiveness and Investment Attraction","The Republic of Serbia will strive to use industrial policy measures to base its competitiveness and attraction of investments less on cheap labour, and more to invest in improving human resources through better education and training in accordance with requirements of the economy and to encourage the creation of innovative products with greater added value, by using the advantages of digital technologies in business and by economic cooperation of domestic companies with European and international partners.",""],[1,"117","1","Digitalization and Export Upgrading Initiative","Significant progress is expected in the areas of digitalization of the economy, innovation, quality of investments and improvement of the technological structure of exports.",""],[1,"117","2","Implementation of Industrial Policy Strategy Action Plan Measures","For the implementation of measures from the Action Plan for the implementation of the Industrial Policy Strategy of the Republic of Serbia from 2021-2030, for the areas of digitalization, investment and improvement of the technological structure of exports, funds will be provided from the RS budget as follows:",""],[1,"117","6","Industrial Zone Infrastructure Equipment Investment","In the next three years, amounts of EUR 12,250,000 per year are planned for infrastructural equipment of industrial zones.",""],[1,"117","6","Regulatory Measures to Promote Higher-Value Investment","Also, regulatory measures which should enable a higher level of investment in activities with higher added value and more balanced regional development are also planned.",""],[1,"117","7","Export Potential Identification and Support Services","Funds in the amount of EUR 83,333.33 per year will be allocated in the next three years for services related to the identification and support to the companies with export potential in areas of higher added value, especially in areas identified in the Smart Specialization Strategy.",""],[1,"117","8","Education-Economy Alignment and Training Measures","A significant number of measures from the Strategy and Action Plan, especially in the field of digitalization, innovation and circular economy, are dedicated to improving human resources through harmonization of education with the needs of the economy, but also numerous promotions and training that should trigger economic activity in these areas.",""],[1,"237","9","Industrial Policy Strategy Action Plan Implementation","In 2021, it is planned to start implementing activities from the Action Plan for the implementation of the Industrial Policy Strategy of the Republic of Serbia from 2021 to 2030, which will be adopted in early 2021, for",""],[1,"252","5","Implementation of the Industry Strategy","the description of the reform should not state: \"Creating a focused and better coordinated policy of industrial development through digitalization of business models of industrial production, increasing the volume of investment in industry and improving the technological structure of exports, and in coordination with the Smart Specialization Strategy\" but, \"Implementation of the Industry Strategy which should provide ... \"",""],[1,"252","6","Industrial Policy Strategy Framework and Action Plan","the Strategy of Industrial Policy of the Republic of Serbia from 2021 to 2030 defines a framework of goals and measures that will be applicable and easier to monitor the achieved results.",""],[1,"254","4","Business Environment Improvement through Digital Services","the proposal is to focus in the ERP on improving the business environment through greater use of digital services, and that the proposed activities be part of a set of measures focused on business facilitation.",""],[1,"255","1","Digital Economy Development and Industrial Modernization","The proposal is that the concept of digital economy also includes: digitalization of work processes and service provision, development of new digital products and services, expansion of domestic software production, application of the IND 4.0 concept in the modernization of industry, etc.",""],[1,"255","8","Business Entity Financial Support Programme","The new component of the structural reform related to the program of financial support to business entities is not currently elaborated in more detail, as it will be developed within the first activity 1.1.",""],[1,"256","10","Sustainable and Green Recovery Support","Support for sustainable and green recovery and development in the field of Agriculture, industry and services, bearing in mind that the circular economy is only part of green recovery/development, and that it implies the transition to clean energy in the whole real sector (not only energy), sustainable and green transport, economic development of cities and municipalities towards sustainable, green and smart cities, research and development in the field of green development, integration of appropriate accounting standards and business reporting, encouragement of green sources of financing, etc.",""]],"31":[[1,"19","3","Timely Consultation on Draft Business Laws","Ensure that companies and all social partners are consulted in a timely manner on all draft new laws relating to their business.",""],[1,"19","4","Public Consultation and Hearing Framework for Regulation-Making","state administration bodies are obliged to announce the start of work on new regulations and conduct ex ante analyses that should indicate key problems and potential solutions, as well as to involve the public in these processes through a consultation process.",""],[1,"19","5","Public Consultation Improvement for Business-Related Laws","Further improve the process of public consultation by involving companies and social partners regarding the adoption and implementation of all new laws relating to their business.",""],[1,"37","4","Administrative Procedure Acceleration and Digitalization Reform","Acceleration of all administrative procedures that accompany these activities, tax relief of the economy in order to increase its competitiveness, signing agreements to ensure the preservation of existing and opening of new foreign markets, more intensive and efficient infrastructure works are just some of the measures to provide sound foundations for growth of the potential GDP.",""],[1,"79","5","Business Regulatory Simplification and Guillotine Procedures","it is expected that the process of simplification and guillotine procedures for business entities will continue",""],[1,"83","16","Digitalization of Administrative Procedures for Public Services","Improvement of the quality of public services through optimization and digitalization of administrative procedures - e-paper",""],[1,"83","17","Unified Public Register of Administrative Procedures and Business Conditions","Establishment of the Unified Public Register of Administrative Procedures and Other Business Conditions, simplification and abolition of redundant procedures (guillotine of regulations) and digitalization of the most frequent",""],[1,"83","18","ePaper Administrative Simplification Programme","Program for the simplification of administrative procedures and regulations \"ePaper\" for the period 2019-2021",""],[1,"84","3","Administrative Procedures Optimization and Digitalization","a list of administrative procedures for citizens is planned, as well as their optimization and digitalization.",""],[1,"84","9","Business Environment Predictability Measures","make additional efforts to increase the predictability of the business environment.",""],[1,"120","2","Electronic Construction Permit Issuance System","the introduction of the system of electronic issuance of construction permits (e-permits)",""],[1,"120","3","Doing Business Improvement Programme and Action Plan","The Government of RS adopted a new Programme for improving the position of the Republic of Serbia on the ranking list of the World Bank on the ease of doing business - Doing business for the period 2020-2023 with the accompanying Action Plan on June 12, 2020.",""],[1,"120","5","Law on Fees for Use of Public Goods","In December 2018, the Law on Fees for Use of Public Goods was adopted (\"Official Gazette of the RS\", No. 95/18), which unifies in a single place all fees paid for the use of natural resources, goods of general interest and goods in general use (until then these fees were regulated by 19 separate laws).",""],[1,"120","5","ePaper Administrative Procedure Simplification Programme","In July 2019, the Government also adopted the Programme for Simplification of Administrative Procedures and Regulations \"ePaper\" for the period 2019-2021 with the accompanying Action Plan for the Implementation of the Programme which provides for concrete measures and actions to streamline 890 procedures and the establishment of a unified public registry of administrative procedures.",""],[1,"123","4","Public Service Administrative Procedure Optimization and Digitalization","STRUCTURAL REFORM 9: IMPROVEMENT OF THE QUALITY OF PUBLIC SERVICES THROUGH OPTIMIZATION AND DIGITALIZATION OF ADMINISTRATIVE PROCEDURES - e-PAPER",""],[1,"123","5","Administrative Procedure Simplification and Single Public Registry","Improving the quality of public service delivery is a multi-year reform process that takes place, among other things, through the simplification of administrative procedures (elimination of redundant by guillotine and simplification of other administrative procedures) for businesses and citizens, as well as the establishment of a Single Public Registry of Administrative Procedures and Other Business Conditions (hereinafter: the Register).",""],[1,"123","5","Single Electronic Contact Point Establishment","The establishment of the Single Register of administrative procedures and other business conditions is the starting point for the establishment of the single electronic contact (PSEC), which is an obligation in accordance with the Services Directive 2006/123/EC, the transposition of which is provided for in Article 59 of the SAA.",""],[1,"124","1","E-Paper Administrative Procedure Simplification and Digitization","Through e-Paper so far: a database of 2,618 administrative procedures for the economy has been created, which is the basis for the establishment of a public Register; 4 procedures were abolished, which resulted in annual savings for the economy of almost EUR 30 million; 130 were completely simplified (savings of an additional EUR 2 million) and optimization has started for another 367 administrative procedures; the e-Permit platform has been established and it is connected to all necessary services (e-Payment and data exchange bus between public administration bodies and organizations); 27 administrative procedures were digitized, while the digitization of another 73 procedures is expected to take place by the middle of 2021.",""],[1,"124","2","Administrative Procedures and Regulations Simplification Programme (e-PAPER)","The reform has been defined by the Programme for the simplification of administrative procedures and regulations 'e-PAPER\" for the period 2019-2021;",""],[1,"124","2","E-Government Development Programme","e-Government Development Programme for the period 2020-2022;",""],[1,"124","2","Public Administration Reform Strategy","Public Administration Reform Strategy for the period 2021-2030.",""],[1,"124","3","Digitalization of Administrative Procedures","one of the focuses of this reform is the digitalization of as many administrative procedures as possible for the smooth functioning of the economy and life of the citizens even in extraordinary circumstances.",""],[1,"124","6","Optimization of Administrative Procedures","Optimization of administrative procedures for the economy and citizens",""],[1,"124","8","Legal Framework for Establishing and Maintaining the Register","Adoption of laws and bylaws for the establishment and maintenance of the Register",""],[1,"125","1","Administrative Procedure Simplification and Optimization Reform","Administrative costs for the economy are expected to be reduced by 15-20%, based on analysis and proposals for simplification and optimization, as well as the possible abolition of at least 50% of the most frequent and most expensive administrative procedures.",""],[1,"125","1","Business Information Register for Public Administration Proceedings","A positive impact on competitiveness will be achieved by establishing a Register with all the necessary information for the economy in proceedings before the public administration, which creates a safer, more transparent and predictable business environment.",""],[1,"125","2","Administrative Procedure Digitalization and Public Service Simplification","Within this ERP cycle, funds in the amount of EUR 360,000 are planned for listing of administrative requirements, EUR 210,000 for optimization of procedures, EUR 2.12 million for digitalization of administrative procedures and improvement of the register of administrative procedures, and EUR 40,000 for creating public services on the principle of business episodes.",""],[1,"133","3","Electronic Public Service Delivery Reform","Once implemented, the reform will support recovery from the negative socio-economic consequences of the pandemic, as well as overcoming possible other/future emergencies in general, by enabling the provision of developed services electronically - i.e. online - without actually visiting the competent authority of the state administration.",""]],"32":[[1,"82","9","Land Consolidation Process Improvement","Improvement of the land consolidation process",""],[1,"82","10","Regulatory Framework for Consolidation Process","The reform implies the establishment of a regulatory framework for the consolidation process, as well as the implementation of IT and technical conditions to support professional supervision in this area, with the aim of creating preconditions for the development of agricultural production and construction of public infrastructure.",""],[1,"82","10","IT and Technical Support for Professional Supervision","The reform implies the establishment of a regulatory framework for the consolidation process, as well as the implementation of IT and technical conditions to support professional supervision in this area, with the aim of creating preconditions for the development of agricultural production and construction of public infrastructure.",""],[1,"82","12","Agricultural Financial Support System Digitalization and Automation","Improvement of the financial support system for agriculture through digitalization and process automation",""],[1,"82","13","Integrated Control and Management System for Farmer Subsidies","Establishment of the Integrated Control and Management System (ICMS) which will digitalize and automate the process to improve the implementation of the system of financial support to farmers and facilitate access to available subsidies, increase transparency and more effective agricultural policy making.",""],[1,"250","4","Pilot Land Consolidation Activities","SR 4: Improvement of the land consolidation process envisages the implementation of pilot land consolidation activities",""],[1,"250","7","Agricultural Financial Support System Digitalization","Improvement of the financial support system of for agriculture through digitalization and process automation.",""],[1,"251","1","Rural Development IT System Implementation","a software solution for rural development (RD IT) for automatic processing of IPARD requirements and its full implementation is expected soon.",""],[1,"251","1","LPIS Integration and IACS Pilot","it is planned to connect it with LPIS, which will be used to pilot IACS.",""],[1,"251","1","Electronic Submission System for Bee Incentive Applications","The Directorate for Agrarian Payments has developed a pilot solution for the electronic submission of applications for incentives for bees, and it is planned to continue work on the development of other software solutions.",""],[1,"251","1","Procedural Improvement for the Directorate for Agrarian Payments","At the same time, we are working on improving the existing procedures that are within the competence of the Directorate.",""],[1,"251","1","IPARD Agency Institutional Preparation","The Directorate for Agrarian Payments \"pilots\" all these activities by implementing IPARD I, and the Government has assigned it the role of IPARD agency, which enables the gradual preparation of users and administration for EU requirements to be implemented after EU membership.",""],[1,"251","2","Agricultural Budget Support Payment Digitalization","SR 5: Improvement of the financial support system for agriculture through digitalization and process automation states the need to improve the mechanism of payment of budget support to agriculture, which is certainly a necessary step in the reform of the agricultural sector.",""]],"33":[[1,"43","2","Export Capacity Expansion and Trade Facilitation Measures","The activation of new and expansion of existing export capacities, more favourable trade relations, but also the abolition of 100% tax on products delivered to Kosovo and Metohija will contribute to the mitigation of negative risks.",""],[1,"80","2","WTO Accession Legal Alignment","the main obstacle in the past period was the inconsistency of domestic legislation regulating the trade of GMO products.",""],[1,"80","2","Trade Barrier Removal and Customs Facilitation","It is necessary to further strengthen regional cooperation, identify and remove barriers to trade, especially technical and phytosanitary measures and facilitate customs procedures,",""],[1,"80","2","Single Digital Service for Technical Regulations","and to establish a single digital service related to technical regulations, with the aim of improving product quality and raising economic competitiveness.",""],[1,"226","3","WTO Accession Negotiation and Regulatory Alignment","Negotiations for accession to WTO - bilateral negotiations, adoption of regulations aligned with WTO rules and principles",""],[1,"226","6","CEFTA Trade Facilitation and Mutual Recognition Programme","Implementation of Additional Protocol 5 on trade facilitation: development of the programme of mutual recognition of documents to be submitted in the import and export of goods, as well as other initiatives for trade facilitation within CEFTA",""],[1,"226","8","CEFTA Trade Facilitation Decisions","On 18 December 2019 Decision on the validation process for mutual recognition of national programmes of certified business entities in CEFTA Parties with respect to security and safety (AEO) was adopted, and on 25 February 2020 Decision on Facilitation of Fruits and Vegetables Trade in CEFTA was adopted.",""],[1,"226","9","Ratification and Implementation of Additional Protocol 6 on Service Trade","MAP REA - CEFTA: Adoption and implementation of the Law on Ratification of Additional Protocol 6 on Service Trade",""],[1,"226","11","CEFTA Service Trade and E-Trade Regulatory Cooperation","National Parliament adopted the Law on Confirmation of Additional Protocol 6 on 24 February 2020, Plan of dialogue on regulatory issues of eTrade in CEFTA was adopted, it was agreed to launch intraregional regional cooperation in the pilot sector of tourism",""],[1,"226","12","CEFTA Dispute Settlement Additional Protocol Negotiation and Adoption","Negotiations and adoption of Additional protocol on dispute settlement",""],[1,"226","15","National Trade Facilitation Action Plan Implementation","Adoption of the new Action Plan of the National Coordination Body for Trade Facilitation for 2020-2021 and implementation of defined activities",""],[1,"241","5","WTO Accession Continuation","the continuation of WTO accession should remain part of this reform",""]],"34":[[1,"80","4","Circular Migration Support Framework","the key challenge in the labor market in Serbia is to stop the departure of highly educated people abroad (so-called \"brain drain\") and attract talent from the country and abroad, which will be solved by creating conditions for monitoring, encouraging and supporting circular migration.",""],[1,"80","4","Returning Point Diaspora Engagement Project","The activities of the project \"Returning Point\", within the broader activities of the platform Serbia Creates, activities of mapping and establishing cooperation with our higher education population in the diaspora have begun, in order to improve the conditions of their return and starting business in Serbia.",""],[1,"86","21","Unified Economic Migration Data Collection System","The reform includes the development of a unified system for collecting data on economic migration, strengthening the",""],[1,"87","4","Diaspora Monitoring and Return Facilitation Mechanism","mechanism for monitoring the Serbian diaspora and general economic migration, as well as improving and implementing procedures for the return of the diaspora.",""],[1,"87","4","Tax and Employment Incentives for Diaspora Return","In order to encourage return, tax and other incentives related to new employment will be additionally promoted, through communication with the economy and returnees.",""],[1,"87","4","Diaspora Dialogue and Research Initiative","One of the steps in building trust with the diaspora will be to establish dialogue and understanding through activities and research.",""],[1,"165","3","Economic Migration Strategy","The Government of Serbia, in order to regulate the area of economic migration, has adopted the Strategy on Economic Migration of the Republic of Serbia for the period 2021-2027 (\"Official Gazette of the RS\", No. 21/20).",""],[1,"167","1","Administrative Environment Improvement for Circular and Economic Migration","IMPROVEMENT OF THE ADMINISTRATIVE ENVIRONMENT FOR ENCOURAGING, SUPPORTING AND TRACKING CIRCULAR AND ECONOMIC MIGRATIONS",""],[1,"167","2","Economic Migration Data and Diaspora Engagement Reform","There is a need to develop a unified system for collecting data on economic migration, strengthening the mechanism for monitoring the Serbian diaspora and general economic migration, as well as improving and implementing procedures for the return of the diaspora.",""],[1,"167","4","Action Plan for Implementation of the Strategy on Economic Migration","Implementation of the Action Plan for the period 2021-2023 for the implementation of the Strategy on Economic Migration of the Republic of Serbia for the period 2021-2027.",""],[1,"167","5","Migration Monitoring Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity of institutions responsible for monitoring migration movements and creating new groups, bodies, etc.",""],[1,"167","7","Administrative Framework Improvement for Employment and Return Procedures","Improving the administrative framework and promoting tax incentives and improved procedures for employment and return to the country",""],[1,"168","6","Action Plan for the Strategy on Economic Migration 2021-2023","In order to implement the Strategy on Economic Migration of the Republic of Serbia for the period 2021-2027 in the plan for 2021 is the adoption of the Action Plan for the period 2021-2023.",""],[1,"168","6","Institutional Capacity Strengthening with GIZ Support","The strengthening of the institutional capacities of the institutions will be carried through with the support of the German Organization for International Cooperation (GIZ), whose support for the entire period will be specified after the adoption of the AP.",""],[1,"168","6","Public-Private Partnership for Circular Migration and Diaspora Return","The organization dealing with circular migration and the return of the highly educated diaspora was established as a public-private partnership.",""],[1,"168","7","Administrative Framework Improvement for Return Facilitation","Improving the administrative framework and eliminating obstacles to return will require additional human capacity, while other activities will require an increase in funding for goods and services.",""],[1,"169","2","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Migration Programmes","Strengthening institutional capacities independently of the Action Plan, based on the Implementation Agreement related to the programmes \"Migration for Development II\" and \"Migration & Diaspora\"",""],[1,"204","2","Administrative Environment Improvement for Circular and Economic Migration","Improvement of the administrative environment for encouraging, supporting and tracking circular and economic migrations",""],[1,"209","6","Administrative Environment Improvement for Circular and Economic Migration","Improvement of the administrative environment for encouraging, supporting and tracking circular and economic migrations",""],[1,"244","5","Circular and Economic Migration Monitoring Capacity Improvement","In addition to improving the capacity to monitor circular and economic migration, the proposed reform has a proactive approach to the diaspora as well as foreign citizens, in order to improve the administrative framework and implement programmes aimed at attracting human capital in demand from abroad.",""]],"35":[[1,"87","13","Central Electronic Health Services","The reform implies the establishment of central electronic health services that will greatly increase the efficiency of the system, eliminate unnecessary patient involvement and contribute to the quality of diagnostics and treatment.",""],[1,"87","13","Single Electronic Health Card System","The single electronic health card will establish a mechanism of digital authorized access to the patient's information and will enable him electronic access to his own health information.",""],[1,"87","13","Digital Radiological Imaging and Central Storage","Also, the introduction of digital technologies for radiological imaging and central storage of radiological imaging is planned.",""],[1,"175","6","Digital Health System Digitization","Digitization of the health system contributes to the efficiency of the health system, higher quality of diagnostics and treatment and enables authorized access to information crucial for making clinical decisions.",""],[1,"175","6","Single Electronic Health Card","The single electronic health card will establish a mechanism of digital authorized access to patient information, which will enable patients the electronic access to their own health information and active participation in the process of diagnosis and treatment.",""],[1,"175","6","Central Electronic Health Services","The establishment of central electronic health services will greatly increase the efficiency of the system, eliminate unnecessary patient involvement and contribute to the quality of diagnostics and treatment.",""],[1,"175","6","Digital Radiological Imaging and Central Storage","the introduction of digital technologies for radiological imaging and central storage of radiological imaging has opened the door for projects that will improve the quality of diagnostics and the efficiency of the entire system.",""],[1,"175","8","Electronic Health Records Connectivity","Connecting health care institutions to the central system of electronic health records",""],[1,"175","9","Central Electronic Health Services Platform","Establishment of central electronic health services - e-Sick leave",""],[1,"175","10","National Radiology Imaging Platform Expansion","Expansion of the national radiology imaging platform",""],[1,"176","6","Introduction of e-Sick Leave","The amount of EUR 1,500,000 has been allocated for the activity of introducing e-Sick leave;",""],[1,"176","6","Expansion of the National Radiology Platform","for the expansion of the national radiology platform EUR 2 million;",""],[1,"176","6","Artificial Intelligence Solutions in Radiology","for the application of solutions based on artificial intelligence in the field of radiology, EUR 1 million were allocated.",""],[1,"176","7","Electronic Health Records Implementation","The implementation of the planned activities will improve access to health care primarily through the use of electronic health records.",""]],"36":[[1,"88","6","Energy Distribution Network Modernization","The introduction of a modern supervisory and management system and the installation of state- of-the-art equipment is a prerequisite for enhancement of the energy distribution network.",""],[1,"89","1","Transmission System Development and Investment Plan","Transmission System Development Plan for the period 2020-2029 and the Transmission System Investment Plan for the period 2020-2022 envisage provision of secure electricity supply, development of the electricity market at the national and regional level, increase of transmission capacities and development of corridors of regional and pan-European importance.",""],[1,"89","1","Mandatory Advanced Metering System Regulations","The introduction of mandatory functionalities of advanced metering systems in the relevant regulations will help the introduction of compatible advanced metering systems in Serbia, which is especially important in the natural gas sector where 32 natural gas distribution system operators operate.",""],[1,"89","1","Gas Transmission SCADA System Establishment","The establishment of the SCADA system for remote monitoring and control of the gas transmission system has begun.",""],[1,"89","1","Substation Installation and Distribution Network Modernization","Works on the installation of new substations and the introduction of mobile substations have been intensified, while the automation and modernization of medium voltage distribution networks continue.",""],[1,"89","2","Non-discriminatory Third-Party Access to Gas Pipeline","It is necessary to ensure non-discriminatory third party access to the gas pipeline from the direction of Hungary in accordance with the Law on Energy.",""],[1,"89","2","Bulgaria-Serbia Gas Interconnection Project","Bulgaria-Serbia gas interconnection project will enable diversification of gas supply routes and sources and connection with the Southern Gas Corridor.",""],[1,"89","2","Natural Gas Transmission System Operating Rules","AERS has approved the rules on the operation of the natural gas transmission system Gastrans d.o.o. Novi Sad governing relations between operators and users, which is to be connected to the Bulgarian and Hungarian national gas pipeline systems.",""],[1,"89","3","Electricity Generation Capacity Expansion and Grid Infrastructure Development","Investment in the construction of new, technologically advanced, production capacities, and those that use renewable energy sources, would contribute to the preservation of the environment, reduction of losses in electric power production and satisfy the growing demand for electricity and gas.",""],[1,"89","3","Hydropower Rehabilitation and Upgrade Programme","Units in HPP Zvornik and HPP Djerdap 1 have been upgraded (one of the 6 units remains to be upgraded) which will contribute to higher power generation capacity and lower maintenance costs.",""],[1,"93","4","Trans-Balkan Corridor Electricity Transmission Infrastructure Upgrade","The construction of transmission lines and upgrades of transformer stations within the Trans-Balkan Corridor (Phase I) includes a set of projects for the renovation of outdated electricity transmission infrastructure, in order to raise the level of security of electricity supply to consumers in Serbia and facilitate trade in energy products on national and cross-border markets.",""],[1,"93","6","Pančevo-Reșica 2x400 kV Interconnection Transmission Line","Double interconnection transmission line 2x400 kV Pančevo - Rešica, between Serbia and Romania, was released under voltage in December 2017 (from TS Pančevo 2 to the border with Romania).",""],[1,"93","7","400 kV Transmission Line and Substation Upgrade","Construction of 400 kV transmission line TS Kragujevac 2 - TS Kraljevo 3 (in progress), with raising the voltage level in TS Kraljevo 3 to 400 kV, which means construction of 400 kV plant in TS Kraljevo 3.",""],[1,"93","8","Western Serbia Transmission Network Upgrade","Raising the voltage level of the transmission network of Western Serbia to 400 kV voltage level between TS Obrenovac and TS Bajina Bašta, which means a new double 2x400 kV transmission line TS Obrenovac - TS Bajina Bašta, upgrade of TS 220/35kV Bajina Bašta in TS 400/220/35kV Bajina Bašta and equipping two 400 kV high-voltage transmission line fields in TS 400/220 kV",""],[1,"94","1","Transmission Substation and Line Design Preparation","Obrenovac - development of design for construction permit for TS Bajina Bašta with an access road and the preparation of an Environmental Impact Assessment Study are in progress.",""],[1,"94","2","Double Interconnection Transmission Line Project","Double interconnection transmission lines 2x400 kV Bajina Bašta (Serbia) - Višegrad (BiH) - Pljevlja (Montenegro) with equipping a single conductor system - a project for a construction permit and an Environmental Impact Assessment Study are underway.",""],[1,"94","6","Reconstruction and Upgrading of TS Kraljevo 3 and TS Kragujevac 2","Reconstruction and upgrading of TS Kraljevo 3 and reconstruction of TS Kragujevac 2, needed for the introduction of the new transmission line Kragujevac - Kraljevo*",""],[1,"94","7","Kragujevac-Kraljevo Transmission Line Construction","Construction of the Kragujevac - Kraljevo transmission line*",""],[1,"94","8","Obrenovac-B.Bašta Transmission Line Construction","Construction of the transmission line Obrenovac - B.Bašta **",""],[1,"94","10","Overhead Power Line Construction","The start of construction of overhead power line is related to obtaining the adequate amount of the donation and signing the loan agreement",""],[1,"95","1","Trans-Balkan Electricity Transmission Corridor Construction","Construction of the electricity transmission system Trans-Balkan Corridor, for the transmission line will be financed from EMS AD's own funds, donations and loans.",""],[1,"210","7","Energy Market Development and Energy Infrastructure Construction","Energy market development coupled with energy infrastructure construction",""],[1,"210","8","Backbone Gas Pipeline Construction","Construction of the backbone gas pipeline Nis - Dimitrovgrad",""],[1,"210","11","Reconstruction and Upgrading of TS Kraljevo 3","Reconstruction and upgrading of TS Kraljevo 3 and reconstruction of TS Kragujevac 2, which is critical for the launching of the new transmission line Kragujevac - Kraljevo",""],[1,"210","11","Reconstruction of TS Kragujevac 2","Reconstruction and upgrading of TS Kraljevo 3 and reconstruction of TS Kragujevac 2, which is critical for the launching of the new transmission line Kragujevac - Kraljevo",""],[1,"210","13","Reconstruction and Extension of TS Kragujevac 2 and TS Kraljevo 3","The reconstruction and extension contract for TS Kragujevac 2 and TS Kraljevo 3 has been agreed with the contractor and approved by the KfW bank.",""],[1,"210","14","Kragujevac-Kraljevo Transmission Line Construction","Construction of the transmission line Kragujevac - Kraljevo",""],[1,"210","16","Transmission Line Construction Project","The construction contract for the TL is signed and works on the construction of the transmission line have begun.",""],[1,"210","17","Technical Documentation Preparation for TL Obrenovac - Bajina Basta","Preparation of technical documentation for TL Obrenovac - Bajina Basta",""],[1,"249","4","Main Gas Pipeline Construction Project","it is suggested to return this project to ERP and monitor the implementation",""],[1,"249","4","Power Line Technical Documentation Preparation","the delay in the realization of the preparation of technical documentation for power line Obrenovac - B. Bašta, is not stated",""],[1,"249","4","Reform Financing Source Specification","It is necessary to indicate the sources of financing the reform",""],[1,"249","5","Main Gas Pipeline Construction Project (Niš-Dimitrovgrad)","The construction of the main gas pipeline Niš-Dimitrovgrad is a project of high priority for the Republic of Serbia.",""]],"37":[[1,"49","18","Road Infrastructure Investment Acceleration","increase in investments in road infrastructure and acceleration of the execution of capital investments.",""],[1,"81","2","Road Sector Contracting and Performance-Based Maintenance Reform","SR 3. Improving the capacity and quality of road traffic through the reform of the road sector in terms of establishing a contractual relationship between RS and state road managers and further application of a new way of contracting performance-based maintenance",""],[1,"91","2","Transport Inspection Services Improvement","it is necessary to improve the work of inspection services",""],[1,"91","2","Border Crossing Procedure Facilitation","facilitate procedures at border crossings",""],[1,"91","2","Road and Railway Infrastructure Improvement","improve road and railway infrastructure",""],[1,"91","2","Road Safety Enhancement Measures","enhance the level of road safety",""],[1,"91","3","Local Roads Reconstruction Programme","The reconstruction of 5,000 km of local roads is to commence.",""],[1,"91","4","Road Toll Adjustment and Maintenance Financing Reform","Road tolls ought to be adjusted to ensure they correspond to the costs necessary for the maintenance of the road infrastructure.",""],[1,"91","4","Performance-Based Road Maintenance System","The transition to a new performance-based regular road maintenance system is under way.",""],[1,"91","4","European Electronic Toll Collection Regulation","Regulation on European Electronic Toll Collection has been adopted for more efficient toll collection and processing of transactions at toll stations.",""],[1,"91","6","Traffic Safety Management and Road Safety Regulation Reform","Conditions are being created for traffic safety management through changes in regulations, in order to reduce traffic accidents.",""]],"38":[[1,"79","3","Railway Infrastructure Reconstruction and Expansion","the reconstruction of existing and construction of new sections continues.",""],[1,"82","3","Railways Regulatory Harmonization and Safety Enhancement Reform","Railways reform through harmonization of the regulatory framework and enhancement of rail transport safety",""],[1,"82","5","Railway Regulatory Framework Harmonization","Improvement of the regulatory framework through the adoption and implementation of a new Methodology for calculating the price of access to railway of laws in the field of railways infrastructure and harmonization with the IV package of railway EU regulations.",""],[1,"82","5","Railway Renewal, Reconstruction and Modernization","In addition to the renewal, reconstruction and modernization of the railways, the modernization of road-railway crossings is also planned.",""],[1,"82","7","Railway Reform Implementation and Regulatory Strengthening","continue the process of implementing railway reform, in particular by regulating contractual relations between infrastructure managers and operators in an economical and transparent manner, further implement adopted legislation and strengthen institutional capacity.",""],[1,"82","7","Transport Infrastructure Maintenance Planning and Border Crossing Simplification","adopt realistic plans for the maintenance of road and railway infrastructure and their financial aspects and start implementing them; harmonize and simplify procedures at border crossings for rail and road traffic; improve the prioritization and preparation of transport infrastructure to achieve the best value for money.",""],[1,"82","7","Railway Market Opening and Regulatory Capacity Building","focus on the implementation of railway reform, including market opening, network statement, infrastructure management and market monitoring, as well as to strengthen the capacity of the railway regulatory body.",""],[1,"91","5","Railway Network Reconstruction and Modernization","A total of 324.7 km of regional and local railways were reconstructed and built, while 227.3 km of main railways were reconstructed, modernized and built, and works are underway on another 116.2 km of regional and local, as well as 143.7 km of main railways.",""],[1,"91","5","Belgrade-Budapest High-Speed Railway Construction","As part of the project for the construction of the Belgrade-Budapest high-speed railway, works are underway on the Belgrade-Novi Sad line (expected to be commissioned by the end of 2021).",""],[1,"99","7","Railway Capital Investment Programme","In addition, investments in capital projects affect the growth of industrial production, employment of the domestic economy, reduction of unemployment and GDP growth.",""]],"39":[[1,"98","8","Railway Infrastructure Access Charge Methodology Reform","the adoption and application of a new Methodology for Calculating Railway Infrastructure Access Charges in line with the Regulation on the method and modalities of calculating the costs incurred as a direct result of operating the train service (\"Official Gazette of the RS\", No. 48/19) i.e. the Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2015/909, which aims at cost-based access prices and enabling a more predictable market",""],[1,"98","8","Railway Safety Improvement at Level Crossings","improving safety, especially with regard to level crossings (contribution to the achievement of SDG 11.2. By 2030, provide access to safe, affordable, accessible and sustainable transport systems for all, improve road safety), with the view to reducing the number of accidents",""],[1,"98","8","Railway Law Harmonisation with EU Fourth Railway Package","harmonising the law with the IV package of regulations, which will contribute to creating efficient and a sustainable railway system",""],[1,"98","10","Railway Legislation Harmonisation with EU Fourth Railway Package","Harmonisation of railways legislation with EU Fourth Railway Package",""],[1,"98","12","Railway Infrastructure Access Charge Calculation Methodology","Application of new Methodology for Calculating Railway Infrastructure Access Charges",""],[1,"99","7","Railway Sector Reform","The ultimate goal of the reform of the railway sector is to increase competitiveness, not only within the sector, but also to raise competitiveness in relation to other modes of transport.",""],[1,"99","7","Efficiency Improvement of Restructured Railway Companies","Work is still underway to increase the efficiency of restructured companies, but given the current level of market development, railway users already benefit in terms of carrier choice.",""],[1,"99","8","Railway Infrastructure Access Charge Methodology Finalization and Implementation","The Methodology for Calculating Railway Infrastructure Access Charges is currently being finalized.",""],[1,"99","8","Railway Safety Alignment with the Fourth Railway Package","the activities related to alignment with the 4th package and safety improvement begun.",""],[1,"99","9","Railway Sector COVID-19 Impact Monitoring","the impact of COVID-19 on economic activities is actively monitored, with the aim of minimizing its impact on the railway sector.",""],[1,"100","4","Railway Project Implementation Efficiency and Access Charge Methodology Reform","More efficient implementation of projects by Infrastruktura Železnica Srbije, provision of alternative routes, and removal of all obstacles to eliminate delays, development of a new Methodology that is in the function of the impact of COVID-19",""],[1,"202","3","Railways Regulatory Harmonisation and Safety Enhancement Reform","Railways reform through harmonisation of the regulatory framework and enhancement of rail transport safety",""],[1,"212","8","Railways Safety and Regulatory Framework Reform","Railways reform through enhancement of rail transport safety and improvement of regulatory framework",""],[1,"212","9","Railway Infrastructure Access Pricing Methodology","Devising of a new methodology for calculating the price for access to railway infrastructure",""],[1,"213","1","Railway Access Price Methodology Development","On 14 July 2020 the Draft Methodology and models for the price calculation were also presented.","MCTI | IRS"],[1,"213","2","Railway Infrastructure Access Price Calculation Methodology","Application of the new methodology for calculation of the access price for railway infrastructure",""],[1,"213","4","Railway Legal Harmonisation with EU Regulations","Harmonisation of railway- related laws with the IV set of railway EU regulations",""],[1,"213","6","Railway Interoperability and Railway Transport Safety Legislative Reform","Working groups have been set up to develop Draft Law on Amendments to the Law on Interoperability of the Railway System and Draft Law on the Safety of the Railway Transport.",""]],"40":[[1,"91","6","Railway Traffic Safety Institutional Capacity Expansion","it is necessary to expand the capacities of the Railway Directorate as a regulatory body responsible for railway traffic safety, improve the work of inspection services and increase the number of road controls, raise awareness through education and adjust legislation in the field of vehicle safety, road design and maintenance.",""],[1,"91","6","Railway Crossing Automation and Safety Markings Upgrade","Automation of road crossings (installation of vibro strips, solar markers and reflector lighting) has improved railway traffic safety.",""],[1,"99","8","Level Crossing Modernization Programme","To increase railway safety, funds have been secured from a World Bank loan for the modernization of level crossings in the amount of EUR 10.9 million",""],[1,"99","8","Additional Level Crossing Modernization Financing","the World Bank has approved in principle the proposal of the funds for the modernization of level crossings in the amount of around EUR 22.6 million",""],[1,"99","8","EBRD Loan Reallocation for Level Crossing Safety Works","A request was also submitted for the reallocation of the remaining funds from the EBRD loan25 (around EUR 10 million, expected realization at 33% per year in the period 2021-2023)",""],[1,"99","8","Level Crossing Safety Upgrading under Existing Projects","around EUR 480,000 under the existing projects relate to raising the level of safety at level crossings (2021).",""],[1,"213","8","Railway Level Crossing Modernisation Project","Funds totaling EUR 10.9 million for boosting safety in railway transport have been ensured through the Project of Trade and Transport Facilitation in the Western Balkans which is funded from a World Bank loan for the modernisation of level crossings (its realisation began in 2020 while actual works are expected to kick off in 2021).",""],[1,"213","8","Reallocation of EBRD Loan Funds for Level Crossing Safety","a request was submitted to reallocate remaining funds of the existing EBRD loan to the amount of about EUR 10 million (EBRD's formal approval is awaited).",""],[1,"213","8","Level Crossing Modernisation and Maintenance Investment","‘Serbian Railways Infrastructure’ JSC invested around 170 million dinars (EUR 1.4 million), and in 2020 around 100 million dinars (EUR 830,000) in the modernisation and maintenance of level crossings.",""],[1,"214","1","Level Crossing Modernisation Investment","the World Bank has generally approved the proposal of funds for the modernisation of level crossings to the amount of around EUR 22.6 million (the realisation is set for 2022 and 2023).",""]],"41":[[1,"105","4","Land Consolidation Reform and Legislative Framework","More efficient implementation of land consolidation procedure (on scattered parcels and fragmented holdings of agricultural producers) will be enabled through the establishment of a legislative framework that includes the preparation and adoption of the Law on Land Consolidation, amendments to the Law on Agricultural Land and the Law on State Survey and",""],[1,"106","1","Cadastre Digitization and Land Consolidation Supervision System","The reform also involves digitization of the expert supervision procedure, transparency and strengthening of the mechanism to control the spending of budget funds, making available to the public the plans created during the implementation of land consolidation on the GeoSerbia National Geoportal and establishing an information system to support expert supervision in the land consolidation process.",""],[1,"106","3","Land Consolidation Legal Framework","Preparation and adoption of the legal framework for the implementation of land consolidation (Law on Land Consolidation, amendments to the Law on Agricultural Land, amendments to the Law on State Survey and Cadastre)",""],[1,"106","4","Bylaw Drafting and Enactment Reform","Drafting and enacting bylaws based on the adopted set of laws",""],[1,"106","5","Land Consolidation Training and Office Equipment Procurement","Conducting training sessions for 9 employees on land consolidation in the Agricultural Land Management (ALM) and procurement of office equipment",""],[1,"106","6","Bylaw for Professional Supervision Methodology in Consolidation Procedures","Adoption of a bylaw defining the Methodology for performing professional supervision in consolidation procedures (RGA)",""],[1,"106","7","Information System for Expert Supervision Control Module","Introduction of information system to support the implementation of expert supervision in the consolidation process - control module",""],[1,"106","8","Integration of Professional Supervision and Real Estate Cadastre Information Systems","Connecting the information system to support the implementation of professional supervision in the consolidation process with the information system of the Real Estate Cadastre",""],[1,"106","9","ALM Server, Software and Network Infrastructure Procurement","Procurement of servers, software and network infrastructure at ALM",""],[1,"107","1","Pilot Land Consolidation","Implementation of pilot land consolidation",""],[1,"107","2","GeoSerbia National Geoportal Public Inspection of Consolidation Plans","Presentation of overview plans (existing condition, consolidation assessment of the value of the old condition land, project of the new condition, distribution of the consolidation mass) for public inspection on the GeoSerbia National Geoportal for all sites and pilot projects started in 2021.",""],[1,"107","6","Land Consolidation for Agricultural Modernization","More efficient implementation of the consolidation process enables: formation of plots of regular shape suitable for access to mechanization, development of roads, drainage and irrigation systems and construction of other facilities that contribute to rural development and creating conditions for implementing agro technical measures on state agricultural land and its leasing.",""],[1,"107","7","Agricultural Land Consolidation and Management Support","The estimated costs for the consolidation of agricultural land in accordance with the estimated needs total EUR 2.8 million.",""],[1,"107","8","Bylaw Drafting and Institutional Capacity Support","In 2022, funds in the amount of EUR 902,260 are foreseen for the needs of hiring experts to draft bylaws, for the costs of salaries, training and office equipment for the needs of five newly hired employees, translation services, server procurement and network infrastructure development",""],[1,"107","9","Agricultural Land Management Support and Pilot Land Consolidation","Funds related to professional and administrative support in the management of agricultural land in 2023 in the amount of EUR 1.95 million are envisaged for the costs of salaries, training and office equipment for the needs of five employees, software development and costs of implementing pilot land consolidation",""],[1,"108","1","Agricultural Land Classification and State-Owned Abandoned Land Identification Reform","the proposed IPA 2021 project aimed to reform the system of classification of agricultural land and identification of state-owned abandoned land in the entire territory of RS in the amount of EUR 1.3 million",""],[1,"108","1","Management Improvement of State-Owned Abandoned Land","the UNDP project component \"Improvement of management of state-owned abandoned land\" which is implemented in the Agricultural Land Administration",""],[1,"108","2","Expert Supervision Information System for Consolidation Process","The estimated costs of the Republic Geodetic Authority for the implementation of information system to support the implementation of expert supervision in the consolidation process (control module and integration module together with system maintenance costs) in 2021 amount to about EUR 400,000.",""],[1,"108","2","Regulatory Framework Drafting for Expert Supervision","The estimated cost of drafting the regulatory framework within the scope of the Republic Geodetic Authority (laws and bylaws), as well as the cost of hiring employees to carry out professional supervision are among the regular operating costs of the Republic Geodetic Authority which are financed from the budget of the Republic of Serbia and do not entail additional costs.",""],[1,"108","4","Land Consolidation and Drainage Improvement Programme","By accelerating land consolidation process, conditions are created for the enlargement of cadastral parcels, prevention of disturbances of natural land functions, preservation of the quality of agricultural land.",""],[1,"108","4","Transparency and Public Access to Land Consolidation Information","Also, transparency of the land consolidation process and public access to environmental information in the land consolidation area will be ensured.",""],[1,"108","7","Stakeholder Consultation on Regulatory Framework Adoption","Conducting public hearings, round tables and other ways of informing stakeholders in the process of adoption of the regulatory framework",""],[1,"108","8","Pilot Land Consolidation Projects","implementation of pilot land consolidation projects, purchase of software and other equipment required for rapid exchange of data, funds available and earmarked in the RS budget refer to one calendar year",""],[1,"108","13","Regulatory Framework Adoption","Provide for the adoption of a regulatory framework in the Government's Work Plan for the next calendar year",""],[1,"214","8","Land Property Consolidation and Agricultural Land Law Reform","Adoption of the Law on Consolidation of Land Property and Law on Amendments to the Law on Agricultural Land",""],[1,"214","10","Land Property Consolidation Programme Handbooks Adoption","Unplanned yet realised activities are two adopted handbooks, namely: Handbook on Content, Process of Development, and Adoption of the Land Property Consolidation Programme ('Official Gazette of the RS', No. 62/20) and Handbook on the Content of Technical Documentation for Geodetic and Technical Works (projects) in Land Property Consolidation ('Official Gazette of the RS',",""],[1,"215","1","Land Property Consolidation Handbooks and Legal Reform","The handbooks closely regulate the matter of land regulation through consolidation of land property.",""],[1,"236","6","Land Consolidation Reform and Legal Amendments","the text which refers to the goals of land consolidation, primarily to: property consolidation, provision of appropriate areas for the construction of public infrastructure (rural roads, irrigation and drainage systems, windbreaks, etc.) and more efficient implementation of the consolidation procedure itself, which will be preceded by the adoption of a new law and amendments to existing laws",""],[1,"237","1","Land Consolidation Procedure","One of the goals in the consolidation procedure can be the consolidation of distributed estates, so that after consolidation the entire property of individual producers, i.e. the area of property of individual producers determined by valuation is in smaller places, which facilitates agricultural production for farmers or to provide construction and consolidation use of public infrastructure facilities for which there is a need (rural roads, irrigation systems, etc.).",""]],"42":[[1,"102","4","Farm Register Eligibility Requirement for Agricultural Subsidies","Farmers must be registered with the Farm Register (FR) as commercial holdings in active status in order to be eligible to apply for funds from national subsidies or funds from the IPARD fund.",""],[1,"109","1","Integrated Administrative Control System Establishment","it is necessary to establish appropriate systems for CAP implementation, there was a need to redefine structural reform 6 of ERP 2020-2022 aimed at expanding the scope of the measure since the Farm Register is only one element/instrument of the necessary Integrated Administrative Control System (IACS).",""],[1,"109","2","Digitalization and Automation of Farmer Financial Support System","This structural reform, which implies a gradual digitization and process automation, will help improve implementation of the system of financial support to farmers enabling them to have easier access to available incentives.",""],[1,"109","3","Integrated Agricultural Administration and Control System Establishment","This measure, through the establishment of the new Farm Register, Land Parcel Identification System (LPIS), application system for processing Single Aid Applications of the farmers in line with the EU and other IACS elements should lead to the establishment of a functional IACS and automation of the application procedure and payment of incentives.",""],[1,"109","3","Directorate for Agrarian Payments Establishment","The establishment of a functional Directorate for Agrarian Payments in accordance with EU rules, which includes introduction of a functional IACS, pursuant to the experience of previous accessions, will be one of the closing benchmarks in the Negotiating Chapter 11.",""],[1,"109","4","Integrated Administration and Control System Establishment","The establishment of a functional IACS is to be done in parallel with the process of establishing a single MAFWM data bus",""],[1,"109","4","Single MAFWM Data Bus Establishment","The establishment of a functional IACS is to be done in parallel with the process of establishing a single MAFWM data bus",""],[1,"109","5","Digital Business Application Processing System","it is necessary to well design the automated receiving, processing and execution of applications in digital format",""],[1,"109","6","Roadmap for Establishing the Directorate for Agrarian Payments","Development of the Roadmap on the establishment of the Directorate for Agrarian Payments",""],[1,"109","7","MAFWM Information Strategy Development","Development of MAFWM information strategy",""],[1,"109","8","Farm Register Software Development","Development of Farm Register software",""],[1,"109","9","LPIS Software Development","Development of LPIS software",""],[1,"110","4","MAFWM Data Bus Development","Development of the MAFWM data bus",""],[1,"110","12","Establishment of the Directorate for Agrarian Payments Roadmap","the development of the Roadmap on establishment of the Directorate for Agrarian Payments will be completed",""],[1,"110","13","Digital Strategy Development","During 2021, a Digital Strategy will be developed, which is financed within the Competitive Agriculture Project from the World Bank loan.",""],[1,"110","14","Farm Register Software Procurement and Treasury Transfer","procurement of new software for the Farm Register from the budget of the Republic of Serbia - source 01 in the amount of up to EUR 169,704.37 will be carried out, and in the following years the Farm Register will be taken over by the Treasury Department of the Ministry of Finance.",""],[1,"110","15","LPIS Software Development","Funds in the RS budget are planned for the development of LPIS software and payment is envisaged in stages in the total amount of up to EUR 560,024.44.",""],[1,"110","16","Agricultural Register System Integration","During 2022, the system integration of LPIS, the Register of Animals and the Farm Register will be carried out.",""],[1,"110","17","Application System for Processing Single Aid Applications","The establishment of the Application System for processing Single Aid Applications of farmers in line with the EU will be financed as part of IACS, through planned IPA funds, without national co- financing.",""],[1,"110","18","Integrated Administration and Control System Establishment","The establishment of the IACS was planned through the IPA 2018 programming cycle.",""],[1,"111","2","Integrated Administration and Control System (IACS) Establishment","Establishment of IACS creates conditions for application of Common Agricultural Policy rules and Cross Compliance with environmental requirements for payment of subsidies as well as incentive pays for environmental measures",""],[1,"202","4","Digitization and Process Automation for Agricultural Financial Support","Improvement of the financial support system for agriculture through digitization and process automation",""],[1,"206","1","Agricultural Financial Support System Digitization and Process Automation","5. Improvement of the financial support system for agriculture through digitization and process automation",""],[1,"215","2","Digital Procedures for RAF Entries and National Incentives Approval","Amendments to the Law on Agriculture and Rural Development and adoption of necessary handbooks which regulate digital procedures for making entries into the RAF and the approval of national incentives",""],[1,"215","3","eAgriculture Software Development","Finalisation of the IT specification for the development of the eAgriculture software, contractor selection, and",""],[1,"215","4","eAgriculture Portal Implementation through Competitive Agriculture Project","Elements of the eAgriculture portal will be implemented through the Competitive Agriculture Project which is in the set- up stage.",""],[1,"216","2","Local Agricultural Producer Service Centres and Expert Support","The set-up of service centres/recruitment of experts to assist local agricultural producers",""],[1,"216","4","Civil Servant and Service Centre Training for Agricultural Request Processing","Training of officers in charge of request processing/civil servants in the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Water Management, Directorate for Agrarian Payments, and service centres/professionals recruited to assist agricultural producers.","Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Water Management | Directorate for Agrarian Payments"],[1,"235","2","e-Agrar Agricultural Subsidy Management Portal","“Improvement to management of register of agricultural estates and approval of national agricultural subsidies through development of e-Agrar web portal”",""],[1,"236","3","Integrated Administration and Control System (IACS) Establishment","in accordance with AP for Chapter 11 IACS - integrated system for management and control (a tool used in all EU member states and along with the establishment of a functional and accredited Paying Agency represents one of the conditions, (in accordance with EU regulations), for closing the Chapter 11) will be established.",""],[1,"237","3","Farmer Digital Skills Training and Transition to Online Administrative Procedures","training should also be provided that will enable farmers to become acquainted with the possibilities and to use online tools more easily.",""],[1,"237","5","Paying Agency Establishment","the establishment of a Paying Agency is envisaged, which will have regional/local offices that will, among other things, provide support to users.",""]],"43":[[1,"117","9","Industrial Circular Economy Transition Measures","The activities to be defined by the Action Plan will be a combination of promotional and incentive ones and will seek to raise the level of results in this area, which are currently at a fairly low level.",""],[1,"118","13","Circular Economy Strategic Framework Development","In order to define the strategic framework for the circular economy, the Ex-ante analysis of the circular economy effects was prepared as a background document to develop policy document.",""],[1,"118","13","Circular Economy Roadmap for Serbia","Also, a Roadmap for the circular economy in Serbia in 2020 was developed, providing recommendations for the transition from linear to circular economy in the area of waste management.",""],[1,"118","14","Circular Economy Programme with a Three-year Action Plan","the basis for the development of a public policy document Circular Economy Programme with a Three-year Action Plan, with an aim at creating a focused and better coordinated policy in this area.",""],[1,"118","16","Circular Economy Policy Document Preparation and Adoption","Preparation and adoption of policy documents for circular economy",""],[1,"119","1","Circular Economy Concepts Introduction in Economic Entities","Introduction of the circular economy concepts in economic entities through cooperation between business and academic sector - circular vouchers",""],[1,"119","2","Circular Economy Concepts in Local Self-Governments","Introduction of the circular economy concepts in local self - governments - circular communities",""],[1,"119","4","Circular Economy Programme Action Plan","Circular Economy Programme with an Action Plan developed and adopted",""],[1,"119","7","Circular Economy Transition Reform","The concept of circular economy provides for the savings in terms of resources and energy, enables and encourages business growth and leads to new investments.",""],[1,"119","8","Circular Economy Programme and Action Plan","Development of the Programme for Circular Economy with the Action Plan is planned for 2021 and will be financed from the RS budget.",""],[1,"119","8","Costing and Financing of Circular Economy Reform Measures","The Action Plan will also estimate the costs of implementing reform measures in 2022 and 2023, and financial resources will be provided from the RS budget, EU funds and from international donors as well.",""],[1,"119","9","Circular Economy Public Investment and Job Creation Reform","Increasing employment through development of the circular economy will depend on the size of public investment required to introduce this concept.",""],[1,"119","13","Circular Economy Strategic Framework Development Working Group","A multisectoral working group for circular economy has been established that brings together all relevant ministries, institutions, and international organisations (UNDP, GIZ, and OSCE) and is tasked with assisting in development of strategic framework for circular economy",""],[1,"221","2","Circular Economy Strategic Framework Development","Introduction of circular economy concept through definition of the strategic framework",""],[1,"221","3","Circular Economy Policy Document Development","Development of a public policy document about circular economy",""],[1,"221","4","Programme for Circular Economy with a Three-Year Action Plan","The document is a preparatory document in the process of defining a public policy document, which is the Programme for circular economy with an Action plan for three years.",""],[1,"235","7","Circular Economy Reform","the decision was made to propose only one reform in the field of environmental protection, which refers to the circular economy.","Ministry of Environmental Protection"],[1,"240","1","Circular Economy Programme Development","work will continue on the development of the Circular Economy Programme.",""],[1,"240","2","Circular Economy Programme with Three-Year Action Plan","the preparation of a strategic framework for circular economy in 2021 through the development of a public policy document Circular Economy Programme with an action plan for three years",""],[1,"240","2","Circular Economy Implementation Measures and Activities","The programme will define measures and activities that will help implement the concept of circular economy in Serbia",""],[1,"240","2","Circular Economy Monitoring Mechanism","monitoring the implementation of the planned activities is a mandatory part of the process",""],[1,"244","3","Circular Economy Structural Reform","and be related to SR 12 \"Introduction of the circular economy concept\"",""]],"44":[[1,"122","5","Real Estate Cadastre Digitization and Real-Time Updating","Establishing an up-to-date Real Estate Cadastre in real time is a precondition for improving business efficiency and shortening the procedures required for registering property rights in the cadastre.",""],[1,"122","5","National Spatial Data Infrastructure","National Spatial Data Infrastructure - NSDI is an integrated geospatial data system, which should enable users to comprehensively find and access spatial information from a variety of sources, ranging from the local, through the national to the global level.",""],[1,"122","5","Legal and Administrative Reform for Cadastre Data Submission","The enactment of the Law on Procedure for Registration into Real Estate and Power Lines Cadastre (\"Official Gazette of the RS\", No. 41/18) prescribes the obligations of public bodies and other entities to submit data from their competencies to the Real Estate Cadastre Service for updating.",""],[1,"123","1","Single Address Register Establishment","With the establishment of the Coordination Body for the improvement of the address register at the end of 2018, a single address register is to be established in three phases: naming streets and facilities in cooperation with local self-governments (in progress), followed by field marking and finally updating the address register by LSGs.",""],[1,"130","7","Geospatial Sector Strategic Digital Platform Development","STRUCTURAL REFORM 12: IMPROVEMENT OF GEOSPATIAL SECTOR THROUGH DEVELOPMENT OF A STRATEGIC DIGITAL PLATFORM TO SUPPORT INVESTMENT DECISION-MAKING",""],[1,"130","8","Strategic Digital Platform for the Geospatial Sector","Creating a strategic digital platform for the geospatial sector facilitates the availability of combined data sets via web services, their efficient, fast and quality exchange, which enables citizens and businesses easier identification and comfortable access to the desired data, crucial for quality investment decision making.",""],[1,"130","10","NSDI Bylaw Adoption","Adoption of bylaws in the field of NSDI",""],[1,"130","12","Real Estate Cadastre and Local Tax Data Consolidation Pilot","Alignment, merging, and consolidation of data held by real estate cadastre and local tax administrations in \"pilot\" municipalities to develop prototype real estate mass valuation system",""],[1,"130","13","Prototype Real Estate Mass Valuation System","Development of a prototype real estate mass valuation system and establishment of procedures at pilot local authorities",""],[1,"131","1","Data Interoperability Establishment","Establishment of data interoperability between Address Register and government bodies and organisations and local authorities",""],[1,"131","8","National Spatial Data Infrastructure Development","By enhancing the efficiency of decision-making for investment purposes, making information more accessible, and providing advanced solutions for R&D institutions and businesses, the NSDI will exert an indirect influence on GDP growth.",""],[1,"131","8","Mass Real Estate Valuation System","Development of a mass real estate valuation system will entail the identification of all real estate transactions, development of a mass valuation model, and registration of all real estate on the territory of Serbia",""],[1,"131","10","Address Register Update","additional employment of civil servants on updating the address register",""],[1,"131","10","National Geospatial Data Infrastructure Bylaw Adoption","engaging foreign consultants in the adoption of bylaws in the field of national geospatial data infrastructure",""],[1,"131","10","Geospatial Data Services Development","development and availability of new services for geospatial data",""],[1,"131","10","Mass Real Estate Valuation System Implementation","engaging consultants for collecting, entering and controlling data for mass real estate valuation, coordination of work and implementation of the system in pilot municipalities, as well as testing of the developed system of mass real estate valuation",""],[1,"131","11","Geospatial Data Services and Mass Real Estate Appraisal System Implementation","Estimated costs for 2022 of EUR 2.4 million relate to: continued development and availability of new geospatial data services; continued engagement of consultants in data entry and control for mass real estate appraisal, coordination of work and implementation of the system in pilot municipalities, as well as testing the developed system of mass real estate appraisal.",""],[1,"131","12","Real Estate Mass Valuation System Development","The development of a real estate mass valuation system, with evidencing all real estate on the territory of RS in the records,",""],[1,"132","1","Real Estate Taxation Reform","will create conditions for taxation of all real estate entered in the register in a way that is more consistent with the economic power of taxpayers, taking into account a larger number of corrective elements that affect the value of real estate - for real estate covered by mass valuation.",""],[1,"132","2","National Spatial Data Infrastructure Development","National Spatial Data Infrastructure will facilitate access to environmental information by making these data publicly available, and will remove obstacles to the exchange of such information between public authorities.",""],[1,"132","7","Cadastral Property Identification and Data Updating Initiative","Cadastral property identification to be implemented by local tax administrations; Initiative to provide and update data",""],[1,"132","9","Working Party for Reform Implementation and Staff Training","Working Party to be established and progress to be constantly monitored; time limits to be set for related activities and appropriate training in various topics to be offered for staff",""],[1,"132","11","Address Register Project Monitoring and Reporting Mechanism","All project stakeholders to be required to regularly notify NGA of their current status and progress, and to submit specific reports as required by Government's Address Register Enhancement Co-Ordinating Body.",""],[1,"203","1","Strategic Digital Geospatial Platform Development","Improvement of geospatial sector through development of a strategic digital platform to support investment decision-making",""],[1,"203","2","E-Space Digital Platform for Spatial Development Management","Improvement to spatial development management in the Republic of Serbia through establishment of e- Space digital platform",""],[1,"207","4","Geospatial Sector Strategic Digital Platform","Improvement of geospatial sector through development of a strategic digital platform to support investment decision-making",""],[1,"218","2","Geospatial Sector Strategic Digital Platform","Improvement of geospatial sector through development of a strategic digital platform to support investment decision-making",""],[1,"218","5","Monitoring and Reporting Regulation for NIGD","In 2020 Regulation on the Monitoring and Reporting of NIGD Activity was adopted (\"Official Gazette of the RS\", No. 91 of 26 June 2020).",""],[1,"218","5","Interoperability Regulation Development","The development of the Proposed regulation on interoperability has been approved by the EU Delegation as a donation within the PLAC 3 project.",""],[1,"218","5","National Strategy for NIGD Formulation","The formulation of a draft Strategy for NIGD is in progress (the draft is 95% complete).",""],[1,"218","6","Geospatial Data Service Development and Availability","Development and availability of the geospatial data service",""],[1,"218","8","GeoSerbia National Portal Enhancement","The 'GeoSerbia' national portal has been improved by new sets of geospatial data and development of new services (in total 285 data sets and 39 services are available).",""],[1,"220","5","Address Registry Data Interoperability","Establishment of interoperability of data in the Address Registry with data kept by state bodies, organisations, and local self- government units",""]],"45":[[1,"135","2","Smart Specialization Strategy","With the aim of improving cooperation, primarily with the business sector, the Smart Specialization Strategy in the RS for the period from 2020 to 2027 was adopted (\"Official Gazette of the RS\", No. 21/20).",""],[1,"135","2","Science-Business Cooperation Programmes","In addition, some of the measures are specific programmes for cooperation between economy and science in the fields of specialization, which are implemented through the Fund for Innovation and the Fund for Science.",""],[1,"135","3","Combined Institutional-Project Financing Reform for Science and Research","The reform of the organization and financing of science and research in Serbia, which is a great progress, implies the introduction of combined institutional-project financing (eliminates uncertainty in work and enables long-term planning of activities of scientific research institutions), as well as the establishment of the Science Fund.",""],[1,"135","3","Science Fund Competitive Research Grant Mechanism","The Science Fund provides support to scientific research activities by announcing public calls and performing the complete procedure and management of competitive project calls.",""],[1,"135","3","Science Fund Research and Innovation Support Programmes","The Fund's programmes support technological development, advanced and innovative ideas, staff development, laboratories and research, construction of scientific infrastructure, integration into international scientific trends, cooperation between science and economy and other topics of strategic and social importance.",""],[1,"135","4","Innovation Fund Support for Innovative Projects and Technology Transfer","Through various financial instruments, the Innovation Fund47 supports the creation of innovations, strengthening the link between science and the economy, establishing new and strengthening the existing companies with innovative potential.",""],[1,"136","3","Innovation Infrastructure and Technological Entrepreneurship Investment","The innovation ecosystem is being developed by further investment in innovation infrastructure and technological entrepreneurship in university centres and regions in Serbia.",""],[1,"136","3","Science and Technology Parks Development","Four state-of-the-art science and technology parks (Belgrade, Novi Sad, Niš and Čačak) have been built, in which science and economy are working together to develop innovations for the global market.",""],[1,"137","7","Applied Scientific Research Support Programme","The programme supports applied scientific research, the creation of interdisciplinary and multidisciplinary teams within three groups of scientific fields: (bio) medical sciences, (bio) medical engineering and information technology, and economic, sociological, psychological research and management of complex systems.",""],[1,"139","3","Strengthening Scientific Research Capacities","STRUCTURAL REFORM 14: SUPPORT FOR SCIENTIFIC RESEARCH ACTIVITY THROUGH STRENGTHENING SCIENTIFIC RESEARCH CAPACITIES",""],[1,"139","4","Scientific Research System Reform","The reform of the scientific research system, on the one hand, should ensure the stability of funding of scientific research organizations, and on the other hand support excellence in science as the basis of an innovative society and ensure long-term quality of scientific research through strengthening scientific research institutions.",""],[1,"139","5","Science Fund Programmes","The implementation of the Law on the Science Fund continues to support the most prominent scientists, teams and their ideas through the Science Fund Programmes.",""],[1,"140","2","Programme of Cooperation of Serbian Science with the Diaspora","Implementation of the Programme of Cooperation of Serbian Science with the diaspora",""],[1,"140","3","Evaluation and Project Selection Activities","Programme Ideas - implementation of evaluation and project selection activities",""],[1,"140","6","Science Fund Programme Development","Preparation of new Science Fund Programmes - People",""],[1,"140","14","Scientific Research Sector Capacity Enhancement Reform","The reform will improve the existing potentials and capacities of the scientific research sector, following the example of developed world economies.",""],[1,"140","15","Science Fund Research Commercialization Programmes","Systematic regulation of cooperation between science and economy through the programmes of the Science Fund will stimulate economic activity and increase market competition.",""],[1,"140","16","Serbia Accelerating Innovation and Entrepreneurship Project","In 2021, through the Serbia Accelerating Innovation and Entrepreneurship Project - SAIGE Project, EUR 34 million were provided, and through IPA 2019 in the amount of EUR 31.5 million.",""],[1,"140","17","Innovation Fund Job Creation Support","Through funding through its instruments, the Innovation Fund has been supporting the creation of new jobs for many years.",""],[1,"141","2","Institutional and Project Funding for Science Development","Full establishment of institutional funding as a basis for science development and the ability of R&D organizations to absorb funds from institutional (through the Ministry of Education, Science and Technological Development) and project funding (through the Science Fund) together","Ministry of Education, Science and Technological Development"],[1,"141","4","R&D-Business Collaboration Support Mechanisms","Continuous provision of support (financial and non-financial) for various mechanisms that stimulate the connection and cooperation between R&D organizations and the business sector",""],[1,"141","5","Institutional Support for Innovative Companies","The aim of the reform is to improve institutional support to innovative companies through various mechanisms and encourage their development activities to find innovative solutions and products, employment, digitalization and improvement of infrastructure for creating a business ecosystem.",""],[1,"141","6","Innovation Fund for Innovative Entrepreneurship","The Innovation Fund establishes long-term institutional support of the state for innovative entrepreneurship and the establishment of cooperation between the economy and the academic sector.",""],[1,"141","6","Business Acceleration Programme","Through the Business Acceleration Programme, a new instrument will be established which will additionally support the development and improvement of the competitiveness of innovative companies in the early phase of development, but also in the growth phase, as well as their training for attracting investments.",""],[1,"141","7","Science and Technology Park Network Expansion","The coordination of the Serbia Creates platform, which operates within the e-Government Office, has contributed to the creation of a network of science and technology parks.",""],[1,"141","7","Science and Technology Park Infrastructure Investment","The successes of the Science - Technology Park Belgrade have contributed to the establishment of new STPs in Nis, Novi Sad (under construction) and Čačak, providing a basis for further investments in infrastructure in order to create a suitable environment for innovation, taking into account the importance of development of the Serbian regions in terms of their specific needs and potentials.",""],[1,"141","8","Smart Specialization Support for Research, Development and Innovation","Smart specialization strategy in the RS for the period 2020-2027 (adopted in February 2020), will be implemented through targeted support for research, development and innovation activities.",""],[1,"141","9","Scientific Research and Innovation Capacity Strengthening Reform","The reform contributes to the realization of SDG 9.5. Improve scientific research, improve the technological capabilities of industrial sectors, which means that by 2030 innovation will be encouraged and significantly increase the number of employees in the field of research and development, as well as increase public and private spending on research and development, as well as SDG 9.b Support the development of domestic technology, research and innovation, including the provision of a favourable policy environment for, inter alia, industrial diversification and the added value of goods.",""],[1,"142","2","Commercialization of Research in SMEs","Development of new products and services through the commercialization of research in small and medium enterprises",""],[1,"142","4","Business Acceleration Programme","Component 2 - Establishment of the Business Acceleration Programme, including IPA 2019 Funds",""],[1,"142","11","Support for Innovative Companies and Research Cooperation","Through institutional and financial support of innovative companies and enabling cooperation with domestic institutes and world experts, the existing innovation potentials will be expanded",""],[1,"142","12","Innovation Fund Support Financing","RS budget funds in the projected amount of about EUR 36 million to support the work of the Innovation Fund, three direct grant agreements from IPA 2014, IPA 2018 and IPA 2019, whereby financing from the IPA funds is planned in the total amount of about EUR 41,2 million with co-financing from the RS budget in the amount of EUR 15 million.",""],[1,"142","12","Business Acceleration Programme Support","In 2021 through the Serbia Accelerating Innovation and Entrepreneurship Project- SAIGE World Bank Project, an additional EUR 7 million have been provided for the Business Acceleration Programme.",""],[1,"142","12","Continuous Support Provision","Continuous provision of support will continue, and the amounts will be determined according to the financial plan for 2021 and projections for the following years.",""],[1,"143","1","Innovation Fund Support for Innovative Companies","Through its programmes, the Innovation Fund supports job creation and monitors the growth of employment in innovative companies that have used the Fund's funds.",""],[1,"143","7","R&D-Business Collaboration Support Mechanisms","Continuous provision of necessary support (financial and non-financial) for various mechanisms that stimulate the connection and cooperation between R&D organizations and the business sector",""],[1,"149","1","Industrial Base and Innovation Infrastructure Upgrade","upgrading the industrial base and innovation infrastructure (supporting youth entrepreneurship, start-ups and early start-ups by introducing mechanisms for the transfer of knowledge from the diaspora, by encouraging green and women's entrepreneurship).",""],[1,"203","3","Scientific Research Capacity Strengthening","Support for scientific research activity through strengthening scientific research capacities",""],[1,"203","4","Institutional Support for Smart Specialization and Innovation Development","Improvement of institutional support for the development of smart specializations and innovations",""],[1,"207","7","Scientific Research Capacity Strengthening","Support for scientific research activity through strengthening scientific research capacities",""],[1,"208","1","Institutional Support for Smart Specialization and Innovation Development","Improvement of institutional support for the development of smart specializations and innovations",""],[1,"221","7","PROMIS Young Researchers Project Programme","Programme for Excellent Projects of Young Researchers PROMIS - the start of implementation by",""],[1,"222","2","Artificial Intelligence Development Programme","Programme of Artificial Intelligence Development - Signing of the contract",""],[1,"222","4","Artificial Intelligence Development Programme","Programme of Artificial Intelligence Development - implementation",""],[1,"237","7","Smart Specialization Strategy Harmonization","it calls for a Smart Specialization Strategy and that in the meantime the Industrial Development Strategy has been adopted.",""]],"46":[[1,"85","17","Broadband Access Network Development","The reform includes the development of broadband access networks by providing state incentives to jointly build communication infrastructure, create detailed maps of the availability of broadband access services, improve conditions for the development of digital education and increase the use of e-government services.",""],[1,"85","19","Electronic Communications Legislative Harmonization","Harmonizes its legislative framework in the field of electronic communications with the 2009 EU regulatory framework.",""],[1,"85","19","Telecommunications Competition and Infrastructure Access Measures","Take measures to ensure the implementation of competition measures and facilitate operators' access to telecommunications infrastructure (channels, antennas, optical infrastructure and fixed telephony infrastructure).",""],[1,"137","4","New Generation Networks Development Strategy","In 2018, the Government adopted the Strategy for the Development of New Generation Networks until 2023, which has the main goal of providing the necessary infrastructure for the development of the digital single market in Serbia, in accordance with the strategic framework of the European Union in this area.",""],[1,"137","4","Electronic Communications Law Drafting and Transposition","The Ministry of Trade, Tourism and Telecommunications has started activities on the preparation of the Draft Law on Electronic Communications, which includes transposing the provisions of the European Electronic Communications Code, which entered into force on December 20th, 2018, and EU member states are obliged to transpose the provisions of this directive by December 21st, 2020.","Ministry of Trade, Tourism and Telecommunications"],[1,"138","1","Rural Broadband Communication Infrastructure Project","Therefore, a project loan of the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development of EUR 18 million60 was approved for the development of communication infrastructure in rural areas (\"white or gray zones\").",""],[1,"138","3","School Internet Connectivity Upgrade","Efforts are also being made to provide funds to improve the quality and speed of internet connections in already connected schools.",""],[1,"138","4","Electronic Communications Law Adoption","The adoption of the Law on Electronic Communications (which is in preparation) will complete the harmonization with the EU regulatory framework in the field of electronic communications.",""],[1,"138","7","Rural Broadband ICT Construction Phase 1","For the implementation of the project \"Construction of broadband ICT in rural areas of the Republic of Serbia - Phase 1\".",""],[1,"146","1","Broadband Access Network Development Incentives","development of broadband access networks by providing state incentives for joint construction of IC infrastructure",""],[1,"146","1","Broadband Availability Mapping","development of detailed maps of the availability of broadband access services in Serbia",""],[1,"146","1","Digital Education and E-Government Access Improvement","improvement of conditions for the development of digital education and increasing the use of e-Government services",""],[1,"146","5","Rural Optical Broadband Network Construction Project","Project of construction of optical broadband network in rural areas of Serbia (phase 1 and 2).",""],[1,"146","6","Education and Cultural-Scientific Institution Connectivity Reform","the reform supports the connection of primary and secondary education institutions and cultural and scientific institutions in order to reduce differences in the availability of modern services.",""],[1,"146","7","Connected Schools Wireless Infrastructure Expansion","The \"Connected Schools\" project is aimed at building and improving local wireless communication infrastructure (WLAN) in all schools in Serbia.",""],[1,"146","8","Rural Optical Broadband Network Construction","Within phase 1 of the Project of construction of optical broadband network in rural areas of Serbia, the construction of infrastructure is planned to connect 600 settlements aiming at about 90,000 households, while phase 2 would include additional 900 settlements with about 135,000 households.",""],[1,"146","10","Rural Optical Broadband Network Construction","The crisis caused by the COVID-19 pandemic affected the implementation of preparatory activities for the construction of optical broadband network in rural areas of Serbia, and they were not fully implemented in accordance with the planned dynamics, so part of the planned activities was transferred to 2021.",""],[1,"146","11","Rural Communication Network and Public Facility Connectivity","Providing stable sources of funds for further implementation of this reform measure will reduce the negative effect of the pandemic by building a communication network in rural areas of the Republic of Serbia and by connecting a significant number of public facilities to enable uninterrupted education, greater availability of digital services and to influence the creation of favourable conditions for the general development of the economy and society in extraordinary circumstances.",""],[1,"147","1","Connected Schools ICT Infrastructure Improvement","Activities on the improvement of IC infrastructure in primary and secondary schools in RS - \"Connected schools\"",""],[1,"147","2","Rural Optical Broadband Network Construction Phase 1","Preparation for construction of optical broadband network in rural areas of Serbia - phase 1",""],[1,"147","3","Rural Optical Broadband Network Construction Phase 1","Construction of optical broadband network in rural areas of Serbia - phase 1",""],[1,"147","4","Rural Optical Broadband Network Construction, Phase 2","Preparation for construction of optical broadband network in rural areas of Serbia - phase 2",""],[1,"147","5","Rural Optical Broadband Network Construction Phase 2","Construction of optical broadband network in rural areas of Serbia - phase 2",""],[1,"147","10","Broadband Availability Mapping and Capital Incentives","Availability map of mobile broadband have been developed for all mobile technologies and are regularly updated by the Ministry of Trade, Tourism and Telecommunications.","Ministry of Trade, Tourism and Telecommunications"],[1,"147","11","Broadband Access Mapping and Infrastructure Sharing Initiative","Development of detailed maps of broadband access availability in Serbia directly affects the transparency of data on the existing communication infrastructure as well as the improvement of joint use of infrastructure by operators.",""],[1,"147","12","AMRES Network Connectivity for Educational and Cultural Institutions","In 2021, EUR 1,925 million will be provided from the RS budget for the needs of connecting educational and cultural institutions to the AMRES network.",""],[1,"147","12","Connected Schools Phase 2 ICT Infrastructure Improvement","For the improvement of IC infrastructure in primary and secondary schools in Serbia, within the project \"Connected schools\" - phase 2, EUR 22.4 million have been provided from the project loan.",""],[1,"147","12","Rural Optical Broadband Network Construction Phase 1","Preparation for the construction of optical broadband network in rural areas - phase 1 will be financed with EUR 1,7 million from grants and EUR 1,2 million from project loan, and the construction itself which is worth EUR 6 million will be financed from the project loan.",""],[1,"147","13","Connecting Educational and Cultural Institutions to AMRES","In 2022, it is necessary to provide EUR 1,925 million from the RS budget for connecting educational and cultural institutions to AMRES (improvement of quality and speed).",""],[1,"147","13","Connected Schools Phase 3","For the implementation of the project \"Connected Schools\" - phase 3, EUR 5.6 million will be allocated from the project loan.",""],[1,"147","13","Rural Optical Broadband Network Construction Phase 1","For the implementation of activities on the construction of optical broadband network in rural areas - phase 1, the amount of EUR 10.8 million will be provided from the project loan.",""],[1,"147","13","Preparation of Rural Optical Broadband Network Construction Phase 2","The funds necessary for the preparation of the construction of optical broadband network in rural areas - phase 2 amount to EUR 2,7 million and have not yet been provided.",""],[1,"148","1","AMRES Network Connectivity for Educational and Cultural Institutions","In 2023, it is necessary to provide funds fromT the RS budget in the amount of EUR 1,925 million for connecting educational and cultural institutions to the AMRES network (improvement of quality and speed).",""],[1,"148","2","Rural Optical Broadband Network Construction, Phase 2","Necessary funds, in the amount of EUR 54 million for financing the construction of optical broadband network in rural areas - phase 2 have not yet been provided.",""],[1,"148","3","Broadband Network Expansion and Next-Generation Access","The construction of broadband communication networks enables employment, but also work over the Internet and an increase in the number of jobs in practically all sectors, including the ICT sector.",""],[1,"148","3","Public Facility Connectivity and E-Government Upgrade","The implementation of the reform will affect the connection of public facilities, especially educational institutions, with modern IT infrastructure and the improvement of e-Government services.",""],[1,"148","9","Common Infrastructure Investment Increase","Increasing budget funds for building common infrastructure",""]],"47":[[1,"44","10","Household Fiscal Stimulus Package","Another aspect of the package of measures was the fiscal stimulus to the population with the aim of preserving the standard of living.",""],[1,"46","7","One-Time Cash Support for Adult Citizens","the payment of a sum of money to all adult citizens of the Republic of Serbia in the amount of EUR 100 in dinars calculated at the official middle exchange rate of the NBS, in order to help the population, preserve living standards and stimulate domestic demand.",""],[1,"46","7","One-Time Pensioner Assistance","as well as a one-time assistance to pensioners in the amount of RSD 4,000.",""],[1,"48","13","Public Wage Increase and Direct Financial Assistance Measures","Wage increase measures and other direct financial assistance (10% increase in salaries of health workers, direct financial assistance of RSD 4,000 to all pensioners, support to agricultural producers)",""],[1,"52","7","Direct Financial Assistance to Adult Citizens","primarily due to the payment of direct financial assistance to the population (EUR 100 to all adult citizens in dinar equivalent calculated at the official middle exchange rate of the NBS) in the total amount of RSD 72 billion.",""],[1,"170","1","Pension Indexation Reform","the Swiss formula for indexation of pensions was re-adopted at the end of 2019",""],[1,"170","1","Social Policy Financing and Institutional Strengthening","Therefore, providing adequate financial and institutional resources for social policy is a priority for the coming period.",""],[1,"170","5","Extension of Social Assistance Payments During State of Emergency","the payment of assistance was extended until the end of the state of emergency.",""],[1,"170","5","One-Time Pensioner Assistance Payment","Pensioners were paid a one-time assistance with the March pension",""],[1,"170","5","Timely Full Pension Payment During Pandemic","pensions were paid without a day of delay despite the pandemic, and in full (not in two parts as was the practice).",""]],"48":[[1,"81","2","Sustainable Environmental Protection Financing System","SR 10. Establishment of a sustainable system of environmental protection financing, it is estimated that, although it is very significant, the new developments are expected and will be included in the next cycle.",""],[1,"220","8","Sustainable Environment Funding System","SR 10. Establishment of a sustainable system for environment funding",""],[1,"220","9","Sustainable Funding System for Environment Programmes and Projects","Specification and formulation of measures and activities for the establishment of a sustainable funding system for environment programmes and projects",""],[1,"220","10","Green Fund Sustainability and Environment Financing System","the preparation of the project proposal entitled 'Support for establishment of a sustainable system of environment funding through an improved functionality of the Green Fund'.",""],[1,"220","10","Environment and Energy Programme Implementation Task Force","The work of the Task Force in charge of installing mechanisms for smooth implementation of programmes/projects in the field of environment and energy",""],[1,"235","7","Environmental Protection Financing Improvement","The Ministry of Environmental Protection certainly continues to work continuously on improving the system of financing environmental protection.","Ministry of Environmental Protection"],[1,"235","7","Multi-Annual Environmental Protection Investment and Financial Plan","the Ministry of Environmental Protection has developed a Multi-Annual Investment and Financial Plan (Plan), which was adopted as an integral part of the negotiating position for Chapter 27, in January","Ministry of Environmental Protection"],[1,"236","1","Multi-Annual Investment and Financing Plan","The multi-annual investment and financial plan includes an overview of the investments required for compliance, an assessment of project costs and an assessment of potential sources of funding.",""]],"52":[[1,"5","5","Strengthen SOE Fiscal Risk Analysis and Reporting","Increase the transparency of the fiscal impact of state- owned enterprises by reinforcing fiscal risk analysis and by publishing quarterly reports on SOEs' financial performance.",""],[1,"5","5","State-Owned Enterprise Governance Reform and Restructuring","To reduce fiscal risks, improve the governance of state owned enterprises including via further restructuring.",""],[1,"6","2","State-Owned Enterprise Fiscal Risk Monitoring and Due Diligence","The Group has also adopted hands-on approach on particular SOEs in case where the potential fiscal risk for the state is recognized.",""],[1,"6","3","SOE Business Plan Revision and Cost Restructuring","The Group has also been responsible for enforcing revision of 2020 annual business plan by SOEs in the light of the Pandemic and its likely negative implications on the financial performances of the SOEs.",""],[1,"6","3","Cost-Cutting Measures for State-Majority-Owned Companies","In addition, the Group was in charge of performing the cost-cutting proposition and execution for a several key State majority-owned companies in defence industry and companies in the portfolio of Ministry of Economy.",""],[1,"6","4","Public and State-Owned Enterprise Structural Reform","Structural reforms of public and state-owned enterprises will significantly reduce fiscal risks3.",""]],"53":[[1,"6","5","Financial Stability Monitoring and Contingency Action","Closely monitor financial stability challenges arising as a result of the coronavirus pandemic and take appropriate action if needed.",""],[1,"6","5","Non-Performing Loan Strategy Implementation","Further implement the measures included in the 2018-2020 NPL strategy and related action plan, including those aimed at preventing the accumulation of new non-performing loans such as reforms of the bankruptcy frameworks.",""]],"54":[[1,"6","5","Local Currency Market Development and Hedging Support","Enhance further the use of the local currency by fostering the development of secondary markets for government and corporate dinar securities, and support the use of hedging instruments.",""],[1,"7","8","Dinarization Promotion Measures","The National Bank of Serbia will continue to take measures and activities aimed at increasing dinarization, which are defined in the new Memorandum on the dinarization strategy signed by the National Bank of Serbia and the Government at the end of 2018.",""],[1,"7","8","Foreign Exchange Hedging Promotion and Client Education","The NBS will continue to promote the use of hedging instruments against exchange rate risk, but also against other risks, by regular updating the NBS website in the section on FX hedging, by advising banks to improve the offer of hedging instruments and by educating clients, primarily from the corporate sector.",""],[1,"15","7","Local Currency Use Promotion Measures","Continue to promote the use of local currency, inter alia, by encouraging the development of interbank markets and secondary markets for government securities, and by considering additional ways to improve long-term bank financing in dinar and hedging instruments.",""],[1,"15","8","Dinarization Support Measures","The National Bank of Serbia will continue to use its measures to support the dinarization process.",""],[1,"15","8","Dinarization Strategy Memorandum","In December 2018, the National Bank of Serbia and the Government of the Republic of Serbia signed a new Memorandum on the dinarization strategy, thus confirming the strategic commitment to further increase the use of domestic currency in the financial system of Serbia.","National Bank of Serbia | the Government of the Republic of Serbia"],[1,"15","8","Promotion of Dinar Savings","In order to promote savings in dinars, the National Bank of Serbia regularly publishes various analyses and information, pointing out the benefits of saving in local currency.","National Bank of Serbia"],[1,"15","8","Limits on Foreign Currency-Indexed Loans","Additionally, in order to encourage greater approval of loans to the economy in dinars, the National Bank of Serbia adopted regulations at the end of 2019 introducing a maximum percentage for new foreign currency indexed non-purpose and non-investment loans and loans in foreign currency approved to the economy.","National Bank of Serbia"],[1,"15","9","Foreign Exchange Hedging Promotion and Information Update","The National Bank of Serbia continuously promotes the use of instruments for protection against exchange rate risk.",""]],"55":[[1,"11","4","Unemployment Compensation Scheme","Provide adequate unemployment compensation schemes for laid off workers in order to mitigate the social impact of the economic downturn.",""],[1,"11","7","Compulsory Unemployment Insurance and Cash Benefit Scheme","Compulsory unemployment insurance is part of the system of compulsory social insurance of citizens which provides rights in case of unemployment on the principles of obligation, reciprocity and solidarity.",""]],"56":[[1,"9","7","Monitoring and Evaluation of Reform Measures","Include monitoring and evaluation of measures introduced",""],[1,"9","7","Public Consultation Process Improvement","further improve the public consultation process by consulting businesses and social partners on the adoption and implementation of all new legislation concerning their operations",""],[1,"10","2","Public Policy Consultation and Coordination Handbook","A Draft Manual on Public Policy Consultation and Coordination within the IPA 2015 Public Administration Reform Support Project was prepared.",""],[1,"10","3","E-Participation Portal for Public Consultations","The e-participation portal should be established, and when it becomes fully operational - it will be used as an accompanying tool for the consultation process and public debate on regulations and public policy documents, as well as for informing stakeholders about the organization of focus groups, round tables, etc.",""],[1,"10","4","Public Hearing Monitoring and Proposer Form for Draft Regulations","The PPS monitors the process of conducting a public hearing during the regulatory preparation process.",""],[1,"10","5","Guidelines for Civil Society Inclusion in Policy Drafting Working Groups","the Government of the Republic of Serbia, by Conclusion 05 No. 011-722/2020, adopted Guidelines for Inclusion of Civil Society Organizations in Working Groups for Drafting Policy Proposals and Draft Regulations",""],[1,"10","6","Stakeholder Participation Guidelines for Policy Drafting","The purpose of the Guidelines is to regulate and encourage the involvement of stakeholders and target groups, primarily civil society organizations, in working groups formed by state administration bodies and thus ensure their participation in the decision-making process as early as possible.",""]],"57":[[1,"9","8","COVID-19 Economic Support Measures Coordination Body","Therefore, it is necessary to coordinate the activities undertaken in order to implement that program, which was done by forming the Coordinating Body for the implementation of the program in question.",""],[1,"11","2","Cross-Sectoral Covid-19 Coordination Mechanism","Ensure cross-sectoral coordination within the government and across public administration to effectively respond to Covid-19.",""],[1,"11","3","COVID-19 Economic Crisis Staff","The Government of the RS has formed a Crisis Staff to eliminate the occurrence and prevent possible harmful consequences of the infectious disease COVID-19 on the economy.",""]],"58":[[1,"59","1","Pension Indexation Method Definition","The method of indexation of pensions has also been defined.",""],[1,"60","1","Pension Indexation Reform Using the Swiss Formula","From 2020, pensions will be harmonized with the so-called \"Swiss formula\", in order to simultaneously ensure the growth of the living standard of pensioners and the sustainability of the pension system and the public finance system.",""],[1,"60","1","Indexation of Social Benefits and Transfers","Other forms of social benefits and transfers to the population in the coming period will be harmonized by applying the prescribed indexation, current and planned policy changes in this area and with the projected number of users.",""],[1,"77","2","Pension Indexation Reintroduction","As of this year, the indexation of pensions has been reintroduced, where pensions are adjusted using the \"Swiss formula\", while respecting the limit of 11% of GDP for total pension expenditures.",""]],"59":[[1,"29","3","Public Sector and Health Worker Salary Increase","the decision of the Government at the end of 2019 to increase salaries in the range from eight percent in the state administration to 15 percent for nurses, but also the decision to permanently increase salaries for health workers by 10% starting from April 2020",""],[1,"44","10","Health System Strengthening Investment","a significant part of the funds was invested in the health system in order to strengthen human resources and procure the necessary medical equipment, funds and medicines.",""],[1,"46","7","Health Worker Salary Increase","additional support was provided to health workers by increasing salaries by 10% from April this year",""],[1,"47","2","Public Health System Support for Coronavirus Response","Additional expenditures to support the public health system in the fight against the coronavirus pandemic are estimated at over RSD 60 billion, or 1.1% of GDP.",""],[1,"49","4","Health Capacity Expansion and Epidemiological Protection Investment","Increase in expenditures for additional health and epidemiological protection of the population, including the construction of additional health capacities and procurement of equipment;",""],[1,"52","9","Public Investment Expansion for Health Facilities and Equipment","One part of the larger execution is based on investments in new health facilities, as well as equipment that has a longer service life.",""],[1,"55","6","Additional Investment in the Health System","In 2021, the fiscal space will be used to increase capital investments, additional investment in the health system, a moderate increase in pensions and salaries in the public sector, and to relieve the tax burden on the economy.",""],[1,"56","3","Public Investment and Health System Investment Expansion","This, above all, refers to the expenditure side, in the form of increased public investment, as well as additional investment in the health system.",""],[1,"59","1","Increased Budget Allocation for Health and Education Functions","The social component of the budget has been improved by better targeting of social assistance programmes and greater allocation for health and education functions.",""],[1,"80","5","Health Care Digitalization","The COVID-19 epidemic highlighted the need for a more efficient health care system, to which its digitalization will significantly contribute.",""],[1,"81","1","Health System Improvement Reform","and a fourth to improve the health system",""]],"60":[[1,"38","3","Inflation Targeting Monetary Policy Regime","Since 2009, the NBS has been applying the inflation targeting regime as a monetary strategy.",""],[1,"38","3","Reserve Requirement Policy Framework","The reserve requirement policy is formulated in such a way that",""],[1,"39","1","Differentiated Reserve Requirement Policy","the differentiation of the reserve requirement rate, depending on the currency of liabilities and maturity, stimulates dinar and longer-term sources of bank financing.",""],[1,"40","2","Managed Floating Exchange Rate Regime","the NBS will continue to implement a managed floating exchange rate regime.",""]],"61":[[1,"16","2","Public Debt Dinarisation and Domestic Securities Market Development","It will be continued with the improvement of the currency structure of public debt in favour of dinar and issue long-term reference dinar securities, expand the investor base and promote the secondary market of these securities, and will continue with activities on their inclusion in the international bond index (JP Morgan GB Index).",""],[1,"16","2","Primary Dealers and Euroclear Settlement System","The process of establishing a system of primary dealers and enabling clearing and settlement of dinar securities at Euroclear is underway.",""],[1,"64","1","Public Debt Management Strategy","the Ministry of Finance of the Republic of Serbia - Administration for public debt prepares the Public Debt Management Strategy for the next medium term.","Ministry of Finance of the Republic of Serbia - Administration for public debt"],[1,"65","6","Fixed-Interest Public Borrowing Policy","contracting new liabilities will be done at fixed interest rates, where possible, especially in the field of loans financing investment projects.",""],[1,"65","7","Medium-Term Debt Strategy Cost-Risk Analysis","a cost-risk analysis of alternative borrowing strategies was performed, using the World Bank model (Medium Term Debt Strategy Model - MTDS)",""],[1,"65","8","Public Debt Management and Flexible Borrowing Strategy","The public debt management strategy in the next medium-term period is based on the assumption that financing will be provided by borrowing on both the domestic and international financial markets.",""],[1,"66","1","Primary Dealers System Introduction","In the coming period, we will actively work on the introduction of a system of primary dealers.",""],[1,"66","1","Financial Derivatives Risk Management Framework","These amendments to the Law also provide for the operation of financial derivatives that would be used to perform transactions for risk management, including the reduction or elimination of the risk of changes in exchange rates, interest rates and other risks.",""],[1,"66","2","Government Securities Clearing and Settlement Reform","Amendments to the Law on Public Debt from December 2019 enable the clearing and settlement of government securities issued on the domestic market, in addition to the Central Register, by another foreign legal entity that performs clearing and settlement operations.",""],[1,"56","1","Fiscal Consolidation and Public Debt Reduction Measures","The goals of fiscal policy in the next medium-term period will be the stabilization of public finances and the return of public debt to a declining trajectory.",""]],"62":[[1,"66","5","Fiscal Risk Management Institutional Strengthening","The organizational unit for fiscal risk management in the Ministry of Finance was established with the aim of working on strengthening legal regulations and methodological framework, capacity building, and developing technical tools and models necessary for monitoring and assessing fiscal risks.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"68","2","Restriction on New State Guarantees","Therefore, actions have been taken to limit the issuance of new guarantees.",""],[1,"68","4","Infrastructure Project Loan Guarantee Scheme","it is planned to issue guarantees up to a maximum of RSD 108 billion, for loans intended for the realization of infrastructure projects",""],[1,"68","5","Targeted New Guarantee Issuance Policy","limited and targeted issuance of new guarantees",""],[1,"70","4","Funding Allocation to Local Self-Government Units","and to place funds to local self-government units",""],[1,"72","6","Local Government Public Finance Control System Improvement","the Ministry of Finance will in the coming period significantly improve the public finances control system of local governments in order to comply with the rules from planning to budget implementation at the local level.","Ministry of Finance"]],"63":[[1,"20","3","Electricity Tariff Harmonization Reform","Gradually harmonize electricity tariffs to reflect real costs, including the costs of necessary maintenance and investment to improve the energy network and meet environmental standards and climate goals.",""],[1,"69","5","Tariff System Review for Cost Recovery","during 2020, an analysis of the tariff system was made, which would enable the company to be able to service the entire operating costs from regular operations, then the costs arising from the increased volume of expenditures arising from production from renewable energy sources, and the need for additional capital investments in existing and new production capacities.",""],[1,"81","10","Electricity Tariff Cost-Recovery Harmonization","Gradually harmonize electricity tariffs to reflect real costs, including the costs of necessary maintenance and investments to improve the energy network and meet environmental standards and climate goals.",""],[1,"82","4","Electricity Pricing and Regulation Reform","To strengthen human resources capacities and encourage investment in energy efficiency, inter alia through the establishment of a sustainable financing system, and to initiate reforms to introduce electricity prices that clearly reflect costs, fully taking into account investment needs, obligations in terms of climate change and the implications of social security, as well as the reform of electricity price regulation.",""]],"64":[[1,"37","4","Digital Transformation and Digital Ecosystem Development","The digital transformation and construction of the digital ecosystem remain the strategic orientation of the Government.",""],[1,"38","1","Digitalization for Capacity Utilization and Productivity","Digitization will significantly speed up these processes and further increase the efficiency of the utilization of available capacities.",""],[1,"80","1","Science and Research Financing Reform","The reform of the organization and financing of science and research in Serbia defines the introduction of institutional and competitive project financing as the most important novelties, as well as the establishment of the Science Fund.",""],[1,"80","1","Support for Innovative Start-ups in Creative Industries","In the following period, greater support will be provided to innovative start-up companies in the field of creative industries, as well as to the digital transformation of companies, while through the activities of the national platform Serbia Creates, adequate communication of the Serbian creative industry to the world will be enabled.",""],[1,"80","1","Digital Transformation Support for Companies","In the following period, greater support will be provided to innovative start-up companies in the field of creative industries, as well as to the digital transformation of companies, while through the activities of the national platform Serbia Creates, adequate communication of the Serbian creative industry to the world will be enabled.",""]],"65":[[1,"79","4","Circular Economy Strategic Framework","it is also planned to gradually introduce the concept of circular economy through the definition of a strategic framework as a tool for achieving sustainable development, in accordance with the UN Agenda 2030",""],[1,"83","13","Circular Economy Strategic Framework","It is planned to define a strategic framework for the circular economy by drafting a public policy document, encouraging the introduction of the concept of the circular economy in economic entities through the allocation of circular vouchers to encourage cooperation between business and academia, as well as encouraging the creation of circular economies for the local communities.",""]],"66":[[1,"37","4","Fiscalization and Customs Regulation Reform","The new system of fiscalization and changes in customs regulations will reduce the share of the grey economy in total economic flows, ensure affirmative competition and improve the economy and efficiency of procedures.",""],[1,"81","1","New Fiscalization Model and Electronic Invoicing Reform","another to introduce a new fiscalization model and move to electronic invoicing",""],[1,"84","10","Fiscalization Model and Electronic Invoicing Reform","Introduction of a new fiscalization model and transition to electronic invoicing",""],[1,"84","11","E-Fiscalization Digital Platform","The first measure involves the introduction of a new model of fiscalization (e- fiscalization) through a centralized digital platform within the Tax Administration, as well as online transmission and verification of data sent from fiscal cash registers to the Tax Administration.",""]],"67":[[1,"37","4","Public Administration Digitalization and Fiscalization Reform","More efficient work of the state administration, shortening of procedures for the population and the economy with a focus on digitalization will accelerate the convergence of our economy towards developed countries.",""],[1,"79","5","Strategic Digital Platform for the Geosector","the creation of a strategic digital platform for the geosector to support investment decision-making",""],[1,"80","1","Expansion of E-Government and ICT Infrastructure","In the field of digital economy, it is planned to increase the availability of e-government to citizens and the economy through the improvement of customer services, as well as further development of the national information and communication infrastructure.",""]],"68":[[1,"17","5","Bank Privatization and Restructuring Completion","Finalize the privatization restructuring remaining banks.",""],[1,"17","7","State Bank Privatization Process","The privatization process of Komercijalna Banka is underway, and is expected to be completed in mid- February 2020.",""],[1,"17","7","Transformation of Srpska Banka into a Specialized Financial Institution","on 21 January 2019, the Working Group for the transformation of Srpska banka into a specialized financial institution was established to provide all types of financial services and support the defence industry of Serbia.",""],[1,"17","7","Bank Poštanska Štedionica New Strategy Implementation","Bank Poštanska štedionica JSC Belgrade is in the process of implementing the new strategy, with the main focus on (i) commercial reorientation of the bank to retail banking, entrepreneurs, micro enterprises and small enterprises, (ii) improvement of the bank's internal organization, corporate governance and risk management, (iii) improvement of IT infrastructure and (iv) Business Strategy of the Bank Poštanska štedionica for the period 2020-2022.",""],[1,"70","2","State Financial Institutions Reform Continuation","reform activities in the area of state financial institutions, which began in 2012 and 2015, will continue.",""],[1,"70","3","Banka Poštanska štedionica Strategy Implementation","With the support of the World Bank, the implementation of the strategy for the Banka Poštanska štedionica will continue, with an emphasis on redirecting business with households, entrepreneurs, micro-enterprises and small businesses; improving the bank's internal organization, corporate governance and risk management; strengthening the IT infrastructure, as well as the business plan for the period 2020-2022.",""],[1,"70","5","Privatization of Komercijalna Banka","On 26 February 2020, representatives of the Ministry of Finance of the Republic of Serbia and JSC Nova Ljubljanska Banka Ljubljana signed an agreement on the purchase of shares of this bank owned by the Republic of Serbia, according to which 83.23% of the bank's ordinary shares were sold for EUR 387 million.","Ministry of Finance of the Republic of Serbia"],[1,"70","6","Transformation of Srpska Banka into a Specialized Financial Institution","the Expert Working Group for the Transformation of Srpska Banka into a specialized financial institution for providing all types of financial services and support to the purpose industry of the Republic of Serbia was formed on 21 January 2019 and began formal work in March 2019 when the constitutive session was held.",""],[1,"74","8","Financial Institution Reform Continuation","with the continuation of reforms of financial institutions (state-owned banks, state development agencies, etc.), in accordance with the",""],[1,"75","1","Structural and Institutional Reform Programme","Structural and institutional reforms in the next medium-term period will aim to improve the business environment, which contributes to a more successful EU accession process.",""]],"69":[[1,"16","4","Problem Loan Resolution Programme","Implement measures that form part of the recently adopted problem loan resolution programme (NPL) as well as the accompanying action plan, including those aimed at further resolving problem",""],[1,"16","9","Receivables Portfolio Sale","In June 2019, the Deposit Insurance Agency, supported by the Ministry of Finance (MoF), successfully completed the sale of the so-called \"Pilot Portfolio\" of receivables managed by the Agency on behalf of and for the benefit of the Republic of Serbia and bankrupt financial institutions in the nominal","Ministry of Finance (MoF)"],[1,"16","12","Problem Loan Resolution Portfolio Sale","In September 2019, the Deposit Insurance Agency, supported by the MoF, announced the sale of a portfolio of receivables in the nominal amount of EUR 1.82 billion, in accordance with the Programme for resolving problem loans.","Deposit Insurance Agency | MoF"],[1,"34","2","Bank NPL Resolution Regulatory Measures","the NBS has continued to take regulatory measures within its competence and use available instruments and supervisory mechanisms to encourage banks to solve NPLs more efficiently and establish a system to prevent their re-accumulation.",""],[1,"34","2","Mandatory Off-Balance-Sheet Transfer of Fully Impaired NPLs","banks are obliged to transfer to off-balance sheet records all NPLs that are fully impaired.",""],[1,"70","8","Non-Performing Loan Resolution Strategy","In August 2015, the NPL Resolution Strategy was adopted, which is implemented through the implementation of two three-year action plans, one prepared by the Government and the other prepared by the NBS, in order to lower the level of NPLs.",""],[1,"70","8","Bank Capacity Building for NPL Resolution","The key areas of implementation included strengthening the capacity of banks to resolve NPLs, improving regulations for assessing the value of collateral, developing the market for NPLs, etc.",""],[1,"70","8","Collateral Valuation Regulation Improvement","The key areas of implementation included strengthening the capacity of banks to resolve NPLs, improving regulations for assessing the value of collateral, developing the market for NPLs, etc.",""],[1,"70","8","Non-Performing Loan Market Development","The key areas of implementation included strengthening the capacity of banks to resolve NPLs, improving regulations for assessing the value of collateral, developing the market for NPLs, etc.",""],[1,"70","9","Non-Performing Loan Prevention and Receivables Write-Off Measures","numerous measures have been implemented to facilitate the write-off and transfer of uncollected receivables.",""],[1,"74","8","Non-Performing Loan Reduction Activities","activities for their reduction will continue, with the continuation of reforms of financial institutions (state-owned banks, state development agencies, etc.), in accordance with the",""]],"70":[[1,"70","7","Banking Sector Regulatory Reform and Supervision Strengthening","The reform of regulations governing the Serbian financial system was implemented in February 2015.",""],[1,"71","3","Deposit Insurance System","Deposit insurance is a mechanism that contributes to the preservation of financial stability and provides protection for depositors.",""],[1,"71","4","Deposit Insurance Fund Financing and Bank Resolution Support","AOD collects deposit insurance premiums from banks for the account of the Deposit Insurance Fund, manages the fund's assets and pays deposits up to the insured amount in case of bankruptcy or liquidation of the bank.",""],[1,"71","5","Banking System Supervision and Asset Quality Improvement","Supervision of the banking system, prudence in the placement of funds and improvement of the quality of banks' assets are the basic pillars of a stable banking system.",""]],"71":[[1,"18","4","Alternative Investment Funds Legal Framework","Adopt special laws on alternative investment funds.",""],[1,"35","6","Instant Payment System Reform and Expansion","The NBS supported the reform of the legal framework and the establishment of the instant payment system - IPS NBS system.",""],[1,"35","6","Merchant QR and Mobile Payment Enablement","A special incentive for the further development and popularization of non- cash payments in the country and competition with card payments from the beginning of 2020 is given by a new method of payment at merchants' points of sale, \"IPS scan\"\"\"IPS show\", which banks have enabled users in mobile banking applications and which enables fast and easy payment, with the current availability of funds in the merchant's account.",""],[1,"36","1","Payment System Infrastructure Development and Upgrade","Further development and improvement of the payment system infrastructure will continue during 2021, when users will be provided with other functionalities of the IPS NBS system.",""],[1,"36","2","Digital Assets Regulatory Framework","the Law on Digital Assets (\"Official Gazette of the RS\", No. 153/20) was adopted in the Republic of Serbia for the first time, which comprehensively regulates the issuance of digital assets, secondary trading in digital assets, the provision of services related to digital assets and the supervision of the business of the persons providing those services.",""],[1,"36","3","Crowdfunding and Alternative Financing Law","the NBS will complete the started activities on drafting a law which will regulate group financing (crowdfunding) and alternative financing, which, while respecting the characteristics of the domestic financial market, will be harmonized with the relevant EU regulation adopted in 2020.",""]],"72":[[1,"17","3","Online Bankruptcy Asset Auction Portal","the establishment of an Internet portal for online auctions of bankruptcy assets",""],[1,"17","4","Online Bankruptcy Asset Auction Portal","Activities on the establishment of the Internet portal for online auctions of bankruptcy assets are also underway, with delays caused by the pandemic.",""]],"73":[[1,"55","5","Reform of Large Public Companies","planned tax policy which implies further harmonization with EU laws and directives and fiscal and structural measures, including further reform of large public companies.",""],[1,"68","3","State and Public Company Restructuring Programme","a key step in reducing and eliminating fiscal risks on this basis is to reform state and public companies, beneficiaries of guarantees, in order to be able to repay their loans.",""],[1,"68","5","Public and State-Owned Enterprise Structural Reform","Structural reforms of public and state-owned enterprises, making them prepared for market competition and financial sustainability",""],[1,"69","3","Public Enterprise Governance and Restructuring Programme","At the beginning of 2016, a new Law on Public Enterprises was adopted, which will strengthen the management structure and responsibility of public enterprises.",""],[1,"69","4","Corporate Governance Improvement Action Plan","The Action Plan for Improving Corporate Governance, based on the recommendations of the EBRD and adopted by the Government in February 2019, is being successfully implemented.",""],[1,"76","3","Public and State-Owned Enterprise Reform","reforms of the largest public and state-owned enterprises are continuing.",""],[1,"76","3","Arrears Repayment and Prevention Measures","In the following period, a plan will be made to repay the accumulated arrears caused by the pandemic and new measures will be adopted in order to prevent their accumulation in the future.",""]],"74":[[1,"69","5","EPS Legal Restructuring and Financial Consolidation","It is envisaged that, during 2021, EPS will change its legal status and register as a joint stock company, which is in line with the current process of restructuring and financial consolidation of the company, with the aim of improving profitability and professionalizing company management.",""],[1,"69","5","EPS Fixed Asset Valuation Exercise","during the last quarter of 2020, a public call was published to assess the value of the company's fixed assets.",""]],"75":[[1,"69","6","Overdue Receivables Collection Measures","it is planned to implement all necessary measures for the collection of overdue receivables, which arose during the state of emergency.",""],[1,"69","7","Receivables Collection and Debt Recovery Measures","The company regularly updates the list of the 20 largest debtors on its website, with the intention of taking all necessary measures to collect overdue receivables.",""]],"76":[[1,"37","1","Agricultural Competitiveness and EU IPARD II Support","Achieving European standards and raising competitiveness in agriculture, by fulfilling the conditions for opening Chapter 11 and through the use of the EU IPARD II programme, will reduce the variability of production in this sector caused by agro meteorological conditions.",""],[1,"60","1","Reallocation of Subsidies to Development Programmes","The reduction of subsidies that serve to help inefficient segments of the public sector enables an increase in the part of subsidies that represent real incentives to the economy, primarily agriculture and small and medium enterprises, and which lead to an acceleration of economic activity.",""],[1,"81","1","Agricultural Reform Redefinition Process","In the field of agriculture in this cycle there are three reforms created through the process of redefining the reforms (two of them) from the previous cycle.",""],[1,"83","4","Rural Infrastructure Development","Improvement of rural infrastructure by constructing: local roads, electricity networks, water supply, as well as investments in environmental protection plants, which should contribute to a higher level of development of rural areas and increase the number of production and processing capacities.",""],[1,"83","4","Agricultural Market Legal Framework Reform","Improving the legal framework in the field of agricultural products market, in accordance with EU regulations, with a focus on the introduction of standards in production and the formation of producer organizations.",""],[1,"83","4","Geographical Indications Protection System","The development of a system of protection of geographical indications for agricultural and food products, in accordance with the European system, will contribute to the increase of agri- food products with added value.",""],[1,"83","4","Organic Agriculture Regulatory Framework","Establishment of a regulatory framework for the production of agricultural and food organic products, as well as other issues relevant to organic production.",""]],"77":[[1,"82","15","Accelerated IPARD II Application Processing","speed up the processing of applications for measures already entrusted under IPARD II in order to avoid the loss of EU funds and to continue entrusting tasks related to the execution of the budget for other measures under the program.",""],[1,"82","15","Accelerated IPA II Implementation","Accelerate the implementation of IPA II pre-",""],[1,"83","5","IPARD II Program Implementation and Budget Execution Entrustment","To implement the measures entrusted under the IPARD II program and request the entrustment of tasks related to the execution of the budget for other measures under the program.",""],[1,"83","7","IPARD II Measures Processing and Task Entrustment Acceleration","speed up the processing of applications for measures already entrusted under IPARD II in order to avoid the loss of EU funds and to continue entrusting tasks related to the execution of the budget for other measures under the program",""],[1,"83","7","Agriculture and Rural Development Acquis Alignment Action Plan","continue to implement the action plan in a timely manner to ensure alignment with the EU acquis in the field of agriculture and rural development",""],[1,"83","7","IPA II Pre-accession Funds Acceleration","Accelerate the implementation of IPA II pre-accession funds in order to avoid the need for last minute contracting",""],[1,"83","7","IPARD II Measure Implementation and Task Entrustment Request","To implement the measures entrusted under the IPARD II program and request the entrustment of tasks related to the execution of the budget for other measures under the program",""],[1,"83","7","Agriculture and Rural Development Acquis Harmonization Action Plan","To continue with the implementation of the action plan for harmonization with the acquis communautaire in the field of agriculture and rural development",""]],"78":[[1,"81","1","Spatial Development Management Improvement Reform","a third to improve spatial development management",""]],"79":[[1,"84","13","Strategic Digital Platform for Geospatial Investment Decisions","Improvement of geospatial sector through development of a strategic digital platform to support investment decision- making",""],[1,"84","14","National Geospatial Platform and NSDI Development","It is planned to update the address register and establish its interoperability, develop the regulatory and strategic framework of the NSDI, improve the National Geospatial Platform, as well as harmonize, combine data for the development of prototypes of the mass assessment system.",""],[1,"84","15","Geospatial Data and Property Rights Registration Reform","Strategy of measures and activities for increasing the quality of services in the field of geospatial data and registration of rights to real estate in the official state records - the reform path of the Republic Geodetic Authority until 2020 NSDI Law",""],[1,"84","16","Real Estate Taxation System Reform","The process has rightly been identified as a major potential challenge and should contribute to the real estate taxation system and increase property tax revenues locally.",""],[1,"84","16","Strengthen Ministry and Judiciary Involvement in Property Tax Administration","Greater involvement of the ministry and the judiciary in the process is needed, which is currently the sole responsibility of the Geodetic Authority.",""],[1,"84","17","E-Space Digital Platform for Spatial Development Management","Improvement of spatial development management in the Republic of Serbia through establishment of e-space digital platform",""],[1,"84","18","Digital Urban and Spatial Planning Platform","Digitalization of data and procedures of urban and spatial planning and the formation of a digital platform e- Space are planned.",""]],"80":[[1,"85","22","WTO Accession Process Continuation","The reform envisages the continuation of the WTO accession process, the implementation of the Multi- Annual Action Plan for the Creation of a Regional Economic Area (MAP REA), the implementation of activities under CEFTA Additional Protocols 5 and 6 and the opening of",""],[1,"85","23","Ratification of CEFTA Additional Protocol 5","Law on Ratification of Additional Protocol 5 to the Agreement Amending and Accession to the Central European Free Trade Agreement (CEFTA 2006)",""],[1,"85","23","Ratification of EFTA Joint Committee Decision No. 2/2018","Law on Ratification of the Decision of the Joint Committee between the EFTA States and the Republic of Serbia No. 2/2018",""],[1,"85","24","WTO Accession and Trade Agreement Implementation","complete WTO accession by adopting amendments to the Law on Genetically Modified Organisms and completing the remaining bilateral market access negotiations; further strengthen MTTT's administrative capacity to manage trade with the EU, accede to CEFTA and accede to the WTO; implement actions under the multi-","MTTT"],[1,"86","4","National Coordination Body for Trade Facilitation","Decision of the Government of the Republic of Serbia on the establishment of the National Coordination Body for Trade Facilitation",""],[1,"86","5","REA Development Action Plan","annual action plan for the development of the REA, in particular to: ensure the full implementation of Additional Protocol 5 on trade facilitation to the CEFTA agreement; implements Additional Protocol 6 on trade in services to the CEFTA agreement; negotiate and conclude Additional Protocol 7 on Dispute Resolution to the CEFTA Agreement; and adopt regional standards for international investment agreements and continue to implement an individual investment reform action plan.",""]],"81":[[1,"86","7","Competitiveness Improvement Financial Support","The reform envisages financial support to economic entities in improving competitiveness, i.e. safety and quality of products and services, using the latest standards organization.",""],[1,"86","7","Product-Info Digital Service Development","the construction of a unique digital service \"Product-Info\" is planned, with the aim of improving information and availability of digital services in connection with the application of technical regulations.",""],[1,"86","9","Acquis Alignment and Enforcement Strategy for Food Safety and Veterinary and Phytosanitary Policy","develop a comprehensive strategy for alignment with the acquis, implementation and enforcement of the acquis in the field of food safety, veterinary and phytosanitary policy.",""],[1,"86","9","Product Contact Point Operating Procedures","it is recommended to establish detailed procedures for the functioning of the Product Contact Point (PCP).",""]],"82":[[1,"86","12","Dual Vocational Education Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","Continuation of the reform of secondary vocational education by improving the model of dual education through the establishment and implementation of a framework for monitoring and evaluation of dual educational profiles, which enables data-based decision making and ensures the quality of dual education, as well as infrastructure and training centers.",""],[1,"86","12","Online Database for Work-Based Learning Content","As one of the answers to the new epidemiological situation, an online database will be created, which will contain teaching units that are implemented in educational institutions and topics for learning through work in companies.",""],[1,"86","12","Recognition of Prior Learning Pilot and NOKS Register Entry","In terms of the implementation of the NOKS system, it is planned to pilot the procedure of recognition of prior learning, as well as to enter data into the NOKS Register.",""],[1,"86","14","National Qualifications Framework Institutional Strengthening","make the institutional structure for the NQF fully functional.",""],[1,"86","14","National Qualifications Framework Alignment with European Qualifications Framework","Link the NQF to the European Qualifications Framework and make the institutional structure fully functional.",""]],"83":[[1,"87","9","Single Social Card Register","The reform implies the establishment of a single Social Card Register, which will enable an overview of the social and material status of users.",""],[1,"87","9","Integrated Social Protection Network","It is planned to connect social protection institutions, and primarily centers for social work, into a single network, as well as to collect and use data from all available sources of state administration.",""],[1,"87","9","Social Protection Regulatory Framework","It is also envisaged to establish a regulatory framework by adopting appropriate laws and bylaws.",""],[1,"87","11","Expand Social Protection Coverage","Expand social protection coverage.",""],[1,"87","11","Strengthen Social Transfers for Income Support","Strengthen social transfers to ensure adequate income support for people at risk of poverty and social exclusion.",""],[1,"87","11","Targeted Employment and Social Policy Resource Support","provide adequate financial and institutional resources for employment and social policy in order to be more systematically targeted at young people, women and the long-term unemployed, and to improve the adequacy of social benefits for people below the poverty line; ensure consistent implementation of labor and social protection legislation throughout the country.",""]],"84":[[1,"87","14","Health Sector Sustainable Financing","Ensure adequate and sustainable funding to strengthen the health care sector in order to improve access to quality public health care for all citizens.",""]],"85":[[1,"88","3","Digitalization of Energy Sector Administrative Procedures","The Action Plan for the implementation of the Government's policy for the period 2020-2022 foresees the digitalization of administrative procedures in the field of energy sector by the end of 2022.",""],[1,"88","4","Digitalization of Mining and Geological Sector Business Processes","it is necessary to improve the legal regulations and digitalization of business processes within the Sector for Geology and Mining, digitalization of geological documentation and improvement of the operations of the Geological Survey of Serbia.",""]],"86":[[1,"90","3","Regulated Electricity and Gas Tariff Policy for Vulnerable Households","It is necessary to set the price of electricity24 for households and small-scale consumers so as to reflect the costs of electricity production network charges and market prices, taking into account the standard of living and protection of energy vulnerable customers.",""]],"87":[[1,"88","1","Energy Efficiency and Renewable Energy Expansion","In order to increase the contribution of the energy sector to economic growth, it is necessary to improve energy efficiency, build modern capacities, develop the internal market and use renewable energy sources.",""],[1,"90","4","Energy Efficiency Measures and Renewable Energy Deployment","it is necessary to implement the adopted energy efficiency measures and use renewable energy sources.",""],[1,"97","5","Energy Consumption Reduction Reform","The reform will reduce energy consumption, which will have a favourable impact on the environment and reduce emissions of all flue gases, including greenhouse gases, that being in line with the objectives of the European Green Deal.",""]],"88":[[1,"90","6","Old Large Combustion Plant Emissions Reduction Plan","National Plan for the Reduction of the Main Pollutant Emissions from Old Large Combustion Plants, adopted in February 2020, prescribes maximum emissions of sulphur dioxide, nitrogen oxides and dust particles per year.",""],[1,"90","6","Coal Plant Emissions Control Investments","Particle pollution has been reduced and a contribution has been made to the denitrification and desulphurisation of flue gases through investments in coal quality management systems, systems for the reduction of sulphur and nitrogen oxides and the installation of electrostatic precipitators.",""],[1,"90","6","Flue Gas Desulphurisation Projects at TPP Nikola Tesla","The construction of the flue gas desulphurisation system in TPP \"Nikola Tesla A\" in Obrenovac is underway, and should be completed in mid-2022, which will contribute to 10 times less emission of sulphur dioxide, and the flue gas desulphurisation project at TENT B has begun and should be completed in the first quarter of 2024.",""],[1,"90","6","Environmental Protection and Improvement Fees","The Law on Fees for Use of Public Resources, has introduced environmental protection and improvement fees.",""],[1,"91","1","Pollution Fee System","pay amounts in proportion to the type and quantity of pollution released.",""]],"89":[[1,"92","2","Combined and Intermodal Transport Capacity Development","Establishment and strengthening of combined/intermodal transport capacity continues through stimulus measures, however, although funds have been allocated for these purposes in the 2020 budget, due to the need to provide additional funds to eliminate the negative impact of COVID-19, the funds have been assigned for other purposes.",""],[1,"92","2","Intermodal Terminal Construction in Batajnica","Construction of the Intermodal Terminal in Batajnica, Belgrade, has started in 2020.",""],[1,"92","3","Border Trade and Transport Facilitation Project","The implementation of the project \"Trade and Transport Facilitation\" will enable the introduction of entirely electronic operation and the improvement of security controls in the field of customs operations.",""],[1,"92","3","Single National Window System","This project also includes the introduction of the \"Single National Window\" system (enables synchronization of the work of all services at border crossings), as well as the creation of conditions for the introduction of intelligent transport systems (ITS) on Corridor 10.",""],[1,"92","3","Intelligent Transport Systems Development on Corridor 10","This project also includes the introduction of the \"Single National Window\" system (enables synchronization of the work of all services at border crossings), as well as the creation of conditions for the introduction of intelligent transport systems (ITS) on Corridor 10.",""],[1,"92","3","National Plan for ERTMS Implementation","The National Plan for the Implementation of the European Rail Traffic Management System (ERTMS) is also being prepared, as a basis for the introduction of ITS in railway traffic.",""],[1,"92","3","Strategic Framework and Legislative Adjustment for ITS","In order to develop ITS in the RS, it is necessary to adopt a strategic framework, adjust legislation and provide capacity for implementation, which will improve the operation of customs services, reduce and simplify border procedures, reduce time delays at border crossings and improve regional cooperation.",""]],"90":[[1,"92","4","Hydrographic Activity Legal Reform","The Law on Hydrographic Activity has further improved the conditions of navigation on inland waterways.",""],[1,"92","4","Inland Waterway Navigation and Port Law Amendments","Amendments to the Law on Navigation and Ports on Inland Waters enabled a more precise determination of the profitability of port services, the operations of port operators and the position of the Port Management Agency.",""],[1,"92","4","Water Transport Safety and Environmental Protection Strategy Update","Amendments to the Strategy for the Development of Water Transport of the Republic of Serbia from 2015-2025 enhanced the safety and security of maritime ships and facilities and the protection of the environment from pollution from ships pursuant to the international regulations.",""],[1,"92","4","National Ship and Shipyard Safety Protection Programme","The adopted National Program for Safety Protection of Ships and Shipyards created the basis for increasing safety in navigable traffic.",""],[1,"92","4","Regional Water Transport Cooperation and RIS Implementation","The strengthening of regional cooperation, active participation in the EU Strategy for the Danube Region and the implementation of RIS has continued.",""],[1,"92","5","River Transport Infrastructure Development Project","The realization of the project for the development of river transport infrastructure totalling EUR 400 million has continued, involving: reconstruction of navigation locks within HPP \"Djerdap 1\" and \"Djerdap 2\", expansion of the capacity of the Port of Smederevo, regulation of the waterway and critical sector on the Sava River, the salvage of sunken World War II-era warships, introduction of hydro-meteorological station and modern water traffic management system.",""],[1,"92","5","Port Capacity Expansion and New Port Development","Complete technical documentation is being prepared for expanding the capacity of ports in Bogojevo, Prahovo and Sremska Mitrovica, as well as for the construction of a new port in Belgrade, for the works of which funds are provided from EIB loans for port infrastructure development in Serbia, loans for integrated development of the Drina and Sava Corridors and the RS budget.",""],[1,"92","5","Marina Port Area Designation Decrees","Decree on determining the port area of the port for special purposes - marina in Kladovo (\"Official Gazette of the RS\", No. 11/20) and the Decree on determining the port area of the port for special purposes - marina in Golubac (\"Official Gazette of the RS\", No. 104/20) were adopted, which",""],[1,"93","1","Detailed Regulation Plan for Lepenski Vir","The development of the Detailed Regulation Plan for Lepenski Vir is in progress, which should enable further realization of the Project for the construction of an international passenger port in Lepenski Vir, and works on the construction of an international passenger port in the settlement of Ram are underway, too.",""],[1,"93","1","International Passenger Port Construction in Lepenski Vir","The development of the Detailed Regulation Plan for Lepenski Vir is in progress, which should enable further realization of the Project for the construction of an international passenger port in Lepenski Vir, and works on the construction of an international passenger port in the settlement of Ram are underway, too.",""],[1,"93","1","International Passenger Port Construction in Ram","The development of the Detailed Regulation Plan for Lepenski Vir is in progress, which should enable further realization of the Project for the construction of an international passenger port in Lepenski Vir, and works on the construction of an international passenger port in the settlement of Ram are underway, too.",""]],"91":[[1,"93","2","Air Transport Law Amendments and Airspace Management Reform","Amendments to the Air Transport Law have further improved security at airports and security checks and controls. The Regulation on Airspace Management enables more efficient use of airspace.",""],[1,"93","2","Morava Airport Cargo-Logistics Centre Development","the third international Morava Airport near Kraljevo has started operating (this airport is planned to become a cargo-logistics centre in Serbia).",""]],"92":[[1,"100","9","Simplified Seasonal Employment Regulation for Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries","the new legal regulation enables a simplified way of employment of persons and payment of taxes and contributions for seasonal work in this sector.",""]],"93":[[1,"101","2","eMarket Serbia Agricultural Product Sales Platform","the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Water Management has launched a platform for the sale of agricultural products eMarket Serbia28, which began operations in April 2020.","Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Water Management"],[1,"101","2","Digital Sales Networks for Agricultural Products","Websites and electronic sales networks have been founded in order to maintain continuity in the sale of agricultural products.",""],[1,"101","3","IPARD Incentives for Farm Diversification and Business Development","The first public call for the submission of applications for approval of projects for IPARD incentives for diversification of farms and business development was published in 2020.",""],[1,"103","1","Agricultural Holdings Diversification and Business Development Support","The first public call related to the diversification of agricultural holdings and business development (Measure 7) was announced in June 2020 and ended on 30 October 2020 with 311 requests received.",""],[1,"103","2","Agricultural Investment and Logistics Support","It is necessary to support investments in sectors where Serbia has comparative advantages (fruit, vegetable, livestock production sectors), improve business management and provide adequate logistical support.",""],[1,"110","9","Accelerated Incentive Payment for Agricultural Value Chain Liquidity","Accelerating the payment of incentives contributes to improving the liquidity of the overall value chain of primary agricultural production - processing.",""],[1,"118","8","Agricultural Production and Mechanization Incentives","Incentives to improve agricultural production and investments in equipment and machinery",""]],"94":[[1,"101","6","Rural Development Support Measures for Young Farmers","In the implementation of national rural development support measures, as well as the accredited IPARD measures that are currently implemented, young farmers have the advantage of scoring and ranking projects/beneficiaries.",""],[1,"101","6","Subsidy Regulation for Young Farmers","Regulation on the allocation of subsidies in agriculture and rural development to support young farmers resulted in disbursement of 200 million dinars.",""],[1,"108","3","Rural Infrastructure and Land Consolidation Measures","Measures to improve rural infrastructure, infrastructural land equipping, increasing the productive capacity of land, increasing the availability of land resources through land consolidation directly affect employment and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"108","3","Unused Land Transfer Mechanism for Young People and Women","Following the land consolidation procedure, a mechanism for the transfer of unused land to young people and women may be established.",""],[1,"108","11","Inclusive Job Placement and Hiring System","Systematize and fill job places hiring individuals with different educational profiles",""],[1,"111","1","Agricultural Subsidy Payment Efficiency Reform","Increasing the efficiency in the payment of subsidies for agricultural production and enhancing the effectiveness in planning agricultural policy measures contributes to the acceleration of the movement of goods and services in agriculture, effectively contributing to increasing employment and reducing poverty.",""],[1,"114","5","Rural Infrastructure Development","The development of rural infrastructure enables individuals and legal entities to develop their own businesses - production and processing capacities, i.e. their self- employment and employment of the local population.",""]],"95":[[1,"102","1","Irrigation Systems Development Phase I","In order to continue the implementation of the project \"Development of irrigation systems - Phase I\" in 2020, 10 contracts were concluded for the construction, rehabilitation and arrangement of water facilities in the area of Bačka, Banat and Srem, as well as construction, reconstruction and modernization of water facilities in Čačak, Pančevački rit and Topola.",""],[1,"102","1","Regional Irrigation Infrastructure Expansion","In 2021, financing of the construction work, rehabilitation and arrangement of water facilities through the implementation of 8 projects in the area of Bačka, Banat and Srem is planned to be continued, which will provide conditions for irrigation of additional 57,248 ha of agricultural land, as well as construction of hydromelioration system on the territory of the municipality of Paraćin.",""],[1,"102","1","Climate-Resilient Irrigation Infrastructure Programme","Also, through the implementation of the Serbian Climate Resilience & Irrigation Programme SCRIP - Phase I, building and rehabilitation of the critical irrigation infrastructure in eastern Serbia (Negotin municipality) and central Serbia (Svilajnac municipality) has been planned.",""],[1,"102","1","Agricultural Irrigation Systems Procurement Support","Procurement of irrigation systems for agricultural holdings is supported through national measures to promote rural development and through the IPARD programme.",""],[1,"102","6","Canal Maintenance and Hydromelioration Infrastructure Works","Works on enhanced maintenance of canals - dual-purpose systems Rečej, Međa, Itebej, Jankov most I and II, on construction of pumping stations Kaloča, Jegrička and Pesir and works on subsystem Nova Crnja - Žitište and Tisa - Palić, Kikinda - CS Mokrinska II have been completed, Mali Iđoš, as well as works on the construction of the section of the canal Kula - Mali Iđoš, from km 10 + 310 to km 15 + 300 on the subsystem Mali Iđoš and the hydromelioration system in the area of Šabac.",""]],"96":[[1,"102","2","Agricultural Insurance Premium Subsidy Scheme","To reduce damage caused by natural disasters, the Government has been subsidising insurance premiums.",""]],"97":[[1,"103","3","Agricultural Green Deal Legal Framework","the future legal framework in the field of agriculture in the Republic of Serbia will include the goals and activities of this plan, in terms of establishing a fair, healthy and environmentally friendly supply chain of food products, and through reduced use of pesticides, fertilisers and antibiotics, as well as reduced risk of their use on the one hand, and improvement of environmental protection and biodiversity conservation, on the other.",""],[1,"103","3","Emission-Standard Compliance for Supported Agricultural Machinery and Equipment","All investments in machinery and equipment that are the subject of support must meet the standards concerning the emission of harmful gases.",""]],"98":[[1,"111","8","Rural Infrastructure Enhancement","The reform, which aims to improve the competitiveness of agriculture, comprises two components: Enhancement of rural infrastructure and Improvement to the legal framework in the field of regulation of agricultural products market, quality schemes for agricultural and food products and in the field of organic production.",""],[1,"111","10","Rural Infrastructure Development Investment","it is necessary to improve rural infrastructure through the construction of: local roads; power network; water supply; as well as investments in environmental protection facilities such as wastewater treatment plants or landfills",""],[1,"113","1","Preparation of Rural Infrastructure Implementation Rulebooks","Preparation of rulebooks for the implementation of measures to improve rural infrastructure",""],[1,"113","2","Training for Rural Infrastructure Improvement Implementers","Training of employees who will implement the measure of improvement of rural infrastructure",""],[1,"113","3","Rural Infrastructure Improvement Measures Call","Announcement of a public call for measures to improve rural infrastructure",""],[1,"113","9","Rural Infrastructure Enhancement for Competitiveness","it is necessary to provide appropriate infrastructure.",""],[1,"113","9","Wastewater Treatment and Landfill Construction","Construction of wastewater treatment plants and landfills will contribute to meeting environmental standards.",""],[1,"115","1","Rural Infrastructure Improvement Measure","Implementation of the structural measure for the improvement of rural infrastructure contributes to the preservation of the environment, since the investments in this regard are intended to finance the construction of wastewater treatment plants and waste management.",""],[1,"115","6","Continuous Education and Expert Support for Project Preparation","Continuous education and expert support to users to prepare adequate projects",""]],"99":[[1,"111","8","Agricultural Market and Organic Production Regulatory Reform","The reform, which aims to improve the competitiveness of agriculture, comprises two components: Enhancement of rural infrastructure and Improvement to the legal framework in the field of regulation of agricultural products market, quality schemes for agricultural and food products and in the field of organic production.",""],[1,"112","2","Agricultural Products Market and Quality Scheme Legal Framework Reform","Improvement to the legal framework in the field of regulation of agricultural products market, quality schemes for agricultural and food products and in the field of organic production",""],[1,"112","3","Agricultural Market and Organic Production Legal Reform","Improvement to the legal framework in the field of regulation of agricultural products market, quality schemes for agricultural and food products and in the field of organic production implies the adoption of the Law on Agricultural Market Regulation, the Law on Quality Schemes for Agricultural and Food Sector and the Law on Organic Production and accompanying bylaws.",""],[1,"112","4","Agricultural Market Regulation and Quality Schemes Reform","The Law on Regulation of the Market of Agricultural Products should regulate markets by sectors in a unique way, with an emphasis on the introduction of standards in production and enable the formation of producer organizations.",""],[1,"112","4","Agricultural and Food Quality Schemes Law","The adoption of the Law on Quality Schemes for Agricultural and Food Sector will establish a system of protection of geographical indications and designations of Traditional speciality guaranteed which is equal to the European one, which will allow our producers to sell their products with protected geographical indications and protection at EU level.",""],[1,"112","4","Organic Production Regulatory Framework","The new Law on Organic Production will prescribe special rules for the production of agricultural and food organic products, animal feed, methods of control and certification procedures in organic production, transport, storage, labelling, sale, import and export of organic products, as well as other issues relevant to organic production.",""],[1,"113","4","Agricultural Products Market Regulation Law","Adoption of The Law on Regulation of the Market of Agricultural Products",""],[1,"113","5","Law on Quality Schemes for Agricultural and Food Sector","Adoption of The Law on Quality Schemes for Agricultural and Food Sector",""],[1,"113","6","Organic Production Law Adoption","Adoption of The Law on Organic Production",""],[1,"113","10","Agricultural Market Regulation Legal Framework Reform","Improvement to the legal framework in the field of agricultural market regulation, as well as improvement to the legal framework in the field of quality schemes for agricultural and food products and in the field of organic production",""],[1,"113","12","Agricultural and Food Product Quality Schemes Development","Developing quality schemes for agricultural and food products will enable domestic producers to protect their products with protected geographical indications at EU level.",""],[1,"113","12","Food Product Quality Control System Improvement","Also, a more efficient quality control system of these products will be introduced, and the development of national quality schemes will be enabled.",""],[1,"114","2","Agricultural Market Regulation and Quality Scheme Legal Framework Reform","Improvement to the legal framework in the field of agricultural market regulation, as well as in the field of quality schemes for agricultural and food products and in the field of organic production",""],[1,"114","3","Agricultural Products Market Regulation Law Implementation Support","Adoption of the Law on Regulation of the Market of Agricultural Products, as well as its implementation requires certain costs related to training, familiarisation of producers with the changes that will follow, procurement of hardware and software, increase of administrative capacity.",""],[1,"114","4","Implementation of Agricultural and Food Quality Schemes and Organic Production Laws","Adoption of the Law on Quality Schemes for Agricultural and Food Products and the Law on Organic Production as well as their implementation requires certain costs related to increasing administrative capacity, conducting trainings and information campaigns.",""],[1,"114","6","Agricultural Market and Quality Regulation Legal Framework Reform","Improvement to the legal framework in the field of agricultural market regulation, as well as in the field of quality schemes for agricultural and food products and in the field of organic production",""],[1,"114","7","Agricultural and Food Market Regulation Law Implementation","The application of the Law on Regulation of the Market of Agricultural and Food Products enables a legally regulated appearance of all entities on the market and will directly encourage the emergence of new legal entities in the sector of production, processing and trade of agricultural products, including employment.",""],[1,"114","8","Implementation of the Law on Quality Schemes for Agricultural and Food Products","The implementation of the Law on Quality Schemes for Agricultural and Food Products will contribute to better regulation of the system of protection of geographical indications of agricultural and food products and the establishment of official control of products with geographical indications on the market.",""],[1,"115","2","Agricultural Market Regulation Legal Framework Reform","Improvement to the legal framework in the field of agricultural market regulation, as well as improvement to the legal framework in the field of quality schemes for agricultural and food products and in the field of organic production",""],[1,"115","2","Agricultural and Food Quality Schemes Legal Framework Reform","Improvement to the legal framework in the field of agricultural market regulation, as well as improvement to the legal framework in the field of quality schemes for agricultural and food products and in the field of organic production",""],[1,"115","2","Organic Production Legal Framework Reform","Improvement to the legal framework in the field of agricultural market regulation, as well as improvement to the legal framework in the field of quality schemes for agricultural and food products and in the field of organic production",""]],"100":[[1,"112","5","Curfew Movement Permit for Agricultural Producers","the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Water Management issued a public announcement prescribing instructions for applying for a license to move during curfew, intended for fruit and vegetable producers.","Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Water Management"],[1,"112","6","Agricultural COVID-19 Support Measures","The programme of economic measures to support agriculture was adopted in April 2020, through three decrees: Decree establishing a guarantee scheme as an economic support measure to mitigate the consequences of the COVID-19, as well as the Decree on financial aid to agricultural holdings and the Decree on financial support to agricultural holdings through easier access to usage of loans in adverse economic conditions caused by the COVID-19.",""]],"101":[[1,"104","2","Entrepreneurship Portal Reactivation and Improvement","the Entrepreneurship Portal37 has been reactivated providing up-to- date information on start-up and business development programs.",""],[1,"104","6","E-commerce Guide for Citizens","Publishing a guide for e-commerce intended for citizens on the online platform \"Smart and Safe\" is also aimed at strengthening e-commerce in Serbia.",""]],"102":[[1,"105","2","Instant Payments System","the instant payments system started to operate in October 2018",""]],"103":[[1,"105","3","Tourism Trip Replacement Voucher Decree","the Government of the Republic of Serbia adopted the Decree on offering a replacement journey for a tourist trip that was cancelled or not realized due to the COVID-19 pandemic (\"Official Gazette of the RS\", No. 63/20).",""],[1,"105","3","Domestic Tourism Voucher Subsidy Scheme","Encouragement of the development of domestic tourism is implemented through the allocation of vouchers for subsidized use of accommodation services in hospitality facilities, on the territory of the Republic of Serbia for a period of at least five nights, outside the residence of the voucher user.",""],[1,"105","3","Tourism Product and Service Adjustment","it is necessary to adjust the offer of tourist products and services in accordance with the newly arisen situation.",""],[1,"105","3","Tourism Capacity Upgrading and Destination Management Systems","Capacities in tourism need to be further improved in order to achieve sustainability and meet environmental goals and reduce global warming in line with the European Green Deal, as well as to implement destination management systems to innovate domestic destinations marketing and management systems.",""]],"104":[[1,"118","10","Financing and Incentives for Public Project Contractors","Financing and incentives for companies participating in the implementation of public projects",""],[1,"118","12","Capacity Building for Reform Implementation","Increase capacities for realization of initiated reforms (financial, personnel ... )",""]],"105":[[1,"122","4","Public Procurement Transparency and E-Procurement Reform","In order to increase the transparency and efficiency of the public procurement process in December 2019, the Law on Public Procurement (\"Official Gazette of the RS\", No. 91/19) was adopted, with effect from 1 July 2020.",""],[1,"122","4","Public Procurement Portal and Electronic Tendering System","A new Public Procurement Portal has been established, as well as electronic tenders and centralized procurement plans for centralized public procurement bodies, while the plan is to add new functionalities such as e-Contracting and e-Concessions.",""],[1,"122","4","Public Procurement Partnership for Innovation Model","The law also recognizes the \"partnership for innovation\" model, the goal of which is the development of innovative goods, services or works and their subsequent procurement.",""]],"106":[[1,"123","2","e-Space Digital Spatial Planning Platform","with the establishment of the digital platform for spatial and urban planning e-Space, the Ministry of Construction, Transport and Infrastructure will provide further improvement of procedures for obtaining construction permit, as well as transparent land management and spatial development processes in general in Serbia.","Ministry of Construction, Transport and Infrastructure"],[1,"132","14","E-Space Digital Platform for Spatial Development Management","IMPROVEMENT TO SPATIAL DEVELOPMENT MANAGEMENT IN THE REPUBLIC OF SERBIA THROUGH ESTABLISHMENT OF E-SPACE DIGITAL PLATFORM",""],[1,"132","15","Digital Spatial Planning Management Reform","The main goal of structural reform is the digital transformation in the field of planned spatial development management in the Republic of Serbia in order to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of development decision-making and better management of spatial development policy, through the digitization of data and urban and spatial planning procedures and the formation of a digital e-Space platform.",""],[1,"133","1","Public Planning and Land Administration Reform","The reform will contribute to improving the efficiency of planning and the quality of planning documents, creating conditions for overcoming the existing inefficiencies and non-transparency of public decision-making and the provision of services in the field of land management.",""],[1,"133","1","Construction Permit and Location Conditions Streamlining","Also, the reform will reduce the number of days and costs of obtaining location conditions and construction permits, which will create conditions for a better position of the Republic of Serbia on the Doing Business list of the World Bank.",""],[1,"133","6","Digital Database and Catalogue for Spatial and Urban Plans","Compiling digital database and catalogue of spatial and urban plans data",""],[1,"133","7","Spatial and Urban Plans Distribution Database Development","Development of a distribution database for spatial and urban plans",""],[1,"133","9","Digital e-Space Platform and E-Participation System","Establishment of a digital e-Space platform (including an e-participation system)",""],[1,"133","10","Digital e-Space Platform User Training","Training of civil servants and other professional users of the digital e-Space platform",""],[1,"133","11","Digital Platform e-Space Regulatory Framework","Development of regulations and establishment of the legal framework for the digital platform e- Space",""],[1,"133","12","Digitization of Spatial and Urban Plan Data","Digitization of spatial and urban plan data (for the entire territory of the Republic of Serbia)",""],[1,"133","14","Digital Database for Spatial and Urban Plans","Digital database of spatial and urban plans established",""],[1,"134","1","e-Space Digital Construction Permitting Platform","Establishment of the digital platform e-Space will enable faster issuance of construction permits through more efficient coordination of all holders of public authority in the field of planned spatial development management.",""],[1,"134","2","e-Space Digital Platform Establishment","For the establishment of the initial digital platform e-Space, EUR 1.5 million are planned in 2022 and EUR 1.37 million in 2023.",""],[1,"134","3","Electronic Information Access for Development Activities","Also, the reform will contribute to the creation of equal opportunities for access to and use of electronic information on planned development activities in a given area, as well as on the impact of such activities on real estate values, which will result in increased attractiveness of the business environment and greater security of investment, and from there to the general improvement of conditions of life and work in the Republic of Serbia.",""],[1,"134","4","Structural Reform for Sustainable Urban Planning and Environmental Tax Collection","The implementation of structural reform will have a positive impact on the environment, in terms of its protection and improvement, and will also contribute to meeting the objectives of the European Green Deal in the Republic of Serbia, through: better definition and more efficient implementation of planning solutions related to the achievement of the goals of the process of sustainable urbanisation and development in general; reduction of social costs caused by irrational use of land and other resources, together with more precise assessment of the amount of the so-called environmental taxes and better collection of them; etc.",""],[1,"134","7","Digitization and Spatial and Urban Plan Data Preparation","Engaging additional resources on digitization and preparation of spatial and urban plan data",""]],"107":[[1,"136","2","Artificial Intelligence Scientific Projects Programme","The implementation of the Strategy for the Development of Artificial Intelligence began with a programme for scientific projects in the field of artificial intelligence",""],[1,"136","2","Artificial Intelligence Software Deployment in Public Administration","as well as the implementation of software that uses artificial intelligence in public administration",""],[1,"136","2","Artificial Intelligence Development Support Action Plan","the Action Plan for the period 2020-2022 was adopted (June 2020), which includes projects to support the development of artificial intelligence with new programmes in the fields of education, economy, science and public administration",""],[1,"140","1","Artificial Intelligence Programme","Implementation of the Artificial Intelligence Programme",""],[1,"141","8","Artificial Intelligence Strategy Implementation Action Plan","Action plan for the implementation of the Strategy for the development of artificial intelligence in RS for the period 2020-2025 (adopted in June 2020) envisages the use of artificial intelligence in the function of science and innovation development, as well as the establishment of the Institute for Artificial Intelligence, a central institution for connecting and strengthening cooperation with world experts in this field.",""],[1,"142","5","Institute for Artificial Intelligence Establishment","Establishment of the Institute for Artificial Intelligence and instruments for providing support to the economic sector",""]],"108":[[1,"136","7","High-Capacity COVID-19 Detection Laboratory Project","The government, in cooperation with the Beijing Genomics Institute (BGI) launched a joint project to build a high-capacity COVID-19 detection laboratory that has started operating in Belgrade (up to 2,000 analyzes per day) and Niš (up to 1,000 analyzes per day).",""],[1,"136","7","Innovation Fund Support for Innovative Projects","The Innovation Fund approved RSD 53 million (about EUR 450 thousand) to finance 12 innovative",""],[1,"137","1","Special Research Programme COVID-19","in May 2020, the Science Fund published a public call for proposals for scientific research projects within the Special Research Programme COVID-1955 with a total budget of EUR 2 million.",""],[1,"139","7","Special COVID-19 Research Programme","The Science Fund has announced a special research programme COVID-19, which gave an effective scientific response to the current pandemic and showed the readiness of the scientific community to respond to new social challenges.",""],[1,"142","1","Innovation Fund Public Call for Pandemic Impact Mitigation","The Innovation Fund financed 12 different innovative projects of companies within the announced Public Call for Suppression of the Effects of the pandemic.",""]],"109":[[1,"143","10","State Data Centre Construction in Kragujevac","The construction of the State Centre for Data Management and Storage is underway - Data Centre (DC) in Kragujevac (activity transferred from the previous ERP), which will house the key information and communication infrastructure of the Republic of Serbia.",""],[1,"143","10","High-Performance Computing Procurement for National AI Platform","The next activity is procurement of high performance computing system as one of the most important parts of the future National Platform for Artificial Intelligence, the establishment of which is defined by strategic documents.",""],[1,"143","10","Smart City Project","The goal of the Smart City project, which is the third activity, is to improve the quality of life of the entire population in those cities by rationalizing the functioning of large cities and more economical resource management.",""],[1,"144","4","Establishment of DC in Kragujevac","Establishment of DC in Kragujevac",""],[1,"144","5","High-Performance Computer System Procurement","Procurement of high performance computer system - Supercomputers",""],[1,"144","6","Urban Area Digitization and Sensor Network Deployment","Digitization and automation of urban areas through mass placement of sensors and their connection, with each other and with the Data Centre",""],[1,"144","10","Supercomputer Production Launch","Launch of the Supercomputer into production",""],[1,"145","1","Future State AI Platform","It is envisaged that the future state platform for AI will be available to the academic community, science and technology parks and the business sector (MSE) in order to support the development of innovative solutions based on AI.",""],[1,"145","1","Smart City Data and Service Development Project","Gathering a large amounts of data and more economical resource management through the Smart City project, leads to the design and development of new services, most of which would be of a commercial nature, which will contribute to starting new businesses and increase economic activity.",""],[1,"145","2","Data Centre Construction in Kragujevac","funds for the continuation of construction are planned within the approved limit on the capital project Construction of Data Centre in Kragujevac in the total amount of EUR 42,041,690",""],[1,"145","2","Supercomputer Procurement","For the procurement of Supercomputers, the total planned costs amount to EUR 1 million from the RS budget for 2021.",""],[1,"145","2","Smart City Project Implementation","For the implementation of the Smart City project, the planned costs from the RS budget are EUR 12.583.333",""],[1,"145","3","Digital Centre Staffing and Cloud Systems Development","it will be necessary to employ 30 highly qualified staff in the field of IT, mechanical engineering and energy, with additional need for IT staff to work on the development, implementation and maintenance of cloud systems.",""],[1,"145","3","Artificial Intelligence Development Initiative","The development of AI will lead to an increase in the quality of life of all citizens through the development of innovative solutions in the areas of public administration, health and medicine, transport, road infrastructure and mobility in urban areas.",""],[1,"145","3","Smart City Project","The realization of the Smart City project through a public invitation to cities (and municipalities) in Serbia to actively participate in this project, together with their universities and schools, as well as the private sector, will affect additional employment and generate new services.",""],[1,"145","9","Contractual and Procurement Compliance Measures","Compliance with contractual provisions and procurement procedures.",""],[1,"145","9","Foreign Manufacturer Reproduction and Equipment Distribution Continuity","Depending on the current situation regarding the COVID-19 pandemic, the start of re-production with foreign manufacturers and the unhindered distribution of equipment from the country where the equipment is produced to the place of delivery.",""],[1,"145","12","Stakeholder-Responsive Infrastructure Development","Infrastructure development in accordance with the needs of stakeholders obtained through a continuous consultation process (collection of feedback from users and improvement based on proposals).",""]],"110":[[1,"148","13","Regional Economic Area Action Plan Implementation","Serbia actively participates in the development and implementation of the Multi-Annual Action Plan for the Development of the Regional Economic Area (MAP REA).",""],[1,"148","13","Regional Investment Reform Agenda Implementation","individual action plans for the implementation of the Regional Investment Reform Agenda have been adopted",""],[1,"148","13","Common Regional Market Action Plan","The Common Regional Market Action Plan under the Berlin Process is adopted on 10 November 2020 at the Western Balkans Summit in Sofia.",""],[1,"148","13","Regional Four Freedoms Facilitation Measures","By the end of 2024, a number of activities are planned in the areas of: a) promoting the four freedoms (through mutual recognition agreements, removing obstacles and reducing costs and time of movement of goods, services, capital and people)",""],[1,"148","13","Regional Investment Promotion and Screening Guidance","improving the attractiveness of the region for investment (through regional investment promotion campaign, developing regional guidance and procedures for screening mechanisms)",""],[1,"149","2","Ratification of the Free Trade Agreement with the Eurasian Economic Union","at the beginning of 2020, Serbia ratified the Free Trade Agreement with the Eurasian Economic Union (Russia, Belarus, Kazakhstan, Armenia and Kyrgyzstan).",""],[1,"149","3","Efficient NCTS Transit Procedure Implementation","The most important activity for a good ranking in this area is the efficient implementation of the NCTS (new computerized transit system) transit procedure by the Customs Administration.",""],[1,"150","2","Regulatory Harmonization and Quality Infrastructure Strengthening","Harmonization of national regulations with technical regulations of the European Union and their efficient application through a developed quality infrastructure system are a prerequisite for product safety on the domestic market and Serbia's inclusion in international and European integration flows and ensuring free movement of goods and services.",""],[1,"151","1","Foreign Trade Expansion and Competitiveness Reform","The goal of the reform is to intensify, improve, diversify and further grow Serbia's foreign trade at both regional and global levels.",""],[1,"151","2","WTO Accession and GMO Trade Restriction Resolution","Serbia continues its activities aimed at achieving WTO membership, and especially at resolving the issue of the existing ban on foreign trade of GMO products in the Republic of Serbia and the end of open bilateral negotiations with certain WTO members.",""],[1,"151","3","Implementation of CEFTA Additional Protocol Obligations","activities will be undertaken to implement obligations from the CEFTA Additional Protocol 5, CEFTA Additional Protocol 6 and continue negotiations on CEFTA Additional Protocol 7.",""],[1,"151","4","Trade Facilitation Action Plan Implementation and Development","Within the National Coordination Body for Trade Facilitation (NCBTF), with the participation of the private sector, the implementation of the Action Plan for 2020-2021 and the development of the Action Plan for the period 2022-2023 will begin in order to identify and remove barriers to trade, especially technical and phytosanitary measures, as well as facilitating customs procedures.",""],[1,"151","6","WTO Accession Negotiation and Regulatory Harmonization","WTO accession negotiations - bilateral negotiations, adoption of regulations harmonized with WTO rules and principles",""],[1,"151","7","Implementation of Additional Protocol 5 on Trade Facilitation","MAP REA - CEFTA - Implementation of Additional Protocol 5 on Trade Facilitation",""],[1,"151","8","Implementation of Additional Protocol 6 on Trade in Services Liberalization","MAP REA - CEFTA: Implementation of Additional Protocol 6 on Trade in Services Liberalization",""],[1,"151","9","CEFTA Additional Protocol 7 on Dispute Settlement Negotiations and Adoption","Negotiations and adoption of Additional Protocol 7 on Dispute Settlement",""],[1,"152","1","Implementation of Trade Facilitation Action Plans","Implementation of activities defined by the Action Plans for 2020 and 2021 within the National Committee for Trade Facilitation (NCBTF)",""],[1,"152","2","NCBTF Action Plan Implementation","Adoption of the new NCBTF Action Plan for 2022-2023 and implementation of the planned activities",""],[1,"152","5","Trade Facilitation and Market Access Improvement Measures","trade improvement through the implementation of CEFTA additional protocols, as well as NCBTF trade facilitation activities will have a significant impact on removing trade barriers",""],[1,"152","13","Trade Partner Coordination Mechanism","Coordination with the most important trading partners in order to amortize the negative effects of potential trade restrictions.",""],[1,"152","15","CEFTA Trade Barrier Removal Dialogue and Coordination","Coordination and communication with CEFTA partners, dialogue on creating conditions for removing trade barriers.",""],[1,"152","17","Law on GMOs","passing the Law on GMOs will facilitate bilateral negotiations with some WTO members.",""],[1,"152","19","Removal from EU Protection Measures List","Activities to exclude Serbia from the list of countries to which EU protection measures are applied.",""]],"111":[[1,"153","1","Financial Support for Business Quality Infrastructure Adoption","The first is a response to the needs of the economy and includes an instrument of financial support to businesses, primarily small and medium enterprises, to increase the use of standards in production and business organization, product certification, management systems and improving the availability of all other services in the field of QI.",""],[1,"153","2","Product-Info Digital Service Development","The second component, \"Product-Info\" refers to the construction of a single digital service to improve the information and availability of digital services in connection with the application of technical regulations.",""],[1,"154","1","Business Support Programme for Product and Service Quality Improvement","Business support programme to improve the quality of products and services",""],[1,"154","2","Business Support Programmes Development","Development of support programmes for business entities",""],[1,"154","4","Single Digital Service for Technical Regulations","\"Product info\" - Establishment of a single digital service related to technical regulations",""],[1,"154","6","Database and Digital Service Improvement for Product Standards Compliance","Improvement of databases and digital service in the Ministry of Economy (Sector for Quality and Product Safety) in connection with technical requirements for products and the portal \"TBT-Enquire point\" (Product Contact Point)","Ministry of Economy"],[1,"154","7","Improvement of Databases and Digital Services in QI Institutions","Improvement of databases and digital service in QI institutions (ISS, ABS and DMPM)",""],[1,"154","11","Unified Digital Product Information Service","Unified digital service \"Product info\" established",""],[1,"154","13","Product Quality and Standards Incentive Scheme","Incentives for increasing for use of standards and improving product quality as well as providing a comprehensive functional digital service \"Product Info\", will directly affect the reduction of technical barriers to trade and increase exports of industrial products covered by NC 1.",""],[1,"154","13","Product Info Digital Service","Incentives for increasing for use of standards and improving product quality as well as providing a comprehensive functional digital service \"Product Info\", will directly affect the reduction of technical barriers to trade and increase exports of industrial products covered by NC 1.",""],[1,"155","2","Economic Reform Implementation Support","Costs related to the implementation of this reform include (a) subsidies to economic entities",""],[1,"155","2","Institutional IT Assessment and Software Analysis","analysis of the state of existing IT and available software solutions in the institutions covered by the reform",""],[1,"155","2","IT Equipment and Software Procurement","procurement of missing IT equipment and software",""],[1,"155","2","Staff Training for Portal Networking and Content Updating","training of staff for networking and continuous updating of portal content as well as costs of promotional activities",""],[1,"155","7","Donor-Funded Support Programme Tightening","Provision of financial resources from donor sources; Tightening the conditions for granting support, planning support programmes as a continuous activity in the coming years.",""],[1,"155","9","Donor Communication and Partner Institution Budget Support","Intensive communication with donors to provide support; Increasing the budget allocation of partner institutions involved in the implementation of the reform.",""],[1,"155","11","Temporary Reform Working Body","Establishment of a temporary working body",""]],"112":[[1,"120","2","Minority Shareholder Protection and Corporate Transparency Measures","the introduction of external audit and detection of related-party transactions, as well as requirements for greater corporate transparency",""],[1,"120","2","Bankruptcy Creditor Representation Procedure","the introduction of a procedure requiring creditors to appoint a representative in the event of bankruptcy",""]],"113":[[1,"120","2","Electric Grid Reliability Improvement and Maintenance","improvements and better maintenance of the grid",""]],"114":[[1,"121","2","Alternative Financing Framework for SMEs and Sole Traders","the legal framework in the field of financial services has been improved by the adoption of the Law on Open-End Investment Funds subject to Public Offering and the Law on Alternative Investment Funds (\"Official Gazette of the RS\", No. 73/19), which provide alternative sources of financing42.",""],[1,"121","2","COVID-19 Loan Repayment Moratorium","The moratorium on repayment of loans, as a support to the economy in order to reduce the negative effects caused by the COVID-19 pandemic, was accepted by 93%43 of economic entities.",""]],"115":[[1,"161","2","Construction and Reconstruction of Regional Training Centers","funds for the construction and reconstruction of regional training centre \"Aviation Academy\" in Belgrade for 2021 amount to EUR 1,305,621",""],[1,"161","3","Equipment of the Aviation Academy Regional Training Center","the funds needed to equip the regional training center \"Aviation Academy\" in Belgrade amount to EUR 2,575,761",""],[1,"161","3","Equipment of Other Regional Training Centers","part of the funds needed to equip other regional training centers will be provided through a loan from the European Investment Bank in the amount of EUR 1,950,000 for 2022 and EUR 360,000 for 2023",""],[1,"209","3","Aviation Academy Training Center Equipment Provision","the funds needed to equip the Aviation Academy training center have been entered and it will be provided from additional funds from the RS budget.",""],[1,"228","7","Dual Education Cooperation and Aviation Academy Equipment Upgrade","Memorandum of Cooperation in the field of dual education was signed with the German air company MTU, for which it was necessary to procure additional basic equipment for the Aviation Academy as it is one of the planned regional training centres, and in 2020 funds were reallocated for this purpose.",""],[1,"228","10","Training Centres Setup and Equipment","Setting up, infrastructural organisation, and equipment of training centres",""],[1,"228","11","Equipment and Reconstruction of Regional Training Centres","Project documentation for the equipment and reconstruction of two regional training centres has been prepared.",""]],"116":[[1,"167","2","Diaspora Return Incentives and Engagement Measures","In order to encourage return, tax and other incentives related to new employment will be additionally promoted, through communication with both the economy and returnees.",""],[1,"167","2","Diaspora Dialogue and Trust-Building Activities","One of the steps in building trust with the diaspora will be to establish dialogue and understanding through activities and research.",""],[1,"167","6","Diaspora Cooperation Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity of the organization for establishing cooperation with the diaspora based on examples of good practice from countries with similar initiatives",""],[1,"167","8","Diaspora Cooperation and Dialogue Initiative","Establishing cooperation and dialogue with the diaspora through the organization of annual conferences Talent Gathering and promotion of successful stories of returnees",""],[1,"168","7","Return Point Program Funding Increase","The budget proposal for 2021 envisages an increase in the budget funds for the Return Point program to RSD 19,500,000 or EUR 162,500 while other funds will be defined later.",""],[1,"168","12","Diaspora Club and Organization Capacity Support","Providing continuous support to diaspora clubs and organizations in building internal capacities.",""],[1,"231","4","COVID-19 Returnee Support and Communication Activities","the team of the Point of Return was primarily occupied with activities supporting the Government of the Republic of Serbia in the fight against the COVID-19 virus, especially in communication with a large number of people who returned to the country during the pandemic.",""],[1,"231","5","Diaspora Humanitarian Return Coordination","the Point of Return have been reallocated to support bodies of the Republic of Serbia in organising the return of citizens of the Republic of Serbia back to Serbia.","Ministry of Foreign Affairs"],[1,"232","2","Diaspora Engagement Conferences","Open dialogue with the diaspora through organisation of the conference Talent MeetUp 3.0 and 4.0",""],[1,"232","6","Diaspora Outreach Podcast and Video Campaign","The Point of Return has launched podcasts as the first model through which it would promote successful stories of returnees.",""],[1,"245","1","Diaspora Return Support and Incentive Scheme","therefore it is of great importance to provide timely direct support and incentives for the people in diaspora to return to Serbia.",""]],"117":[[1,"168","5","Skilled Talent Attraction for Deficit Occupations","the implementation of the reform will work on attracting individuals who can, in addition to knowledge and experience, bring closer and open many markets through their contacts.",""],[1,"245","2","Deficit Occupations Labour Market Attraction Reform","the implementation of the reform will work on attracting individuals who, in addition to their knowledge and experience, can also contribute to the development of the labour market.",""]],"118":[[1,"170","4","Procurement and Delivery of Protective and Health Equipment for Social Protection Institutions","Necessary protective and health equipment was procured and delivered to all social protection institutions (masks, gloves, coats, hats, socks, non-contact thermometers, disinfectants, etc.).",""],[1,"170","4","Employment Expansion for Social Protection Institutions","The government has approved the employment of about 700 people, in order to further strengthen social protection institutions through the employment of medical and non-medical staff.",""]],"119":[[1,"171","7","Clinical Centre Reconstruction and Equipping","There are delays in the reconstruction and equipping of clinical centres that are important for improving the quality of tertiary health care.",""],[1,"172","4","Construction of Two New COVID Hospitals","As a solution to the problem of lack of hospital capacity, Serbia has started the construction of two new COVID hospitals in Belgrade and Kruševac.",""]],"120":[[1,"172","7","COVID-19 Information System for Epidemiological Surveillance","In order to perform epidemiological surveillance related to the corona virus pandemic in Serbia, the Government has formed a unique and centralized software solution - Information System COVID-19103",""],[1,"172","8","Volunteer Registration Platform","A national platform for volunteer registration has been established through which all citizens who do not belong to the risk group and want to help the oldest citizens and other risk groups can apply.",""],[1,"172","8","National Plasma Donation Platform","Also, the National Platform Donate Plasma104 was established",""],[1,"172","8","Digital Solidarity Portal","the Digital Solidarity Portal was created for everyone who is in their homes due to the corona virus pandemic.",""],[1,"172","9","COVID-19 Self-Assessment and e-Health Referral System","The self-assessment test on COVID-19 in the form of a questionnaire of self-assessment of symptoms has been available since the beginning of April 2020 on the e-Health Portal.",""],[1,"172","10","PCR Test Result Notification Service","A new service (notification application) has been developed and is available on the e-Government Portal since the end of July 2020, which enables citizens to receive e-mail and SMS notifications whether their PCR test result on COVID-19 is available.",""],[1,"175","7","COVID-19 Real-Time Self-Assessment Service","a real-time self-assessment service for COVID-19 patients was established, through which Serbian citizens can, with data from the health card, access the portal, log in and report possible symptoms of COVID-19.",""],[1,"175","7","Foreign Persons Registration Service","Also, a service for registration of foreign persons is provided, due to supervision, according to the Law on Protection of the Population from Infectious Diseases.",""]],"121":[[1,"212","4","Performance-Based Contracting for National Road Maintenance","Continued transition to a new method of contracting with companies involved in the maintenance of the rest of the national road network (PBMC- 12,000km) (PCRS)",""]],"122":[[1,"214","2","Rural Agricultural Infrastructure Development","Improved competitiveness in agriculture through rural infrastructure development, land cultivation, and regulation of the market and quality of agricultural products",""],[1,"214","2","Agricultural Land Cultivation Support","Improved competitiveness in agriculture through rural infrastructure development, land cultivation, and regulation of the market and quality of agricultural products",""],[1,"214","2","Agricultural Market and Quality Regulation","Improved competitiveness in agriculture through rural infrastructure development, land cultivation, and regulation of the market and quality of agricultural products",""],[1,"214","3","Rural Infrastructure Improvement Implementation Handbook","Preparing handbook for the implementation of the measure of rural infrastructure improvement",""],[1,"214","4","Agricultural Farm Electrification Investment Incentive Handbook","Handbook on incentives for investments in physical property of agricultural farms for field electrification has been adopted.",""],[1,"214","6","Handbook on Incentives for Farm Field Electrification Investments","Handbook on incentives for investments in physical property of agricultural farms for field electrification has been prepared.",""]],"123":[[1,"219","2","Prototype System for Mass Real Estate Valuation","Adjustment, combination, and linking of data from real estate cadastres and data from local tax offices in 'pilot' municipalities to develop a prototype of the system for mass evaluation of real estate value",""],[1,"219","4","Mass Real Estate Valuation System Development","A whole set of preparatory actions needed to implement the activity has been carried out: information on available databases in the territories of pilot municipalities has been collected; the cooperation agreement with the municipality Vracar has been signed, thus incorporating all five pilot municipalities into the system of mass evaluation of the real estate value; demographic and social-economic data for pilot municipalities have been collected; registries and local databases from which data will be extracted for the Registry of data for mass evaluation have been defined; requests for functionalities of the system of the registry of data for mass evaluation have been formulated; external and internal data sources have been defined, as well as basic and supplementary tables in the data model; data on the year of construction of facilities in three pilot municipalities have been collected (Zrenjanin, Pirot and Cacak); the project design for the registry of data for mass evaluation has started.",""]],"124":[[1,"222","14","Early Development Programme and Innovation Cofunding Programme","Project implementation 1 PC (Early Development Programme and Innovation Cofunding Programme) by beneficiaries and monitoring by the Innovation Fund",""],[1,"223","2","Programme of Cooperation Between the Scientific and Business Community","Project implementation 3 PC (Programme of cooperation between the scientific and the business community) by beneficiaries and monitoring by the Innovation Fund",""],[1,"223","5","Project Evaluation and Implementation by Beneficiaries","Project evaluation and implementation 4 PC (Early Development Programme and Programme of Cooperation between the Scientific and Business Community) by beneficiaries and monitoring by the Innovation Fund",""],[1,"223","8","Publication and Evaluation of Received Projects","Publication and evaluation of received projects, implementation of 5 PC (Early Development Programme and Innovation Cofunding Programme), consultations, workshops, and open door days",""],[1,"223","10","Technology Transfer Programme","implementation of the Technology Transfer Programme",""],[1,"223","10","Innovation Vouchers Programme","realisation of the Programme of Innovation Vouchers",""],[1,"223","10","Proof of Concept Programme","realisation of the Proof of Concept Programme + potential development of new service lines",""],[1,"223","12","Technology Transfer Programme","Technology Transfer Programme is going according to plan.",""],[1,"223","12","Proof of Concept Programme","The second call for the Proof of Concept Programme has been carried out and applications are currently being assessed.",""],[1,"223","12","Innovation Voucher Allocation Calls","Public calls for the allocation of innovation vouchers are going according to defined dynamics.",""],[1,"224","7","Early Development Programme and Innovation Cofunding Programme","Publication, evaluation and implementation of 1 PC (Early Development Programme and Innovation Cofunding Programme), consultations, workshops, and open door days",""],[1,"224","8","Innovation Fund Grant Application and Contracting","Innovation Fund has submitted a preliminary Application to the CFCU.",""]],"125":[[1,"224","1","Business Incubator Services Improvement","Realisation of activities of the second project component - Improvement of business incubator services",""],[1,"224","3","High-Tech and Self-Employment Business Incubator Support","Handbooks for the provision of services of hi-tech business incubators and self-employment business incubators are prepared.",""],[1,"224","3","Capacity Building for Business Incubators","Intensive capacity building programmes in hi-tech business incubators and self-employment business incubators have been carried out.",""],[1,"224","4","Business Incubator Capacity-Building Component","Realisation of activities in the third project component - Improvement of capacities of relevant stakeholders to establish and manage business incubators",""],[1,"224","6","Business Incubator PPP Model Development","The PPP model for setting up and managing business incubators is being developed.",""],[1,"224","6","International Business Incubator Knowledge Exchange","Participation in the International STP Conference was organised (IASP), as well as the exchange of experience and know-how through participaton in virtual study visits to business incubator eco-systems in Lithuania, Estonia, and Poland.",""],[1,"224","9","Digital Transformation Support Programme for SMEs","Implementation of the Digital Transformation Support Programme SMEE *",""]],"126":[[1,"203","5","E-Government Infrastructure and Technology Upgrade","Increasing the availability of e-Government by improving infrastructure and introducing new technologies",""],[1,"224","12","National Data Management and Storage Centre","Setting up of the National centre for data management and storage in Kragujevac - Data Centre Kragujevac",""],[1,"224","14","Central Information System for Hotel, Hospitality and Tourism","Development of the 'Central Information System in hotel and hospitality industry and tourism' (CIS)",""],[1,"225","5","Rural Optical Broadband Network Installation","Preparations for the installation of optical broadband network in rural areas of Serbia",""],[1,"225","6","Broadband Infrastructure Development in White Zones","the project for joint development of broadband communication infrastructure in 'white zones' in the Republic of Serbia.",""],[1,"226","1","Rural Optical Broadband Network Development","development of the optical broadband network in rural areas of Serbia.",""],[1,"240","4","Customer Service Improvement and E-Government Expansion","Extending this reform to include other activities related to the improvement of customer services and the development of e-Government, such as e-Office and e-Archive, strengthening information security, etc;",""],[1,"241","2","Information Security Improvement","The plan is to propose the improvement of Information Security in the coming period as one of the activities, since many projects in this area are expected.",""]],"127":[[1,"227","1","Single Digital Service for Technical Regulations","SR 17. 'Product info' - establishment of the single digital service relating to technical regulations",""],[1,"227","2","Product Information Portal Development and Progress Tracking Methodology","Identification of stakeholders' needs, structure and content of the 'Product info' portal coupled with the development of methodology for tracking progress in this area",""],[1,"227","4","Stakeholder Needs Assessment Questionnaire Development","The support for development of the questionnaire for the assessment of stakeholders' needs was agreed with the IPA 2017 project.",""],[1,"227","4","COVID-19 Impact Assessment on Quality Infrastructure Institutions","in order to determine the impact of the COVID-19 crisis on the sector of quality infrastructure (QI) and provision of conformity assessment services, the assessment of the crisis impact on the operations of QI institutions was done","Accreditation Body of Serbia | Institute for Standardisatin of Serbia | Directorate for Measures and Precious Metals"],[1,"227","7","Public Procurement for IT Needs Assessment and Digitalization Project Documentation","Terms of Reference have been prepared to implement public procurement of the service of needs assessment and the analysis of IT capacities in place, and development of project documentation for the procurement of hardware, sofware, digitalisaton of services.",""],[1,"227","8","Database and Digital Service Upgrade for Product Quality and Safety","Upgrading of databases and the digital service (Sector for Product Quality and Safety) linked with technical requirements for products and of the portal 'TBT Enquire point' (Point of contact for products)",""],[1,"241","7","Product Info Portal Development and Acceleration","the call for the establishment and improvement of the Product Contact Point - Product Info - this process in Serbia should be accelerated by setting this goal as a priority in this structural reform.",""],[1,"241","7","Financial Support for Product Safety and Quality Upgrading","Adding a part that provides financial support to companies to improve the safety and quality of products and services using the latest standards in production and business organization is a good complement to the service Product Info, which was proposed in last year's ERP cycle.",""],[1,"242","3","Single Digital Access Point for Product Information","The establishment of a single digital access point Product Info and digitalization of services in the field of IC, through the implementation of this component of the SR, conditions will be created for fulfilling the recommendation of the European Commission to improve the Product Contact Point (PCP) in accordance with European Regulation 2019/515.",""]],"128":[[1,"230","5","National Employment Strategy and Employment Action Plan Development","Development of the new National Employment Strategy for 2021-2026 with the employment action plan for 2021-2023",""],[1,"230","7","Strategy and Action Plan Drafting Task Force","Decision on establishment of the Task Force for drafting the Proposal of the Strategy and the AP;",""]],"129":[[1,"243","2","Youth Guarantee","The proposal is to introduce the Youth Guarantee, following the example of the ERP of North Macedonia, whose focus would be on increasing formal employment, vulnerable categories of the population and the sectors most affected by the consequences of COVID-19.",""],[1,"244","2","Youth Guarantee and National Employment Policy Improvement","Serbia is considering bringing in the Youth Guarantee (YG), which has proven to be an effective remedy to youth unemployment and inactivity in the European Union.",""],[1,"244","2","Formal Economy Transition Incentives and Social Protection Expansion","Extend social protection coverage and provide incentives for businesses and employees in the informal economy sector to register and to facilitate their transfer to the formal economy",""],[1,"244","2","Short-Time Work and Active Labour Market Policies","Take measures to preserve employment including through short-time work schemes and ensure increased provision of effective active labour market policies to the unemployed",""],[1,"244","3","Youth Guarantee Structural Reform","the proposal is to formulate a new structural reform that would relate to the introduction of the so-called Youth Guarantee",""],[1,"245","4","Youth Guarantee Programme","The Youth Guarantee programme, implemented in EU Member States, is an example of an intervention in which young people who are inactive and unemployed are approached through the cooperation of various sectors and social partners, including civil society organizations, with a view to long-term sustainable integration into the labour market.",""],[1,"245","5","Youth Guarantee Programme","\"Youth Guarantee\" means that young people up to the age of 25 are provided with job offers, continuing education, internship or training within a period of 4 months from entering the status of unemployment or leaving, i.e. completion of formal education.",""],[1,"245","6","Policy Coordination and Reform Implementation Mechanism","This programme requires a stable policy coordination system, especially between the institutions in charge of education, employment, social protection and youth policy, a managing mechanism that should guide activities at the national and local level, as well as the commitment of the competent institutions to implement necessary structural reforms and, finally, significant human and financial resources.",""],[1,"245","7","Youth Guarantee Active Employment Measures Funding","it is necessary that the National Employment Service has sufficient funds for active employment policy measures to enable availability of measures throughout the year, that is, with a sufficient number of quality vacancies to which young people are referred.",""],[1,"245","9","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Youth Guarantee Implementation","Therefore, the ILO recommends that organizational and administrative challenges affecting the capacities of both institutions should be tackled first, and then that the intervention be piloted in a maximum of three NES branches, but only for certain elements of the Youth Guarantee, such as measures to reach and activate a passive",""],[1,"246","1","Youth Guarantee Pilot and Outreach Measures","youth who are able and willing to work (outreach), and which can be implemented in cooperation with civil society organizations.",""]],"130":[[1,"249","2","Government Bond Sales Through Primary Dealers Pilot Project","A pilot project to sell government bonds through primary dealers is in preparation.",""],[1,"257","3","Regulatory Reform for Financing Access and Capital Market Development","Improving regulations that will enable greater access to sources of financing and development of capital markets in the area of Business environment of financing and development of capital markets",""],[1,"257","7","Regulation of Innovative Financing and Crowdfunding","the National Bank of Serbia initiates and participates in the process of comprehensive regulation of innovative types of financing, such as crowdfunding.","National Bank of Serbia"],[1,"257","7","Digital Assets Legal Framework","the National Bank of Serbia took an active part in the drafting and adoption of the law that governs digital assets and enables the operation of platforms for trading in virtual currencies.","National Bank of Serbia"]],"131":[[1,"249","3","Fiscal Risk Monitoring and Analysis of State Enterprises","The Sector for Monitoring Fiscal Risks of the Ministry of Finance analyses fiscal risks arising from the operations of national public companies, companies that perform activities of general interest and other state enterprises, through annual business programs, development programs, quarterly business reports, financial reports, audit reports.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"256","5","Financial Management and Control Strengthening in Local Self-Governments and Public Enterprises","Accelerating the process of introducing Financial Management and Control in local self- governments and public enterprises through strengthening institutional capacity and continuing education;",""],[1,"256","5","Professionalization of Public Company and Civil Service Management","Professionalization of the management of public companies and civil servants through the implementation of transparent competitions and employment procedures;",""],[1,"256","6","Public Property Management Reform","Improving the management of state property through 2.1 Preparation of a single register of users of public funds; and 2.2. Preparation of a single register of state property and indirect state property (property owned by municipalities, cities, the army of the Republic of Serbia, the Republic Pension and Disability Insurance Fund, the Development Fund and other state institutions); 2.3. Improving the regulatory framework related to the disposal of state property in terms of efficiency and transparency of the sale of state property and its leasing; 2.4. Improving the area of public-private partnership by changing the regulatory framework and strengthening institutional capacity in terms of efficiency and transparency and 2.5. Improving the area of bankruptcy of companies and banks by changing the regulatory framework and strengthening institutional capacity in terms of efficiency and transparency.",""],[1,"257","8","Monitoring of ECOFIN Recommendation Implementation Challenges","When it comes to the second comment that in the context of the measures and activities undertaken to implement ECOFIN recommendations it should be defined how the challenges are monitored, who forecasts them and in what way, and how these challenges are defined and identified in practice, in monitoring challenges, the National Bank of Serbia acts as a single",""]],"132":[[1,"251","2","National Agrarian Policy Reform and CAP Harmonization","The recommendation is that the ERP envisages a substantial, comprehensive reform of the agrarian budget in the direction of: 1) formulating a national agrarian policy that will achieve the maximum effect on production and income of persons engaged in agriculture and 2) improving the harmonization of domestic agrarian policies with EU Common Agricultural Policy.",""],[1,"251","3","Harmonization of Agricultural and Rural Development Policy Measures","Gradual harmonization of agricultural and rural development policy measures is envisaged by the Action Plan for the adoption and implementation of the EU acquis communautaire in the field of agriculture and rural development, the National Agriculture Programme 2018-2020, the National Rural Development Programme 2018-2020, as well as the National Programme for the adoption of EU acquis communautaire.",""],[1,"251","3","Agricultural Competitiveness Budget Support Reform","The ERP already contains in part the reform of budget support through structural reform 6: Improvement of the agriculture competitiveness, through the adoption of the Law on Regulation of the Market of Agricultural Products and the establishment of a legal basis for support in this area.",""],[1,"251","3","Future Harmonization of Agricultural and Rural Development Budget Support","The harmonization of other elements of budget support in the field of agricultural and rural development policy can be foreseen by the ERP in the following years, in accordance with the foreseen dynamics of harmonization with the acquis.",""],[1,"252","3","Agricultural Market Regulation and Producer Organization Framework","The legal framework on the regulation of the market of agricultural products should regulate markets by sectors in a unique way (with an emphasis on the introduction of standards in production), but also enable the formation of producer organizations, as well as enable and encourage contractual connection of all actors in the market chain.",""]],"133":[[1,"251","4","Local Rural Infrastructure Capacity-Building","it is recommended to envisage activities that will improve the capacities of local self-governments, both in planning and in the implementation of measures.",""],[1,"251","4","Producer Organization Support Scheme","it is recommended to maintain the activity of supporting the formation of producer organizations from the previous ERP, especially since it is possible to plan within IPARD 3, and it can significantly affect market access in the sector of fruit and vegetable production, milk production and dairy.",""],[1,"251","4","Agricultural Skills Development Initiative","It would be desirable for the ERP to envisage ways to improve the knowledge of people employed in this sector (farmers, farm managers and other employees in the agriculture and food industry).",""],[1,"252","2","Rural Infrastructure Improvement Support Measure","The measure related to the improvement of rural infrastructure is in the preparation phase.",""],[1,"252","4","Agricultural Advisory and Business Planning Support","Services for the needs of small agricultural farms make simple business plans (for investments up to EUR 50,000) free of charge and provide advisory services.",""],[1,"253","5","Rural Infrastructure Investment for Wastewater Treatment and Waste Management","Improvements of the agriculture competitiveness in the field of implementation of structural measures for the improvement of rural infrastructure is done through the financing of investments related to the construction of wastewater treatment plants and waste management.",""],[1,"253","6","Rural Infrastructure Improvement Measure under IPARD 3","the measure related to the improvement of rural infrastructure at the time when the measure is accredited in the IPARD 3 programme.",""]],"134":[[1,"252","7","Circular Economy Programme","the area of circular economy will be defined by a special programme, and not by a special strategy.",""],[1,"253","1","Circular Economy Programme with Three-Year Action Plan","needed for the area of circular economy, namely the Circular Economy Programme with a three-year Action Plan.",""],[1,"253","1","Environmental Protection Strategy with Circular Economy and Low-Carbon Development Goals","two strategies will be adopted for the field of environmental protection: the Environmental Protection Strategy, which will define special goals - one will be the circular economy, and the other is the Low Carbon Development Strategy.",""],[1,"253","1","Sectoral Environmental Programmes for Waste, Air Protection, and Cleaner Production","All other areas of environmental protection will be defined through programmes (waste, air protection, cleaner production, etc.), as specific objectives of these two umbrella strategies.",""],[1,"253","1","Industrial Policy Support for Circular Economy Transition","Industrial policy strategy for the period 2021-2030 cannot be an umbrella strategy for the circular economy because this topic is multisectoral and covers many areas such as waste management, innovation, digitalization, circular design, use of renewable energy sources, energy efficiency, green public procurement, urban mobility, etc., but it is very important because it creates a business environment for the development of micro, small and medium enterprises that can accelerate the transition from a linear to a circular model of the economy.",""],[1,"253","7","Industrial Circular Economy Structural Reform","it is necessary to clarify how to work on the transformation of the industry from a linear to a circular model.",""],[1,"254","1","Circular Economy Promotion and Business Education","first measure consists of activities to promote the circular economy and education of business entities with the support of the Serbian Chamber of Commerce and the Ministry of Environmental Protection.","Ministry of Environmental Protection"],[1,"254","1","Equipment Procurement Criteria Adjustment for Circular and Energy-Efficient Equipment","The other two measures relate to the adjustment of the criteria for the procurement of equipment, within the existing programmes of the Ministry of Economy, in the sense of gradually encouraging the procurement of equipment used in the circular economy and equipment that is energy efficient.","Ministry of Economy"],[1,"254","2","Circular Economy Voucher Support for Companies","The target number of companies that will apply the concept of circular economy through circular vouchers is 10 by the end of 2022.",""],[1,"254","2","Local Circular Economy Roadmap Development","The target number of local self-government units that will create local Roadmaps for the circular economy and become part of the circular community is 5 by 2023.",""],[1,"254","3","Circular Economy Voucher Incentive Scheme","10 companies are expected to go through a cycle of the allocation of circular vouchers (cash incentives), which entails the joint activities of the business and academic sectors on innovation and the design of measures that will contribute to environmental protection and meet sustainable development goals.",""],[1,"254","3","Circular Economy Company Selection Competition","In order to select adequate companies, a competition with criteria will be announced in cooperation with the Chamber of Commerce of Serbia.",""],[1,"254","3","Circular Economy Project Selection Commission","A special commission will be formed to select the best 10 projects, in which representatives of relevant institutions and organizations will participate.",""],[1,"254","3","Local Government Circular Economy Analysis Selection","Also, the selection of local self- governments in which analyses will be made for the application of the concept of circular economy will be the task of the commission, which will consist of representatives of relevant institutions and organizations.",""],[1,"258","4","Circular Economy Incentive Measures for Food Surplus and Donations","The proposals refer to SR 8 Introduction of circular economy and refer to the suggestion that: 1. inclusion of measures related to food surplus management in the circular economy programme and 2. consideration of proposals for abolition of VAT on food donations before the expiration date, be listed in the annex to the ERP document as incentive measures that will contribute to the development of the circular economy and the reduction of environmental pollution.",""],[1,"258","5","Circular Economy Programme Action Plan","we agree that the issue of food surpluses is very important and will be included in the Circular Economy Programme with an action plan for three years.",""],[1,"258","5","Public Procurement Criteria for Document Use","when initiating the public procurement, one of the criteria for bidders will be to use all relevant documents in order to obtain the highest quality data.",""],[1,"258","6","VAT Exemption for Near-Expiry Food Donations","the proposal to abolish VAT on food donations near the expiration date needs to be specifically considered.",""]],"135":[[1,"253","3","Erosion Mapping Activity","it is very important to make a map of erosion, which is also provided by the Law on Land Protection from 2015, therefore it is proposed to include this activity in the reform No. 6.",""]],"136":[[1,"255","5","Smart City Project Promotion and Experience Exchange Initiative","The proposal is to invite IT companies that have an offer of \"Smart City\" solutions to more agilely promote their offer, to stimulate the interest of local governments in these projects.",""],[1,"255","5","Smart City Implementation Coordination and Knowledge Sharing","Also, the Ministry of Public Administration and Local Self-Government and the Standing Conference of Towns and Municipalities should initiate, coordinate and organize the exchange of experiences in the implementation of \"Smart City\" projects.","Ministry of Public Administration and Local Self-Government | Standing Conference of Towns and Municipalities"]],"137":[[1,"255","7","Product Information Platform and TEHNIS Portal Expansion","in the part of this structural reform related to the establishment of the Product Info platform, it is necessary to present the procedure for the functioning of this service, i.e. the way in which the TEHNIS portal will be expanded to serve as a Contact Point for removing technical barriers to trade",""],[1,"255","8","Product Info Portal Development and Digitization Project","A detailed description of the functioning of the new access point \"Product Info\", together with project documentation for the procurement of missing computer and communication equipment, software and digitization of services, will be the result of public procurement of services of analysis and needs and preparation of project documentation for \"Product Info\" portal and service, which will be implemented in the first half of 2021.",""],[1,"255","8","TEHNIS Portal, Database, and E-Services Upgrade","Based on that project documentation, not only the existing TEHNIS portal will be improved, but also the existing databases, electronic services, as well as the networking of the Ministry of",""]],"138":[[1,"257","1","Agile Management Capacity Building for Research, Development, Innovation and Digital Transformation","Introduction of mechanisms and capacity building for agile management in the field of Research, Development, Innovation and Digital Transformation, in order to provide mechanisms for fast and adequate management of economic recovery and development.",""],[1,"257","2","National Data Strategy and Data Management Framework","Adoption of a data strategy and introduction of a systematic approach to data that will enable society and data-based management in the field of research, development, innovation and digital transformation.",""]]}});